msgid "**Gaps:** Both original full Ubuntu attempts failed at fresh neighbour startup with template_quarantined. The 507.23-second and 449.24-second diagnostics stopped after original VM 102 start/write without reproducing failure or completing deletion/survival. Later imported inspection demonstrated st_dev-only strict refusal, not the failure-instant predicate; original cause remains unknown. Both final actions exercised exact reuse only. Device-only public-cache quarantine/retirement/deletion/replacement remains unexecuted. Current NixOS focus covers only the 200-line prefix; its later 161 lines retain prior full-run scope. The first production NixOS Codex timeout retained no child TLS stderr; Ubuntu creation was not issued. Independent old-chain rejection, same-root preparation and encrypted round-trips do not establish commit/push of the leaf change, both-host live Rustls/SSH acceptance or successful renewed production canaries. Limited Codex/curl trust refusals do not establish every Claude mode. Native/fleet fixtures, production artifacts, live providers, sustained load, independent physical hosts and retained-disk upgrades retain separate scopes; production Anthropic remains disabled. Dangerous defaults intentionally remove client-level approval and sandbox protections; guest OS/VM/network/Marshall boundaries remain, and no stronger local confidentiality claim is made."
