#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:2169
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "**Lean pool-locked preparation (ADR-0152):**\n- **One logical snapshot:** each preparation retains two consecutive native tree\n  reads and identity checks under the pool lock. The `PoolSnapshot` holds their\n  validated observation, one owner listing and one mount table.\n- **Derived checks:** the absence proof, allocation audit and template audit all\n  derive from that snapshot. The template audit\n  joins observed mountpoint, seal and GUID rows. Template sealing and reader\n  validation keep the exec, setuid and devices check.\n- **After a mutation:** after its own create, `zfs set` or rename, a preparation\n  re-reads only the affected child. It then re-verifies the whole pool exactly\n  once.\n- **Fencing:** a snapshot whose lock was released is refused.\n- **Refusals:** all existing refusals are kept.\n- **Measured effect:** the native trace halved the whole-pool listings for a\n  claim, from 12 to 6. The production concurrency campaign is\n  outstanding."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:2173
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "**Open VS Code** requires the current completed stored login and current machine\nwrite authority. Viewer and web access do not grant editor access. Customer\nrequires the exact machine owner, including against administrators. A personal\norigin binds the full machine UUID and permanent GuestAccount UUID; a retired\nidentity loses authority before roster reconciliation. Every same-User email\nchange preserves the guest account, origin and current lease. Login approval is\nsingle-use, fixed to the personal origin, and cannot be transferred to another\naccount. Current grants, login and execution are checked again on each renewable\nlease. See [interactive access](#interactive) and [security boundaries](#security)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:2177
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "**Plan** and **Work** are collaboration modes; new threads default to Work. The\nexisting low/medium/high/ultra choices remain reasoning settings. Plan instructs\nthe agent to explore, clarify and prepare a decision-complete proposal. It is\nnot a read-only execution sandbox. A repository file, skill or summary cannot\nchange the persisted mode. Each admitted turn captures it, children inherit it,\nand running or unanswered work prevents changing it."
