msgid "- **machine, present**: [native OpenSSH reaches the per-user guest account with the registered key](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/audi.py) — Native guest account SSH..\n- **machine, present**: [revoking the platform SSH key closes the nested session and preserves the VM](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/audi.py) — Live revocation with retained VM..\n- **machine, recorded**: [VM owner with zero registered SSH keys receives actionable onboarding](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/user-ssh-journey.py) — September 25 ADR-0120 review records both NixOS and Ubuntu owner-with-no-keys journeys passing before the final main rebase; not a rerun of this handbook revision.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-ssh-onboarding-guidance.md).\n- **property, present**: [arbitrary request histories cannot acquire authority twice or escape diagnostics](repo:audi/test/ssh_state_test.exs) — Generated SSH channel requests preserve diagnostic confinement and single admission..\n- **property, recorded**: [same-email generations allocate distinct stable guest identities](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/guest_identity_history_test.exs) — Real retirement and verified registration actions preserve historical names/UIDs and reject inherited credentials/grants; database fixtures only.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fresh-guest-identity-verification.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [UID exhaustion rolls back earlier successful batch allocations](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/guest_identity_bounds_test.exs) — Base 63a1443c plus durable feature f1bd0e05, before incoming d4499c4c integration: Focused corrected 12-check rerun: finite noncycling UID exhaustion refuses a complete batch, rolls back earlier inserted accounts and preserves historical reservations; database evidence, not a native execution or the historical email-name collision property.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-durable-guest-identities.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [opposite VM owners acquire overlapping roster users in one canonical order](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/guest_identity_distributed_test.exs) — Three independent BEAMs and Repo pools, actual PostgreSQL contention and committed-state observer; both rosters succeed. Removing canonical sort causes a PostgreSQL deadlock and failed roster. No physical-host claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fresh-guest-identity-verification.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [retired guest home stays reserved and explicit fresh sharing restores usable access](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/account-lifecycle/driver.py) — Complete fourth NixOS native journey on f4de549a passed original home/UID/sentinel retention, expiry, sudo removal, old-key/unshared/old-name refusal, distinct fresh account and survivor controls; fresh explicit sharing preserves all historical reservations.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fresh-guest-identity-verification.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [packaged Lyra config installs the discovered fresh identity and reaches its home](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/account-lifecycle/driver.py) — Complete fourth NixOS native journey on f4de549a passed real Porsche discovery, verified HTTPS CA installation and actual generated Lyra-profile SSH with the persisted fresh username/UID and writable home. Tester-owned HOME/XDG paths execute the packaged production startup.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fresh-guest-identity-verification.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [fresh same-email team rejoin preserves every surviving guest identity](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/guest_identity_history_test.exs) — Two real retirement/verified-registration generations and explicit team member rejoin preserve owner/teammate boot rosters and every historical allocation; no inherited membership, no member manage and no native home claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fresh-guest-identity-verification.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [generated owner, grant and team histories serve exactly the durable writer identities](repo:marshall/test/marshall/ssh/guest_roster_history_test.exs) — Generated owner/grant/viewer/revoked/team/retirement compositions compared against an independently derived writer oracle with exact durable username/UID pairs, strict version increase and stable re-fetch allocation; retired and revoked candidates excluded while identities stay reserved. Database fixtures only.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-roster-identities.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [candidate bound denies 513 atomically and admits exactly 512 with durable identities](repo:marshall/test/marshall/ssh/guest_roster_history_test.exs) — 513 seeded candidates deny atomically with zero identity allocation; exactly 512 admitted with unique durable names/UIDs and stable re-fetch.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-roster-identities.md).\n- **unit, present**: [UID exhaustion rolls back the roster and recovery preserves identities](repo:marshall/test/marshall/ssh/guest_roster_history_test.exs) — Finite noncycling UID exhaustion rolls back a complete roster allocation while an existing identity remains stable; removing the unallocatable writer restores access without recycling reservations. Present database fixture, not the historical email-name collision-budget check..\n- **unit, recorded**: [a roster fetch refuses a concurrently retired candidate atomically and preserves survivors](repo:marshall/test/marshall/ssh/guest_roster_distributed_test.exs) — Three independent BEAMs, separate Repo pools, production retirement UPDATE gate and committed-state observer: an in-flight roster blocks on the retiring candidate's User row, refuses :unauthorized after commit, allocates nothing, and the next fetch serves the preserved owner identity with a fresh version. The deleted_at recheck mutant is detected. Complete public-table row-hash preservation asserted.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-roster-identities.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [two concurrent roster fetches commit the same durable identities with fresh versions](repo:marshall/test/marshall/ssh/guest_roster_distributed_test.exs) — Three independent BEAMs: concurrent same-VM fetches serialize on the locked VM row, commit one identical durable identity set with distinct increasing versions, and a third peer observes no uncommitted allocation. Complete public-table row-hash preservation asserted.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-roster-identities.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [SSH keys admit exactly one hundred and refuse oversized material](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/credential_management_bounds_test.exs) — Owner key registration and removal through the real actions: exact 100-key admission and next-key refusal, 4,096-byte public-key and 128-byte label argument bounds, removed keys remain archived, refusal leaves the inventory unchanged. No guest transport claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-credential-management-histories.md)."
