msgid "- **machine, present**: [post-import-template-fenced-replacement](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/zfs-guest/template-post-import.exs) — The device-only branch remains unexecuted: a common st_dev-only change across all four otherwise exact eleven-field vectors must cause ordinary sealed refusal without callback effects, one public ensure through old quarantine/retirement/deletion and a distinct fully verified incarnation. Stable source lock, successful native absence and absent VM 102 authority are asserted. Production identity and terminal Executor guards are unchanged. Imported retained-state inspection demonstrated strict refusal but cannot identify the original full-run failure instant. Recorded exact reuse in both final native runs does not establish this replacement branch..\n- **machine, recorded**: [post-import-exact-vector-classifier](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/zfs-guest/template-post-import.exs) — Corrected complete Ubuntu passed twelve subtests in 2,203.23 seconds with 0.75-second cleanup; action 22.26 seconds/subtest 40.85 seconds. Focused current NixOS passed six subtests through the exact 200-line current prefix and original VM 102 cleanup in 1,246.95 seconds with 0.72-second cleanup; action 36.53 seconds/subtest 74.89 seconds. Both exercised exact reuse: original template ready revision 4, same record/incarnation on subsequent VM 102 materialization and no scoped lifecycle transitions. Independent full hashes, native proof and absent pre-start authority were asserted. Device-only replacement remains unexecuted; later 161 NixOS lines have only prior full-run evidence, and original failures/unknown cause and production boundaries remain separate.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-13-native-guest-coding-clis.md).\n- **property, present**: [retired standby datasets withhold the pool wherever they are mounted](repo:lilly/test/host/zfs_test.exs) — ADR-0177: a standby-* child left after standby retirement withholds the pool from accounting wherever it is mounted, sealed or not, and is never measured as owned storage. Pure accounting over generated rows; no native leftover dataset is planted..\n- **property, recorded**: [snapshot-derived artifact shape equals the targeted per-command read](repo:lilly/test/host/pool_snapshot_test.exs) — ADR-0152: over generated accepted pool trees, the snapshot-derived template shape check equals the targeted per-command read, including probes of retired standby-* names; the template audit join equals the per-template native audit; a snapshot outliving its lock is refused by classification. Pure predicates only; native ZFS behavior is the image-template machine test. The record predates ADR-0177, which removed the standby kind and claim from this property; the narrowed property has no new recorded run.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0152-lean-pool-locked-preparation.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [pool-locked preparation native command count](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/image-template/driver.py) — ADR-0152: real ZFS traces the pool-locked part of Disk preparation for a claim and a bound resume, bounding zfs/zpool commands and whole-pool recursive listings. The record measured a standby claim; since ADR-0177 the claim prepares an empty owned dataset and this fixture has not been rerun. Fixture-scale hold times; no production concurrency campaign.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0152-lean-pool-locked-preparation.md).\n- **manual, recorded**: [Current fleet](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md) — Reviewed declarations then enabled templates, same-pool block copies and 128 standbys per image on both hosts; incoming e3300040 attributes production activation and three standby-source samples to its author. ADR-0177 has since retired standbys, so this review is historical for root-disk preparation. Source review establishes declared configuration and provenance of the report, not independently observed deployment, matched timing or native cutover acceptance.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **manual, present**: [Retired evidence provisioning-fastpath item 1](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md) — Reviewed historical scope at the captured baseline; no current runtime acceptance claim..\n- **unit, recorded**: [test_manifest_precedes_mutation_and_cleanup_is_confirmed](repo:scripts/test/test_provisioning_benchmark.py) — Twenty-four unprivileged runner cases preserve request IDs before effects, refuse foreign cleanup, reconcile lost replies without another mutation, bind a failed or terminal-success creation's original request and currently owned VM before submitting its preplanned deletion identity even when the client reply lacks a usable VM ID. The runner refuses before effects when hosts report different image NARs, an installed artifact disagrees with the selected catalog image, or the enabled campaign lacks a matching baseline summary/NAR identity or has disabled producers. Other cases require catalogued native method/source and template UUIDs, reject cold-template warm samples and invalid guest boot IDs/load, bind the guest username to Porsche proof, and keep Audi guest SSH separate from admin transport. Mocked SSH/SQL calls do not establish a real guest, template hit, complete baseline custody or physical deletion.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [test_different_registration_times_produce_identical_valid_databases](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/ubuntu/test_normalize_nix_db.py) — Three local typed cases normalize guest Nix SQLite registration times and sidecars while retaining paths/references and refusing empty or symlinked databases. Offline normalization of the two observed host databases yielded identical DB bytes. A complete rebuilt image and new catalog ID on both hosts have not passed.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [assert lib.hasInfix normalizeNixDb rootfsScript;](repo:nix/verification/tests/evaluation/ubuntu-guest.nix) — The exported ubuntu-guest-unit Nix check inspects the actual Ubuntu rootfs build script for the sandboxed Nix DB normalization call and reruns three typed database cases. It does not rebuild or compare a complete rootfs or establish a production image ID.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md).\n- **machine, present**: [guest-nix-registry-valid](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/user-ssh-journey.py) — In the revised Ubuntu authenticated-SSH journey, the real guest queries the pinned development-tools closure through its normalized Nix registration DB and returns a fixed verdict. The new assertion is present but not executed; the complete image rebuild, cross-host byte equality and native runtime proof remain gaps..\n- **manual, recorded**: [compatible-reader `153db737` commit was pushed](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md) — Strict read-only updater/system/role checks on both enrolled hosts plus the additive Marshall pool_id column at the exact reader release; producers off. Deployment status does not establish native template use.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md).\n- **manual, recorded**: [ssh_authenticated](repo:scripts/provisioning_benchmark.py) — One NixOS and one Ubuntu run-owned production canary each passed actual authenticated SSH ls, observed boot ID and verified uncached source, then confirmed original deletion and read-only absence of reservations and ZFS dataset. They are uncontrolled one-off samples; no warm median or native restart/clone acceptance.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [Porsche browser keys and native SSH execute real guest lifecycle](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/porsche.py) — The existing NixOS Porsche lifecycle subtest passed on the reader revision with native SSH, restart, cross-host relocation, independent clone and cleanup. Its combined fleet run failed later in the unrelated terminal/browser stage; no complete VM-test pass or Ubuntu claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [Porsche relocation preserves the Overalls login, account and home](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/user-ssh-journey.py) — The complete reader-revision Ubuntu native journey passed authenticated login, key revocation and renewal, Porsche relocation, reboot and cloning with VM-test cleanup. Its disposable hosts configure readiness and templates true; the test does not assert a native template hit, exact-boot readiness journal, delayed refusal or full Ubuntu Porsche lifecycle. Production producers were off at this captured reader revision.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md).\n- **machine, present**: [fleet-provisioning-verify](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/user-ssh-journey.py) — Revised disposable NixOS/Ubuntu guest journey checks the production-validated Lilly readiness journal against authenticated guest boot, host and placement, current running intent and boot challenge, and the 120-second deadline. It refuses stale boot digest and foreign host, including after restart. The revised VM test has not yet run; no warm template or production activation conclusion..\n- **machine, recorded**: [porscheLifecycleOnly then](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/default.nix) — Focused final typed NixOS variant passed in869.30seconds with real browser/SSH lifecycle703.71seconds, cross-host copy relocation, physical source/copy deletion and exact retained clone audits. Captured image/fixtures predate incoming Starship defaults. Ubuntu and the separate complete clone fault matrix remain unrun; native boot/trust prerequisites and original physical assertions are preserved.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [generated progress, faults and replays preserve prerequisites and bindings](repo:lilly/test/lifecycle/provisioning_test.exs) — Independent prerequisite histories reopen durable journals and preserve state/audit on invalid writes. Separate cases exercise typed corruption, late receipts and ACKs.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [sealed cross-dataset source and independent writable VM file](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/image-copy/driver.py) — Rust helper on disposable NixOS/ZFS: actual cross-dataset copy fallback, independent writes after template destruction, sparse fallback, overwrite refusal and ENOSPC.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [only_recognized_unsupported_errors_can_copy](repo:lilly/native/image-copy/src/tests.rs) — Hegel exercises real materialization with generated errno values and an independent fallback oracle; six additional properties cover bytes, independent writes, boundaries and identities. A weakened classifier mutant fails.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [owner death revokes the stream and contention cannot start a second](repo:lilly/test/transfer/stream_test.exs) — Private lilly-hostd with the packaged helper (ADR-0183): a stream connecting to an unreachable peer holds its lease; a second stream is refused as busy; killing the owner releases the lease, so hostd kills and reaps the pipeline and the stable owner.lock is reacquirable. Not native guest isolation or fleet cleanup evidence.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-16-guest-dataset-streams-in-hostd.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [recovery after interrupted native](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/image-template/driver.py) — Production Ash adapter on actual ZFS: restart/warm use, seals, independent VM disks, active-reader exclusion, retirement, mutable artifacts, foreign nonce and GUID refusal, interrupted create/copy/seal/destroy, 4096-record catalog bound, interrupted empty publication and no VM capacity credit.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [OverallsProtocol.uuid?(sealed.template_record_id)](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/image-template/probe.exs) — The extended disposable native ZFS probe passed on reader revision 153db737: a validated warm image carried a native lease and both record/incarnation UUIDs, while the verified uncached callback carried none. The full machine check also exercised independent disks, recovery and retirement. Synthetic artifacts cannot establish guest SSH or production cache use.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [interrupted sparse copy is retried before atomic disk publication](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/zfs-lifecycle/driver.py) — Disposable NixOS/ZFS lifecycle test exercises real sparse copy interruption, nonce/GUID ownership and durable retry through production storage code. Synthetic boot artifacts do not establish live guest SSH readiness.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [fn offload_refusal_before_progress_is_the_only_fallback](repo:lilly/native/image-copy/src/tests.rs) — Generated errno histories drive the real kernel-offload branch: only an allowlisted refusal before any transfer falls back to exact userspace bytes; every other error leaves an empty unpublished destination. Unprivileged temporary files; no native ZFS block-sharing claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-create-clone-delete-latency.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [fn partial_or_short_offload_never_falls_back_or_publishes](repo:lilly/native/image-copy/src/tests.rs) — Generated partial transfers followed by refusal or a short read always fail instead of falling back or publishing a mixed file. Isolated files only.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-create-clone-delete-latency.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [identity observations tolerate usage-only drift that exact observations refuse](repo:lilly/test/host/zfs_test.exs) — Generated usage-counter drift keeps the non-usage identity fingerprint, is accepted by deletion's identity observation and refused by exact capacity observations; incoherent accounting still retries. Pure decision function; no native pool churn or delete latency claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-create-clone-delete-latency.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [cross-mount same-pool source offloads into shared blocks](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/image-copy/driver.py) — Disposable NixOS ZFS pool: a bind-mounted same-pool source refuses FICLONE, lilly-image-copy reports offload, bcloneused grows by the full 8 MiB and the destination stays independent after writes and source destruction. Synthetic file; not the fleet kernel or real images.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-create-clone-delete-latency.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [delete-identity-fence-under-pool-writes](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/zfs-lifecycle/driver.py) — Disposable NixOS ZFS pool: the prepared neighbor's delete refuses a quota change injected between its two observations before the fence, then succeeds although a real 4 MiB pool write lands between them, leaving a retired deleted claim. Synthetic fixture; no production latency claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-create-clone-delete-latency.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [nix-sandbox-never-holds-guest-dataset](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/zfs-guest/namespace-cleanup.py) — Disposable NixOS ZFS host with a real Firecracker guest: with a daemon-routed sandboxed Nix build running, nix-daemon's namespace holds no pool mount and the fenced guest delete completes while the build keeps running (ADR-0144).; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-create-clone-delete-latency.md)."
