msgid "- **machine, recorded**: [The crash variant MUST observe a first-boot VMM SIGKILL, restart the same](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/native-services/default.nix) — Seven host boundary checks and the composed NixOS driver passed. An initial FreeBSD crash run exposed scheduled-only libc sync and lost acknowledged home/marker bytes. The corrected native UFS suspension/resume flush passed the final reviewed image 5022d714 crash variant in 224 seconds: observed SIGKILL, same-disk/new-MMDS/new-boot restart, exact retained bytes, stale-authority refusal, native UFS snapshot background fsck, all eight crash checks, both complete service oracles and final clean exit. The source-qualified OmniOS image passed the same crash oracle with fresh MMDS/boot identity, old-authority refusal, exact retained bytes, a completed zero-error ZFS scrub and final clean exit. Exact image/kernel/firmware/VMM and immutable receipts are recorded in the review.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [class](repo:nix/verification/tests/support/native_crash_recovery_test.py) — Seven host checks validate retained data, filesystem-result and source/mode boundaries without crashing or recovering a native guest.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md).\n- **manual, recorded**: [The crash receipt records](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-18-guest-os-matrix.md) — Final exact OmniOS 45983 disk passed process-SIGKILL/same-disk restart, stale-authority refusal, retained bytes and native ZFS integrity; no physical power-loss or relocation guarantee.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-18-guest-os-matrix.md)."
