msgid "- **machine, recorded**: [assert claim[\"state\"] == ADOPTION_KILL_STATES[operation]](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/zfs-transfer/driver.py) — Production received-rootfs adoption against real ZFS recovers native destroy, mount and policy interruption markers; two generated replay cases inspect durable claims and cleanup. This does not boot a transferred guest or establish cross-host relocation.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [cancellation after physical source stop restores data and fresh authority](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/relocation-failures.py) — Source restoration after confirmed physical stop passes in 207.57 seconds in the complete captured disposable native fleet; data, fresh execution authority and cleanup are inspected. One KVM failure domain, without independent physical-host or retained-state upgrade acceptance.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [private_services_ready(source)](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/relocation-failures.py) — Actual host-bound Ziggy response and bounded exact Audi-private role/version/ready frame recover after physical source reboot within the original setup timeout; only the exact real public issuer root persists across reboot. Endpoint-restart recovery passes in 381.13 seconds with durable receipt replay, data and cleanup; service unit state alone is insufficient. One KVM failure domain.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [Delete while destination cleanup is unavailable retains its disk and address](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/relocation-failures.py) — Unavailable destination cleanup retains its physical disk, capacity hold and address until actual cleanup succeeds; the captured native case passes in 206.12 seconds. One KVM failure domain, without physical-host power-loss or production acceptance.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [actual endpoint updates resume an interrupted native transfer](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/relocation-failures.py) — Real endpoint package updates resume the interrupted physical transfer, preserve guest data and complete cleanup in 336.29 seconds in the captured disposable fleet. One KVM failure domain; this does not establish a packaged retained-state legacy upgrade.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [failed destination readiness retries under a new boot without source rollback](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/relocation-failures.py) — A destination readiness failure retains the fenced source and retries under a new boot without source rollback; actual readiness, data and cleanup pass in 389.19 seconds. Disposable native fleet within one KVM failure domain.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [physical source pool pressure does not block the stopped copy or co-resident guests](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/relocation-failures.py) — Incoming stopped-only relocation-fleet recorded source pool pressure in its earlier 19-subtest pass after the probe-scheduling fix, followed by a final 20-subtest pass. Actual source pressure does not gate admission because relocation holds no source headroom; guest identity, unrelated native processes/data and cleanup are inspected. Historical 484.63s pre-copy fallback remains separate; no merged-editor or independent physical-host acceptance.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-stopped-only-relocation.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [destination ENOSPC preserves holds and resumes after physical headroom returns](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/relocation-failures.py) — Physical destination ENOSPC retains partial-receive/resume evidence and source holds, then completes adoption, readiness, data verification and cleanup after headroom recovery in 269.67 seconds. Disposable native fleet within one KVM failure domain; faults, oracles and deadlines are unchanged.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **manual, recorded**: [Acceptance failed: a pre-existing clone retained Overalls' transfer slot.](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-production-clone-relocation.md) — Production relocation refusal with an occupied host slot; database confirms no relocation admitted for the new source. Physical movement remains unverified.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-production-clone-relocation.md).\n- **property, present**: [generated clone and relocation claims retain exclusive host slots](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/relocation_ownership_test.exs) — Local Ash/PostgreSQL generated clone-versus-relocation claim on either endpoint with one to three retries; paired rollback, exclusive per-host occupancy, single owner role and release/reacquisition. No concurrent Marshall process or native stream observation."
