msgid "- **machine, recorded**: [assert page.request.get(origin + removed).status == 404](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/otel-marshall/browser.py) — Current source-built Marshall verified-TLS browser receives HTTP404 for retired SLO/log routes before and after ordinary-reader login, sees no overview links and refuses current/copied remembered sessions after exact stored revocation. This verifies Marshall's retired diagnostic presentation and retained login boundary; Grafana's independent operator login, production activation and seven-day compliance remain separate.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [check_operations_dashboard(grafana)](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/log-store/driver.py) — Current native Grafana HTTP API verifies all fifteen stable operations-panel IDs, titles, visualization types, Prometheus bindings and nonempty queries. Pinned VictoriaLogs plugin, verified TLS, hidden reader credentials, exact trace/log correlation, path/credential refusals and queued backfill also pass. This establishes current automatic provisioning and log-reader transport, not physical-host availability, production activation or numeric values for every operations query.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [/api/datasources/uid/overalls-victorialogs](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/log-store/driver.py) — Native provisioned datasource/plugin, hidden reader credentials, exact trace correlation and wrong-scope insert refusals over the real log-store entry and Grafana proxy.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [before-reboot](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/logging/driver.py) — Native source routing and durable unread journal backfill after reboot, destination outage and collector loss; isolated fixture disk budgets explicitly fit its disk.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md)."
