#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:2953
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "- **machine, recorded**: [current.issubset(closed)](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/vscode-web/authorization.py) — Both complete corrected pre-template startup snapshot family scripts passed real Audi missing/foreign Origin refusal, ordinary sign-out, established editor WebSocket closure and fixed-origin fresh authentication after browser/policy/recovery. NixOS 805s and Ubuntu 829s are total build/execution durations; final authorization subtests 12.06s/8.96s. No two-writer, broader host fault, recurring or production claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [editor compatibility binds the complete immutable release and image identity](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/image_editor_capability_test.exs) — Generated complete exact release tuples accept only matching content-bound image identity; changing commit, release or manifest content refuses, while catalog enabled status does not revoke existing image capability. Pure logic, no user or native authority.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [native editor opens from Marshall with personal terminal and isolated webview](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/vscode-web/fleet.py) — Exact058f13d8 NixOS and Ubuntu cold subtests passed actual Marshall opening, native custody, save/readback, personal terminal identity and isolated Markdown in35.12s/32.10s. Both full runs then failed policy; no later recovery/revocation or production acceptance.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [a disabled matching image remains usable and its authorized views are read only](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/editor_workspace_test.exs) — Actual SQL-backed authorized get/resolve/list projections expose only finite status without allocating accounts or changing persisted image attributes; LiveView renders the real link and fresh domain launch still admits the disabled-catalog matching image. No native isolation or production claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [a mounted writer downgrade removes the link and fresh launch authority refuses](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/editor_workspace_test.exs) — Actual stored write-grant downgrade removes mounted controls and direct launch returns403. Adjacent fixed cases inspect legacy/new-image guidance, configured-release changes, missing configuration, stopping with observed running, stored-login revocation and safe missing-status rendering. No native transport or guest-migration claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **unit, present**: [machine list exposes terminal and VS Code actions for an eligible owner](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/machines_live_test.exs) — The mounted Machines LiveView presents the Open VS Code link in a new tab for eligible running projections, disabled reasons for stopped, unsupported-image and unavailable states, and no control for hidden authority. Fresh launch admission, native transport and guest isolation remain separate evidence.\n- **unit, present**: [overview exposes terminal and VS Code actions for an eligible owner](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/overview_live_test.exs) — The bounded Overview preview presents the same Open VS Code eligibility and disabled-state reasons as the Machines list while retaining terminal and thread links; shared, unrelated and revoked projections remain authorization-scoped. Fresh launch admission, native transport and guest isolation remain separate evidence.\n- **machine, recorded**: [VM stop/start keeps saved files and opens only the new physical execution](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/vscode-web/fleet.py) — Pre-integration native record: Complete NixOS real stop/start preserved placement/epoch, advanced generation, rotated physical challenge/guest boot UUID, matched current-generation committed physical-running/Provisioning readiness and saved data. Ubuntu failed before this assertion.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [VM stop/start keeps saved files and opens only the new physical execution](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/vscode-web/fleet.py) — Corrected merged NixOS snapshot 849d8022 plus eligibility/SSH projection/root-UID diff later committed as af01b4b9: actual stop/start preserved placement and epoch, advanced generation, rotated challenge/guest boot UUID, and checked exact committed current physical guest_ready and saved data. Total 742 seconds build plus native execution; no postcommit, Ubuntu or production scope.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [current sharing roles independently decide editor write admission](repo:marshall/test/marshall/editor_test.exs) — Current role matrix exercises persisted SQL-backed grants; fixed adjacent tests exercise account, login, execution/release and rollback refusals. No native isolation or transport claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [fresh sign-in recovers while a stale editor cookie remains authentication-required](repo:marshall/test/marshall/editor_test.exs) — Normalized control requests distinguish stale stored login/cookie, current write denial and unavailable execution. Fresh stored sign-in replaces credential without reviving the old lease; no public browser/transport claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [current, revoked and unanswered stored logins retain different control classes](repo:marshall/test/marshall/editor_login_check_test.exs) — Actual SQL-backed current login and removal, plus an unshared-sandbox caller that cannot answer lookup, preserve authentication refusal versus infrastructure unavailability. No native transport or production database fault.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [current.issubset(closed)](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/vscode-web/authorization.py) — Pre-integration native record: Complete NixOS real browser checked unsafe/missing/sibling Origin refusal, ordinary sign-out, established editor WebSocket closure within thirty seconds and fixed-origin303 recovery to real sign-in. Ubuntu failed before these assertions; broader revocation/host-fault histories remain separate.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [current.issubset(closed)](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/vscode-web/authorization.py) — Corrected merged NixOS snapshot 849d8022 plus eligibility/SSH projection/root-UID diff later committed as af01b4b9: actual Audi foreign/missing Origin refusal, ordinary sign-out and established editor WebSocket closure passed after the complete real browser journey. Total 742 seconds build plus native execution; Ubuntu stopped before this stage. Broader revocation/host-fault and production histories remain separate.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [a single-label zone refuses editor launch before allocating a guest account](repo:marshall/test/marshall/editor_test.exs) — Actual authority launch refuses an incompatible zone and rolls back GuestAccount allocation; module evaluation and actual runtime configuration refusal retain disabled-editor compatibility. No native discovery or guest claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [unsafe requests reject sibling or missing origins before admission or connection](repo:audi/test/http_editor_test.exs) — Local generated unsafe HTTP/upgrade requests assert no admission/connector call for sibling or missing Origin. Actual public TLS/WebSocket closure remains native scope.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [origins retain complete independent identities and reject noncanonical spellings](repo:protocol/test/editor_test.exs) — Pure canonical origin parsing retains complete independent UUIDs; no browser-storage or native principal claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md)."
