#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:2957
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "- **machine, recorded**: [fresh same-email registration inherits nothing while old cleanup remains pinned](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/account-lifecycle/driver.py) — Separate feature f1bd0e05 plus incoming d4499c4c merged captures passed all eight subtests on NixOS438.33seconds and Ubuntu574.18seconds: real retirement, fresh same-email identity/no inheritance, pinned cleanup, retained shared storage/process/home, permanent old-home reservation and explicit fresh re-sharing. One disposable KVM failure domain; not later incoming source or complete Ubuntu SSH/editor acceptance.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-durable-guest-identities.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [retirement rejects an active team owner with a stable reason](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/account_lifecycle_test.exs) — Base 63a1443c plus durable feature f1bd0e05, before incoming d4499c4c integration: Current focused lifecycle/Ingress 26-test rerun: a real team-owner refusal after GuestAccount retirement begins preserves the prior account marker/audit, active User and absent deletion receipt through transaction rollback.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-durable-guest-identities.md).\n- **machine, present**: [lifecycle-refused-admission-retry](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/account-lifecycle/driver.py) — Present revised disposable fixture requires two real fresh enabled/execution-ready host/pool reports initially and one during the deliberate owned-host outage. It retries only exact closed insufficient_capacity with unchanged request key and bounded deadline; accepted/unknown outcomes stop. Both native witnesses passed creation under real admission, without fabricating telemetry/capacity; the refusal-retry branch is not separately forced..\n- **machine, present**: [lifecycle-independent-shared-transport](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/account-lifecycle/driver.py) — Present corrected fixture resolves co-location through authorized public relocation, waits complete/finished plus running/current destination and requires distinct hosts before GUID/PID capture and owned-host fault. Both complete native witnesses and composed-driver checks passed; no readiness or placement is fabricated..\n- **machine, recorded**: [lifecycle-enrolled-transfer-identity](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/account-lifecycle/driver.py) — Base 63a1443c plus durable feature f1bd0e05, before incoming d4499c4c integration: Both complete native witnesses wait for the actual transfer listener, validate canonical eth2 IPv4 and Ed25519 public key, enroll the endpoint through the real host command and assert exact persisted equality before authorized relocation/setup. No transfer authority is fabricated.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-durable-guest-identities.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [lifecycle-no-shared-retirement-deletion](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/account-lifecycle/driver.py) — Base 63a1443c plus durable feature f1bd0e05, before incoming d4499c4c integration: Both complete native witnesses capture whole-VM delete count after completed authorized setup relocation, prove that total unchanged after retirement and separately prove zero retained-current-placement deletes. Retained GUID/PID/native storage/home and fresh-VM checks also passed.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-durable-guest-identities.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [lifecycle-stream-lease-closure](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/account-lifecycle/driver.py) — Base 63a1443c plus durable feature f1bd0e05, before incoming d4499c4c integration: Both complete native witnesses closed already-open invited SSH streams with successful client-unit completion; the wait after browser retirement observation took 0.086 seconds on NixOS and 0.075 seconds on Ubuntu. This is not measured database-commit latency. Live roster reconciliation expired the old account and removed sudo authority while retaining historical home UID ownership.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-durable-guest-identities.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [fresh same-email registration inherits nothing while old cleanup remains pinned](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/account-lifecycle/driver.py) — Base 63a1443c plus durable feature f1bd0e05, before incoming d4499c4c integration: Both complete native witnesses passed fresh same-email registration (NixOS 52.32 seconds; Ubuntu 41.79 seconds): new User UUID has no inherited roles/credentials/grants/membership/machines, receives different canonical login/UID and opens real own SSH/browser home without retired marker while cleanup stays bound to old UUID. Later old-home reservation, explicit sharing and physical cleanup also passed.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-durable-guest-identities.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [same-email generations cannot inherit retired authority or redirect cleanup](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/account_lifecycle_history_test.exs) — Twelve generated histories of two or three same-email retirements with real Ash actions and synthetic physical outcomes; no native reclamation claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-account-lifecycle-verification.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [native-account-lifecycle-journey](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/account-lifecycle/browser.py) — Source-built browser/admin flow over verified HTTPS, virtual WebAuthn, encrypted local outbox, same-email replacement and copied authority refusal.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-account-lifecycle-verification.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [real resize recovery and reclamation release old holds without deleting shared-only guest](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/account-lifecycle/driver.py) — Three Marshall VMs and two real nested-KVM/ZFS provisioners; offline accepted resize delays retirement cleanup until source-built services reclaim owned storage.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-account-lifecycle-verification.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [same-email generations allocate distinct stable guest identities](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/guest_identity_history_test.exs) — Real retirement and verified registration actions preserve historical names/UIDs and reject inherited credentials/grants; database fixtures only.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fresh-guest-identity-verification.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [opposite VM owners acquire overlapping roster users in one canonical order](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/guest_identity_distributed_test.exs) — Three independent BEAMs and Repo pools, actual PostgreSQL contention and committed-state observer; both rosters succeed. Removing canonical sort causes a PostgreSQL deadlock and failed roster. No physical-host claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fresh-guest-identity-verification.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [retired guest home stays reserved and explicit fresh sharing restores usable access](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/account-lifecycle/driver.py) — Complete fourth NixOS native journey on f4de549a passed original home/UID/sentinel retention, expiry, sudo removal, old-key/unshared/old-name refusal, distinct fresh account and survivor controls; fresh explicit sharing preserves all historical reservations.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fresh-guest-identity-verification.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [lifecycle-personal-guest-identity](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/account-lifecycle/browser.py) — Complete fourth NixOS native journey on f4de549a passed old and fresh personal terminal username/UID/home checks on different VMs with separate sessions; shared-session revocation was not exercised.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fresh-guest-identity-verification.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [fresh same-email team rejoin preserves every surviving guest identity](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/guest_identity_history_test.exs) — Two real retirement/verified-registration generations and explicit team member rejoin preserve owner/teammate boot rosters and every historical allocation; no inherited membership, no member manage and no native home claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fresh-guest-identity-verification.md)."
