#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3009
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "- **machine, recorded**: [upstream success retains immutable custody and explicit replay is independently durable](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/trace-spool/default.nix) — Final eager runtime with pinned protobuf success: exact UID/cgroup refusal, SIGKILL/reboot, Collector outage, immutable ACK archive/replay, quota/privacy/corruption refusal and producer independence in a disposable native machine. The 256-request fixture establishes bounded admission, not deployed throughput or physical power-loss durability.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [successful_forwarding_drains_backlog_eagerly_and_retains_replay_archive](repo:elixir/diagnostics/native/spool/src/main.rs) — Real Unix/Store 32-batch backlog drains under two seconds without the custody mutex during network I/O; exact immutable IDs, timestamps, expiry and bytes survive reopen/replay. The old fixed-success-delay mutant is rejected. Separate injected delivery/expiry failures retain pending custody and publish poison health. This is bounded regression evidence, not strict fairness, fleet sizing or physical guest acceptance.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [upstream success retains immutable custody and explicit replay is independently durable](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/trace-spool/default.nix) — Corrected native fixture returns the pinned Collector's explicit empty partial_success response. Exact UID/cgroup refusals, SIGKILL/reboot, immutable ACK retention/replay, corruption/quota and producer independence pass against the fixed production parser; no production sizing or physical power-loss claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [pinned_collector_reply_and_private_warning_confirm_complete_delivery](repo:elixir/diagnostics/native/spool/src/main.rs) — Actual Unix forwarding validates official OTLP success including zero-rejection warnings, while malformed/truncated/ambiguous replies, nonzero or negative rejection and oversized responses preserve pending delivery. This is transport regression execution, not guest or physical-host acceptance.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [upstream success retains immutable custody and explicit replay is independently durable](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/trace-spool/default.nix) — Canonical hierarchical UID/cgroup identity and foreign refusal, process SIGKILL, reboot, exact retained digest, upstream ACK preservation, replay, bounded quota stress, corrupt-archive startup refusal and producer progress while observer stopped.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [startup_refuses_orphan_pending_mismatched_index_and_missing_tables](repo:elixir/diagnostics/native/spool/src/lib.rs) — Actual SQLite library regression rejects an orphan pending row, mismatched digest index and missing required table at startup. This is unit execution, not native host identity or reboot evidence.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [otel-worker-trace-queue-replay](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/otel-fleet/default.nix) — Corrected fsynced, bounded guest queue accepts a trace during real Tempo outage, survives immediate Collector SIGKILL and restart, and recovers the exact trace over authenticated fleet transport. No prequeue batch or elapsed retry expiry; original deadlines and refusal boundaries retained. No physical host power-loss claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [otel-wireguard-outage-replay](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/otel-fleet/default.nix) — Real authenticated fleet tunnel is down when the corrected guest queue acknowledges intake; immediate Collector SIGKILL and restart retain the trace. Exact Tempo query refuses before tunnel recovery and succeeds afterward within the original deadline. No direct physical route bypass or physical host power-loss claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [application-trace-queue-ack-custody](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/otel-fleet/default.nix) — Corrected private, fsynced 64-entry application queue acknowledges Unix OTLP200 while Tempo is stopped, survives immediate Collector SIGKILL and restart, and delivers its exact trace after backend recovery. Separate guest queue and unprivileged storage refusal remain. No physical host power-loss or production sizing claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [collectorTraceCustody](repo:nix/verification/tests/evaluation/module-configuration.nix) — Evaluated production modules require separate bounded storage/exporter bindings, explicit fsync, enabled queues, unlimited elapsed retry and no asynchronous batch before either trace queue. This configuration regression does not establish runtime recovery or physical durability.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [application-trace-queue-ack-custody](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/otel-fleet/default.nix) — Historical pre-fsync-correction fixture: actual application Unix OTLP200, immediate orderly Collector restart during Tempo outage and exact trace query after backend recovery; independent guest queue retained. Does not establish the subsequent fsync or immediate SIGKILL boundary.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md)."
