on, deterministic backoff doubling to the fifteen-minute/sixteen-failure cap with no expiry, operator manual switch, fetch-only stale window, then verify-only recovery that never re-stages, migrates or switches; published bundle bytes pinned throughout.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-custody-updater.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [def test_recipient_only_rekey_descriptor_handoff(](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/auto-update/custody_histories.py) — Recipient-only rekey through real stage/resolve/descriptor_id handoff with actual ssh-to-age/sops/secretspec: staged bytes published byte-exactly despite a concurrent document replacement at switch time, stale handoff retired at staging entry, handoff keys bound to exact descriptor digests.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-custody-updater.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [def test_custody_wedge_label_backoff_and_recovery(](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/auto-update/custody_histories.py) — Host removed from a still-selected document wedges staging with exact operation_failed/stage label, deterministic backoff, untouched last bundle and uninterrupted serving; both config-removal and custody-restored fixes converge healthy in one tick.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-custody-updater.md)."
