#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3141
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "- **property, present**: [revocation and generation changes fence arbitrary verification sequences](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/security_test.exs) — Generated authority histories..\n- **unit, present**: [replayed and cross-session challenges fail](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/security_test.exs) — Fixture WebAuthn replay and cross-session denial..\n- **machine, recorded**: [native-control-room-authority](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/control-room/browser.py) — Browser first enrollment and elevation using virtual WebAuthn, followed by stored-session revocation and expiry; one serving replica.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-control-room-verification.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [native-control-room-authority](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/control-room/browser.py) — Current packaged verified-TLS browser with virtual WebAuthn: stored-login revocation and mounted expiry/export404, followed by real sign-out revoking independent remembered authority and fresh sign-in/export404 refusal. One serving replica; no hardware-authenticator or independent-host acceptance.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [subsequent login histories separate ordinary access from passkey elevation](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/mfa_login_history_test.exs) — The current two-login signed-assertion property passed all twenty histories/oracles in the 91.7-second pinned-test target, seed 922579, and in the complete c5747868 Marshall gate: 1,476 checks in 1,400.4 seconds, with zero failures/invalids. The narrow 240-second SQL owner tag matches the existing test budget, preserves the default when absent, async sharing, cleanup and all operation-matrix assertions. The earlier full run lost its 120-second SQL owner inside live overview before any failed MFA assertion; the target finished below 120 seconds and does not establish owner-expiry stress. The interrupted development-format target has no acceptance. Production authentication and native-browser behavior are unchanged.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-13-native-guest-coding-clis.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [native-subsequent-mfa-login](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/mfa-login/browser.py) — Three colocated serving replicas, virtual WebAuthn, subsequent magic-link and remembered login, actual backend and WebSocket observations, admin-UI mounted/copied-cookie revocation including a no-MFA account.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-mfa-login-verification.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [remembered login exchange and Sign out everywhere serialize in both orders on three nodes](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/distributed_admission_test.exs) — Three independent BEAMs sharing committed PostgreSQL; both lock orders, copied-credential refusal, mutation-sensitive gates and bounded failure cleanup. No independent-host claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-mfa-login-verification.md).\n- **unit, present**: [remembered enrolled login allows reads, requires its own admin elevation and revokes copied cookies](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/remember_me_login_test.exs) — Updated real HTTP-issued remember cookie test permits ordinary reads, keeps independent admin elevation and preserves copied-cookie revocation. The September 25 recorded run covered the earlier login-MFA policy, not this updated test..\n- **property, recorded**: [generated passkey and SSH key histories match the raw inventory oracle](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/credential_management_history_test.exs) — Real signed WebAuthn ceremonies and SSH key actions over generated register/verify/rename/remove/add/remove/relogin histories; an independent raw-SQL oracle recomputes credential inventory, verification receipts, stored sessions, elevation and completion; every refusal preserves the exact prior inventory; ordinary last-passkey removal revokes every stored session.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-credential-management-histories.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [credential changes require recent elevation and an existing credential](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/credential_management_bounds_test.exs) — Elevation, unknown-credential and fresh-email refusals (including the 299/301-second primary-window boundary) preserve the exact credential and challenge inventory.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-credential-management-histories.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [administrators keep a last passkey; ordinary last removal revokes every session](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/credential_management_bounds_test.exs) — Administrator last-passkey refusal; ordinary last-key removal disables MFA, bumps the generation and revokes two concurrent stored sessions including the issuing one, with the audited kind inventory intact.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-credential-management-histories.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [removing the proving credential kills elevation; another credential preserves it](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/credential_management_bounds_test.exs) — Removing the verification-bound passkey ends elevation and completed login MFA until a retained credential verifies in the same login; removing a different credential preserves both.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-credential-management-histories.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [malformed and oversized payloads consume the challenge without credential effects](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/credential_management_bounds_test.exs) — Malformed/oversized attestation, client data and signatures and over-bound labels consume the single-use challenge without credential or MFA changes; exact ten-passkey, ten-retained-challenge and 100-SSH-key bounds hold and prune recovery succeeds.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-credential-management-histories.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [committed credential lifecycles preserve unrelated fixture history and restore inventory](repo:marshall/test/marshall/committed_credential_inventory_test.exs) — A complete committed passkey/SSH-key lifecycle (enroll, verify, rename, remove, second-session revocation, fresh-email recovery) leaves an unrelated committed credential fixture and the complete public-table row-hash inventory untouched after exact teardown.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-credential-management-histories.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [native-subsequent-mfa-login](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/mfa-login/browser.py) — Three colocated serving replicas, virtual WebAuthn, subsequent magic-link and remembered login of adjacent sessions, actual backend and WebSocket observations, admin-UI mounted/copied-cookie revocation including a no-MFA account, and an expired-ceremony refusal (SQL-backdated challenge deadline) followed by a fresh verified ceremony served by a different replica.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-login-races.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [magic-link sign-in and account revocation serialize in both orders on three nodes](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/distributed_admission_test.exs) — Advisory-gated real sign-in create action versus administrator session revocation, MFA reset and retirement on three independent BEAMs sharing committed PostgreSQL; both orders; issued session and remembered credentials read from committed token rows; ordered-after global revocation remains an intentional fresh sign-in.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-login-races.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [controller sign-out and remembered login exchange serialize in both orders on three nodes](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/distributed_admission_test.exs) — Ordinary sign-out of a remember-only browser raced against an in-flight remembered exchange; exchange committed first survives as an independent session while its credential is then revoked; committed sign-out fences a later exchange into refusal.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-login-races.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [a login revoked between issuance and the success callback refuses the session](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/auth_controller_test.exs) — Revoked-before-callback browser login: clean redirect refusal, no stored session, generic message, closed-reason event without token material.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-login-races.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [challenge issuance prunes expired rows and bounds retained challenges per account](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/security_test.exs) — Retained-row bound of ten per account with the specific :try_later boundary, expired-row pruning on issuance, and refill to the same boundary.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-login-races.md).\n- **unit, present**: [delivered link automatically submits a remembered sign-in once](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/magic_link_flow_test.exs) — HTTP GET preserves the token; sign-in POST issues a stored login and remembered cookie for new, existing and MFA-enabled users; invalid replay is refused. Browser auto-submit is verified separately by the recorded machine test.\n- **machine, recorded**: [assert any(\"remember\" in cookie[\"name\"] for cookie in page.context.cookies())](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/mfa-login/browser.py) — Updated NixOS native browser journey: automatic magic-link sign-in without a second click, remembered cookie, pending MFA, expired-ceremony refusal and cross-replica revocation across three colocated Marshall instances over verified TLS with a virtual WebAuthn authenticator; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-02-automatic-magic-link.md)."
