msgid "- **property, present**: [terminal exchange fences stop generated actor rosters without losing intent](repo:lilly/test/lilly/control/historical_fence_test.exs) — One to four real actors across six terminal exchange classes; all actor processes stop, every durable Store command remains, status stays unavailable and ticks cannot self-recover. No native VMM, Marshall allocation or external restart claim.\n- **machine, recorded**: [restore recovers deleted host bytes and a usable isolated database](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/backups/driver.py) — Recorded native restore drill: the operator-mode boot against the isolated restored database starts exactly the persistence, encryption and authorization children with no Endpoint process, and Oban normalizes to no queues, plugins, stager or peer leadership, so no AshOban trigger or queue consumer runs. Decryption succeeds only with the restored keyring.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-historical-authority-characterization.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [regressed command replay is acknowledged without rolling back durable intent](repo:lilly/test/lilly/control/historical_fence_test.exs) — Historical fixed fence characterization: regressed and duplicate command replay acknowledge after rereading matching-or-newer durable intent without rollback; unknown-pool and corrupt-store receipts fence :command_store_failed without acknowledging; :unauthorized/stale-session results stop actors, terminal and clone/transfer workers, preserve durable intent and never reopen by themselves. The original capture also included an ambient-host inventory assertion removed in the current merge; it establishes no controlled native inventory or Runtime-init fence composition.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-historical-authority-characterization.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [large tracked unit inventory omits descriptions and still rejects unknown resources](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/native-zfs/driver.py) — Incoming d4499c4c merged native subtest passed8.22seconds:56 real sleeping tracked systemd units/cgroups exceed the verbose64KiB inventory frame; compact ID-only inventory accepts, omitted live placement and unknown child cgroup refuse. Ownership.verify_units with actual systemd/cgroups only, without Firecracker or Runtime initialization composition. Complete native-zfs later failed unrelated auto-update enrollment receipt validation, so no complete suite pass.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-historical-authority-characterization.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [physical units unknown to the durable command set fence execution readiness](repo:lilly/test/lilly/control/historical_fence_test.exs) — Incoming bee03919 captured separate-BEAM fake systemctl unknown-unit and failed-scan refusal with exact ID-only arguments; avoids assumptions about the developer host and changes no shared PATH. Latest combined execution remains separate, without native cgroup ownership or historical fleet reactivation claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-launcher.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [a restored journal cannot resolve egress before a fresh running observation](repo:lilly/test/vm/actor_test.exs) — Guest-facing restored-authority refusal: after an actor restart the recovered journal authorizes neither ingress nor egress before the new incarnation records a fresh physical running observation; missing owner metadata and durably superseded intent stay unresolved.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-historical-authority-characterization.md)."
