msgid "- **property, recorded**: [replay credit histories preserve exact output and drain only after consumption](repo:lilly/test/terminal/channel_history_test.exs) — Five generated local TCP Channel/Stream-callback properties cover replay/live byte and frame exhaustion, exact input/wire receipts, duplicates/gap isolation, invalid consumption, EOF with outstanding credit and old-PID rejection by an actual same-ID successor. Both input-credit families and replay byte exhaustion have fixed witnesses. No Stream authentication, guest hello/PTYS, TLS, native isolation or hosted fault claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-29-antithesis-property-audit.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [live host channels cede on renewal and replacement across session takeovers](repo:marshall/test/marshall/terminal/host_takeover_history_test.exs) — Three generated two-takeover histories run actual local Bandit/WebSock host channels with real credential/session/epoch and PostgreSQL directory authority. Explicit renewal and successor registration both close the old process; stale nonce renewal and delayed old hello are refused while current successor output works. HTTPS and guest replies are synthetic; no timer deadline, native Lilly, remote peer or partition claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-29-antithesis-property-audit.md).\n- **property, present**: [generated mailbox pressure sheds only the stalled viewer](repo:marshall/test/marshall/terminal/host_stream_test.exs) — Local HostStream with 60 to 64 queued messages on one stalled task and one to three healthy channels; exact output bound, one slow-viewer signal and channel-close frame, healthy sequences advance after shed. No peer or browser transport.\n- **property, recorded**: [a future output sequence closes its channel while a replay is ignored](repo:marshall/test/marshall/terminal/host_stream_test.exs) — Generated future gap values after one valid output and duplicate replay check viewer closure, state removal and channel-close control; local HostStream frame decoding only, without Lilly interruption or browser reattachment.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-29-antithesis-property-audit.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [generated mass owner death reclaims exactly the available slots](repo:marshall/test/marshall/terminal/peer_budget_test.exs) — Generated saturation at limits two through eight, partial mass owner death, replacement admission and full reuse; no distributed socket or partition claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-29-antithesis-property-audit.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [issued tickets compose current roles, explicit sharing and one-use socket lifetimes](repo:marshall/test/marshall/terminal/attachment_history_test.exs) — Generated actual Bandit/WebSock attachment processes compose issued/current direct roles, creator versus explicit sharing, ticket consumption/mode/expiry and foreign-actor refusals. Input, resize and production one-second idle checks traverse all six withdrawal boundaries, then permit explicit fresh attachment. Root-session, browser-auth, injected epoch/time and synthetic relay limitations are recorded; unchanged scoped VM/access/capacity/session inventories are inspected.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-terminal-attachment-verification.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [completed controls isolate duplicate and stale replies without consuming other messages](repo:marshall/test/marshall/terminal/relay_test.exs) — Generated response outcomes and replay sequences isolate subsequent requests and preserve unrelated mailbox messages.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-terminal-startup-recovery.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [transient failure histories preserve execution and never resurrect closed shells](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/terminal_opening_test.exs) — Generated transient failures preserve execution identity and phase; definitive failure stops automatic opening until a new execution.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-terminal-startup-recovery.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [late replies do not crash or change a connected workspace](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/terminal_live_test.exs) — Connected workspace rendering survives legacy replies; startup notices and recovery to one session have application evidence, not native guest coverage.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-terminal-startup-recovery.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [verified terminal v2 sessions, sharing and reconnect across three Marshall machines](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/terminal.py) — Complete NixOS and Ubuntu native journeys on base 3f679eff, captured tree e710ef1e: personal identity/home/sudo/account restoration, fifty shells, 10,000 sixel images and accessible completion, replay/retained shell, whole-Marshall loss, original database/live deadlines, sharing, writer refusal and grant/login revocation.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-terminal-workspace-verification.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [Unexpected settled terminal attachments](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/browser.py) — Both complete NixOS and Ubuntu journeys on captured tree e710ef1e passed settled selected-only attachment checks throughout the real guest/browser sequence. Closing and closed sockets are excluded; historical pre-CA failure scopes remain in the review.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-terminal-workspace-verification.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [accessibility output keeps mixed-width and blank rows without layout per row](repo:marshall/test/browser/xterm_accessibility_test.mjs) — Actual vendored accessibility methods preserve mixed-width text, logical columns, ARIA positions and scales while batching modeled layout. Includes partial refresh and resize; does not establish native throughput or screen reader acceptance.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-terminal-workspace-verification.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [fleet-accessible-terminal-selection](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/browser.py) — Both complete native journeys on captured tree e710ef1e passed exact ASCII/CJK/combining accessible DOM selection before the full 10,000-image graphics workload and after replay. This establishes DOM-to-xterm selection, not separate assistive-technology integration.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-terminal-workspace-verification.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [create selects once when the listing arrives](repo:marshall/test/browser/terminals_test.mjs) — Both listing/reply orders preserve a later user tab selection across refreshes; no native transport claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-personal-terminal-workspace.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [refusal diagnostics classify the boundary without logging terminal contents](repo:marshall/test/marshall/terminal/viewer_test.exs) — Generated private terminal strings remain absent from authority and credit-refusal diagnostics; socket stop behavior is preserved.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-personal-terminal-workspace.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [only the closed viewer refusal reasons survive tagged process redaction](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/terminal_log_filter_test.exs) — The tagged production filter keeps the ten fixed refusal categories and rejects arbitrary reasons, terminal bytes and original message text.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-personal-terminal-workspace.md).\n- **unit, present**: [an attached viewer survives a late report and closes once the host is lost](repo:marshall/test/marshall/terminal/authority_test.exs) — Database-backed host liveness: a late report keeps an attached viewer and a report beyond the host authority window closes it with authority_host (ADR-0140); no native availability claim..\n- **property, recorded**: [bounded acquisition waits for the same native inode and retains exclusive ownership](repo:lilly/test/host/lock_test.exs) — Generated native lock holds include the one-second roster wait; exclusivity, stable inode and persistent-contention refusal are checked without claiming guest execution.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-personal-terminal-workspace.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [lifecycle-personal-guest-identity](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/account-lifecycle/browser.py) — Complete fourth NixOS native journey on f4de549a passed old and fresh personal terminal username/UID/home checks on different VMs with separate sessions; shared-session revocation was not exercised.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fresh-guest-identity-verification.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [ticket delivery respects current selection and connection](repo:marshall/test/browser/terminals_test.mjs) — Actual mounted-hook late replies attach only the selected connected pane; malformed external replies preserve retries. This does not establish native graphics or transport acceptance.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-terminal-workspace-verification.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [All release Repo connections reclaimed](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/database-recovery/driver.py) — Captured two-machine candidate with the actual release Repo and verified PostgreSQL TLS passed a healthy 20-second active query, one holder and three observed queued statements, 20-second holder/35-second all-connection bounds and row reacquisition; all ten connections disappeared in 27.719 seconds. The original settings and a polling-only candidate both failed the 35-second bound. Full source bases, executable-input equivalence and wider release differences are recorded; the two complete integrated terminal journeys supply separate passing browser-recovery evidence.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-terminal-workspace-verification.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [expected_holder_state](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/database-recovery/driver.py) — Recorded six-case native matrix: idle/active holder crossed with machine crash, bidirectional silent loss and asymmetric client-to-server loss, seed-126 waiter submission permutations, actual release Repo and verified PostgreSQL TLS, three independently observed waiters, ten connections and unchanged twenty/thirty-five-second deadlines. All sessions reclaimed in 19.432–27.882 seconds; row reacquired in every case and positive DROP counters observed in each tested direction. Submission order does not establish queue order. No surviving release contender, repeated reconnect, uncertain commit or hosted claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-02-database-loss-histories.md)."
