msgid "- **unit, present**: [closed native response verifies every boot and kernel identity](repo:protocol/test/kernel_attestation_test.exs) — Pure protocol validation compares expected placement, epoch, challenge, OS and digest fields and validates the boot ID; no guest or transport..\n- **unit, present**: [local proxy framing verifies a boot-bound response across writes](repo:lilly/test/vm/kernel_attestation_test.exs) — A local Unix socket fixture checks bounded CONNECT framing and stale-response refusal; this does not establish Firecracker vsock peer CID enforcement..\n- **unit, present**: [FreeBSD rejects an artifact outside its firmware/disk file set](repo:lilly/test/host/image_test.exs) — Image loading refuses stray files and incomplete native kernel descriptors before an image is usable..\n- **property, recorded**: [state_properties](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/native-kernels/common/ov_vsock_test.c) — The actual shared C parser/credit core passed 400000 generated transitions plus malformed headers, unchanged-on-refusal, credit/counter-wrap and directional shutdown checks with address/undefined-behavior sanitizers. This executes on Linux and does not cover either native wrapper, DMA, kernel scheduling, host CID enforcement or guest isolation.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [and .malformed_length_refused and .disconnected_history_recovered](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/native-transport/driver.py) — Captured FreeBSD token 5e1fd7cf inputs passed in 139 seconds under nested KVM/Firecracker: executing token, CID2/3, native ABI and immutable buffer/capacity refusals, malformed-length/disconnected/reconnect histories and exact sizes 0, 1, 44, 4096, 65535, 65536, 65537, 262144, 1048576. Receipt binds exact image, firmware and VMM digests. No production service closure, wrong-CID injection, device reset, physical isolation or recovery; later inputs require a fresh run.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md).\n- **machine, recorded**: [.boot_ids | unique | length](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/native-services/driver.py) — Protocol/Lilly units cover closed schemas and stale framing through local sockets. Image admission remains closed despite separate native candidates. Lyra compares a read-only executing transport token with a bounded root-owned expected file and separately hashes the kernel file. FreeBSD two-boot candidate assembly checks actual installed bytes/Git/trust and executing sysctl identity. A scoped 139-second nested-KVM run checked the actual FreeBSD socket token/CID2/3, native ABI refusals, oversized/disconnected refusal/recovery and nine exact echo sizes through 1 MiB. Corrected illumos objects passed native nine-module link/install, QEMU file/runtime checks and seven native helper safety tests. The seed-fixed clean-export OmniOS candidate then passed the complete executing-AF40 verifier and native Rust token/CID2/3/refusal/nine-size transport checks under Firecracker with a debugger-only stock pseudo_isa override. The assembler now binds persistent pseudo ISA and serial configuration; exact final-image replay remains required. The final reviewed FreeBSD image 5022d714 passed all five native variants with actual current-boot kernel responses, complete per-boot service oracles and exact image/kernel/firmware/VMM receipts. Linux shared-core properties and extracted listener harnesses retain model scope.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md).\n- **manual, recorded**: [def exercise(](repo:nix/verification/tests/support/native_transport.py) — A diagnostic OmniOS Firecracker boot ran the actual separately packaged Rust listener: executing token4b1627f1, CID3/2, native malformed bind/connect/token/privilege/buffer/capacity refusals, malformed-length/disconnect recovery and all nine exact sizes through 1 MiB passed. The boot required a debugger-only stock pseudo_isa override and disposable loader settings; it is separate from the final reproducible image or service gate, reset and admission.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [test_digest_size_and_regular_file_boundary](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/native-kernels/illumos/test_native_candidate.py) — All seven helper boundary tests passed on the host and natively under the pinned OmniOS image Python 3.12.3: exact 26-object/nine-module layout, digest/size/regular-file/FIFO/symlink and alternate-root/ownership/configuration refusals. Separate native linkage and boot archive execution do not establish Firecracker virtio-vsock, reset or isolation.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md).\n- **manual, recorded**: [def assemble(](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/native-kernels/illumos/native_image.py) — The seed-fixed exact4b1627f1 kit imported a separately identified pinned-image pool, cloned its root, linked/installed all nine modules and payload, rebuilt the archive, selected bootfs and exported cleanly. QEMU checked installed files, Git, trust, exact resolver persistence and five disabled stock services. A separate diagnostic Firecracker boot passed the complete executing-AF40/file verifier after a debugger-only stock pseudo_isa override. Final persistent-image replay, complete services, isolation and admission remain pending.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md).\n- **manual, recorded**: [service_bundle type=\"profile\"](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/omnios/native-services.xml) — The stock SMF seed lacked imported cloud-init services. Binding SVCCFG_REPOSITORY to the validated clone repository before native import/apply passed without changing the live repository. Seed-fixed native assembly and fresh QEMU verification confirmed all fou