ecovery and all nine exact sizes through 1 MiB passed. The boot required a debugger-only stock pseudo_isa override and disposable loader settings; it is separate from the final reproducible image or service gate, reset and admission.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [test_digest_size_and_regular_file_boundary](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/native-kernels/illumos/test_native_candidate.py) — All seven helper boundary tests passed on the host and natively under the pinned OmniOS image Python 3.12.3: exact 26-object/nine-module layout, digest/size/regular-file/FIFO/symlink and alternate-root/ownership/configuration refusals. Separate native linkage and boot archive execution do not establish Firecracker virtio-vsock, reset or isolation.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md).\n- **manual, recorded**: [def assemble(](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/native-kernels/illumos/native_image.py) — The seed-fixed exact4b1627f1 kit imported a separately identified pinned-image pool, cloned its root, linked/installed all nine modules and payload, rebuilt the archive, selected bootfs and exported cleanly. QEMU checked installed files, Git, trust, exact resolver persistence and five disabled stock services. A separate diagnostic Firecracker boot passed the complete executing-AF40/file verifier after a debugger-only stock pseudo_isa override. Final persistent-image replay, complete services, isolation and admission remain pending.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md).\n- **manual, recorded**: [def assemble(](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/native-kernels/illumos/native_image.py) — Historical wz4r assembly passed nine modules, 764 payload records, all three SMF validations, the safe native SSH executable guard, five stock service disables, four network removals, read-only receipt extraction/export and clean shutdown. Its sealed disk e7fc0c04 was later found to contain a stale cached kit with the old /workspace/* Git config and pre-fencing workspace receiver, so it cannot qualify current workspace, lease, service, growth or recovery behavior. The current source-derived kit requires a fresh target-native assembly. Runtime and admission remain false.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md).\n- **manual, recorded**: [service_bundle type=\"profile\"](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/omnios/native-services.xml) — The stock SMF seed lacked imported cloud-init services. Binding SVCCFG_REPOSITORY to the validated clone repository before native import/apply passed without changing the live repository. Seed-fixed native assembly and fresh QEMU verification confirmed all four cloud-init instances and stock SSH disabled plus exact resolver persistence. This establishes startup authority configuration, not complete Overalls service acceptance.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md).\n- **manual, recorded**: [def validate_native_services(root: Path) -> None:](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/native-kernels/illumos/native_image.py) — All three exact corrected manifests pass actual native svccfg validation; a deliberate Uncommitted mutant fails with the expected enum error. Assembly and booted verification now require this schema-only gate. No method/import/readiness or corrected normal-boot claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md).\n- **manual, recorded**: [illumos-static-device-lifetime](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/native-kernels/illumos/viosock.c) — Independent control-flow review confirms fallible resources precede DRIVER_OK, runtime detach refuses, and unavoidable postactivation failures retain bounded DMA/interrupt-visible resources while withholding this device readiness. Source evidence only; build