corded**: [`machine_key` nullable `NO` and zero rows with null keys](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-15-user-threads.md) — Read-only observations on 2026-10-15 at 22:35:55-22:36:04 UTC found both hosts healthy on exact contraction revision 32624e1bf80df120beb69b923eee4362427aee23 with healthy TLS readiness. SQL confirmed NOT NULL and zero null keys. The reported recovered thread retained its same running VM and completed initial turn, with one VM and one turn total; no new retry or prompt was issued. This verifies deployment and that continuity, not native archive/reopen or fault recovery.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-15-user-threads.md).\n- **manual, recorded**: [one VM existed for its machine admission key](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-15-user-threads.md) — One authorized public retry of the reported failed thread on deployed expansion revision d5e03c080204a33a11b8c136e983593630e4fccf reached ready. Read-only SQL showed one running VM for its admission key, one completed initial objective turn, and completed provisioning and title jobs. This records that recovery only; native archive/reopen, worker-loss recovery and broader provider behavior remain separate.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-15-user-threads.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [thread creation requires an explicit machine admission key](repo:marshall/test/marshall/threads_machine_key_test.exs) — The Ash resource refuses thread creation without its explicit machine admission key; this does not establish deployed schema convergence.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-15-user-threads.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [the database refuses a missing machine admission key](repo:marshall/test/marshall/threads_machine_key_test.exs) — PostgreSQL refuses an update that would remove the machine admission key after the dependent migration; this does not establish fleet deployment.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/revie