reads.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [a ready thread routes prompts to its bound agent thread](repo:marshall/test/marshall/threads_test.exs) — The worker binds the registered root and thread; a prompt and request-key replay resolve to the same low-level turn, and the prompt plus a durable assistant event advance the enclosing user-thread activity clock after commit. The projection uses the current binding; native cross-node and archived/deleting behavior remain unverified; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-16-thread-sharing.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [retry resets a failed thread and archive requires current creator](repo:marshall/test/marshall/threads_test.exs) — Foreign archive is refused, and the creator can retry a failed thread and archive an unbound failed thread.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-15-user-threads.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [reopening an archived thread clears the old binding and queues a fresh admission](repo:marshall/test/marshall/threads_test.exs) — Reopen preserves the original create key, changes the machine key and clears the current binding; the fixture does not establish native VM replacement.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-15-user-threads.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [create replay retains its original identity through archive and reopen](repo:marshall/test/marshall/threads_lifecycle_test.exs) — The original request key resolves to one high-level thread while archive and reopen change its lifecycle and machine admission key.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-15-user-threads.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [archiving a pending machine retains its binding until physical deletion](repo:marshall/test/marshall/threads_lifecycle_test.exs) — A provisioned but pending VM keeps its thread binding while deletion is pending; an injected deleted outcome permits archival, repeated delete reuses its operation, and a later provision job cannot resurrect it