#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3831
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Acceptance requires the deployed revision, healthy required services, current host\nreports, an authorized guest lifecycle, terminal/SSH access, and working configured\nmail/provider paths. A build or push alone proves none of these runtime outcomes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3839
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Account retirement requires current administrator membership, recent passkey\nverification and typed email confirmation. Self-retirement and retiring a current\nteam owner are refused. Transfer team ownership before retrying. Accepted retirement\nimmediately disables the old UUID and its browser/remembered authority, revokes\naccess to its owned workloads, and queues physical cleanup. The receipt stays\nbound to the old UUID even if the requester later loses administrative authority.\nBusy resize or unavailable hosts leave cleanup pending and storage holds intact.\nAn administrator gains no Customer guest-content access through retirement."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3843
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Account role changes, global browser revocation, MFA reset, invitation and\nretirement retain current actor authority through their audit commit. Actor and\ntarget User rows are acquired in sorted order after the installation latch;\nretirement first holds the target's exclusive account-admission fence. Actor-only\nrows exclude authority mutations while allowing unrelated foreign-key references;\ntargets retain their strong row lock before team work and identity changes. Completed\nrevocation refuses later mutations, including an existing retirement receipt.\nPreviously committed durable cleanup remains valid after actor demotion.\nThe [account authority review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-admin-account-authority-verification.md)\nrecords five generated histories, 27 three-process schedules and passing native\nstale-page/reset acceptance with verified TLS and virtual WebAuthn. Full component\nacceptance and the native run retain their captured revision; hardware authenticators,\nphysical hosts and rollout remain separate. Prior Control room and retirement\nresults retain their exact scopes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3851
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Activation stops only what the candidate changes (ADR-0165): a consumer,\nsocket or secret preparation unit whose unit file or drop-ins resolve to a\ndifferent store path than the active system's, or that exists on one side\nonly; the consumers of a secret bundle whose staged files differ from the live\nbundle or whose preparation unit itself changed (the manifest's\n`bundleConsumers`); consumers the candidate no longer lists; and the consumers\nthat require, bind to or are part of any of those (`consumerDependents`), so a\nretained dependent's restart cannot pull a stopped unit back up. The resource\npolicy oneshot, whose command line names the per-release manifest, is not\nrestarted by the switch (the updater applies the policy itself), so Lilly,\nwhich requires it, is not stopped by propagation. Every other running consumer, its sockets and its secret\npreparation stay up across the switch, and `update.units_retained` records\nhow many, so a Marshall-only release no longer restarts Lilly, drops its\ncontrol channel or exits guest actors. A changed unit follows the ordered\nstops, deadlines and restoration below unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3855
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Active model context is separate from retained transcript history. An immutable\nsnapshot identifies applied instructions, their source digests, selected skill\nversions, working directory, configuration owner, collaboration mode and\nreasoning. A checkpoint summarizes covered eligible work; reconstruction adds\naccepted continuation exactly once. Coverage includes the active turn's event\nfrontier as well as turn eligibility, because a later queued prompt can be\nrecorded before an active turn's tool result. Tool calls and their results stay\ntogether. Transcript visibility and retention do not change when context is\ncompacted."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3859
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Actor restart begins without volatile execution proof or a proof-target binding.\nRecovery must verify the current confined VMM before publishing boot or live rows.\nAn exit observer retained after a negative observation preserves its genuine\nterminal report; it cannot restore withdrawn authority. Replacement VMMs require\ntheir own verified target and armed watcher before receiving the longer backstop.\nStopping the actor closes its observer while independently managed guests survive.\nSee the [execution proof boundary](#lifecycle) and scoped\n[verification evidence](#coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3863
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Actual TLS pending-call properties observe a healthy request and one through\nthree outstanding requests before close4001 or draining4008. Ziggy preserves\nunsupported_version for4001 and authority_unavailable for4008; Porsche preserves\nunsupported_version versus transport_error. The original adapters misclassified\npending4001 as outages; the repaired focused files passed3Ziggy and9Porsche checks.\nDomain authorization, provider effects, native rollout and hosted mixed-version\nacceptance remain separate. See the\n[control review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-control-first-envelope.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3867
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Actual parent dataset GUID as a decimal string."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3868
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Actual unsigned 64-bit zpool GUID as a decimal string."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3869
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Actual-supervisor generated histories inspect file bytes, inode identity, drain\nand retry in disposable Linux namespaces; their ready files represent synthetic\nregistration. A dedicated strict NixOS guest journey passed invalid-format and\nregistration-timeout recovery with the same supervisor, exact prior executable,\nfresh Marshall fences and completed operator tool work after each failure.\nDirect candidate injection bypasses artifact delivery. The\n[recovery review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-guest-cli-recovery.md)\nkeeps these scopes separate from historical two-distribution private delivery,\npower-loss/I/O failures and production rollout. Registration is readiness, not\ncode attestation or semantic rollback authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3873
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Additional arguments passed to each module in addition to ones\nlike `lib`, `config`,\nand `pkgs`, `modulesPath`."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3877
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Additional canonical IPv4 networks denied to guests, including public management endpoints."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3881
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Administrative access path. Console-only deployments must disable administrative OpenSSH."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3885
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Admission binds the current stored login, write grant, account incarnation,\nlive host session, gateway identity, placement, execution epoch/generation,\nrelease and origin. Renewal rechecks all of them except the provisioner's control\nsession: a Lilly restart opens a new session while the execution and the\ndetached bridge stay current, so a renewal while Lilly reconnects is answered\n`unavailable` (Audi retries within the unchanged lease) and succeeds once the new\nsession reports\n([ADR-0192](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0192-staged-detached-ingress.md)).\nA stale report on a live session still refuses. Unsafe HTTP and WebSocket requests require the exact origin;\nsame-site sibling origins cannot use the credential. Missing/mismatched capability,\nretired accounts, stale logins, changed execution and expired leases refuse without\nfallback. Generic guest-web visibility or port settings cannot grant editor access.\nAn upgraded editor or guest-web WebSocket ends with its lease, either peer's close\nor 60 s without a browser frame; the gateway listener's 5 s HTTP read timeout does\nnot apply to it, so a client with a 5 s keepalive is not cut off\n([regression test](repo:audi/test/http_proxy_test.exs))."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3889
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Admission combines current usage, policy budgets, configured overheads, holds,\nimage requirements, and freshness. CPU/RAM budgets are mutable policy; changing a\nbudget does not kill existing guests. IOPS remains unknown unless supported by an\nexplicit measurement source. Pool-level I/O is not per-VM I/O."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3893
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Admission reports carry effective CPU/memory limits, measured capacity headroom,\nverified image IDs, execution and terminal capability, the Inception image ID,\nand each pool's current GUID-bound physical accounting. Report inventory keys\nare strings only; any other key refuses the report. Arbitrary inventory,\nutilization, logical-used/compression observations and native I/O diagnostics do\nnot travel to Marshall. Busy retains the previous pool observation and its age;\nunavailable revokes freshness and credit. Collector, Grafana and Tempo outages\ncannot create capacity or revoke live control authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3901
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Admit port 80 on the proxy address from any source through the fleet perimeter (ADR-0181), so the public CA can reach HTTP-01 challenges. The listener serves only challenges and HTTPS redirects."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3905
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Adoption of an already running, proven confined VM preserves its physical boot\nchallenge and execution epoch while updating the durable boot generation to the\nexact current running intent. This permits the same physical boot's trust receipt\nto be reused; it does not reuse a previous generation's readiness acknowledgement.\nA new physical boot cannot use that receipt. Metadata properties and native\nrepeated-start guest readiness with unchanged process identity passed. The\ncomplete native clone matrix also passed; physical foreign/corrupt ownership\nrefusal is not established by this scoped result."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3909
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "After a gateway service credential rotates, a fresh acknowledgement of the same\nactive wildcard may replace the installation row only for a newer generation of\nthat same service and exact fingerprint. The previous credential cannot rebind\nit. Generated ingress and focused certificate tests pass this database path;\nnative gateway rotation and live route restoration remain unverified."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3917
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "After a running observation, the actor also starts `lilly-vm-watch` on the\nverified Firecracker process. The watcher holds a pidfd for that process and\nwatches its unit cgroup. When the process dies or the cgroup empties, it\nreports the exit within milliseconds, and the actor deletes the live row at\nonce and logs `vm.watch_ended`. A crashed or confused watcher also revokes,\nwhich fails closed. Without the helper, the two-second deadline alone applies."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3921
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "After activation, inspect current Audi asset readiness and exact image identity.\nOnly gateways with live matching immutable assets publish editor/webview discovery.\nThe guest `overalls-vscode-web` unit is the broker; personal worker units have their\nown systemd ownership and native lifetime. Restarting the broker does not reset\nsaved editor state or prove that workers exited. See [monitoring](#monitoring) and\n[recovery](#recovery) for authority and retention boundaries. Dungarees activated\n`0fcab4f6`, then loader correction `849d8022`, healthy with zero updater failures;\nthis records host activation, not a production editor journey. Overalls build\nfailed before activation because its\nstandalone image-ID script omitted the `EditorRelease` dependency required by\nmanifest v3. The correction loads it before the shared `ImageManifest` validator,\nincluding the Inception standalone fixture. Derive identity from the exact\ninstalled manifest; do not replace its validator or relabel retained images.\nThe exact corrected Overalls default-image evaluation and later 309-second local\nfull deployment bundle passed. Overalls subsequently activated `849d8022` healthy\nwith zero updater failures. Its anonymous machine-code request redirected to\nsign-in, proving only deployed unauthenticated route behavior. Keep bundle, host\nactivation and authenticated editor acceptance as separate evidence in\nthe [review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\nBoth hosts subsequently activated `af01b4b9` healthy with zero updater failures;\nthe updater revision and host system closure are separate from a browser-visible\nproduction workbench. Existing VM disks retain their original image capability."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3925
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "After an approved destination and private runtime files are provisioned, enable\n`services.overallsOtelFleet.burnAlerts` on the central telemetry host. Restart\n`alertmanager.service` to reload systemd credentials after changing a file.\nInspect service status and the `fleet-burn-delivery` Prometheus job; notification\nfailure counters indicate failed attempts, while successful requests still need\nreceiver-side receipt verification. Startup validates HTTPS and the completed\nconfiguration. Non-HTTPS destinations refuse startup. Production currently leaves\nthis capability disabled while destination provisioning is unresolved.\nAfter correcting a startup refusal, run `systemctl reset-failed alertmanager.service`\nand restart the service to clear any systemd start limit.\nNinety-day retention and seven-day objectives are independent."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3929
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "After an independent root copy is flushed and published, Lilly's catalogued\nmaterialization event records the actual `reflink`/`offload`/`copy` method and a closed\n`template`/`verified` source kind. A template source carries only the UUIDs\nof its validated ready Ash record and native incarnation;\nthe uncached path carries neither. No image string, filesystem path or command\noutput enters the event.\nBenchmark readers can correlate the record UUID with host/pool-bound lifecycle\ndiagnostic timestamps from the host-local reviewed event for staging-to-ready\nconstruction cost. Those events emit after journal fsync and confirmed writer release to structured\nlogs and OpenTelemetry with resource, host/pool UUIDs, revision and persisted microsecond\ntime. Marshall receives no template history. Diagnostic custody never authorizes\na copy or establishes a native seal."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3941
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "After reviewing public users and host inventory, use a retained recovery identity:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3949
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "After the boot-generation repair, native retry replay passed in 8.83 seconds,\nand repeated public Start of the OSS copy passed with unchanged native process\nidentity, inherited guest markers and subsequent divergent writes. The run\nfailed later before cancellation at an incorrect stopped-state precondition:\nan unpublished allocation has pending observed state and stopped desired state.\nThe corrected cancellation fixture uses a fixed 512 MiB incompressible guest\nwitness and requires occupied native stream custody, an offered unfinished copy,\nno publication or destination Start, pending observed state and no running VMM.\nIts public cancellation measurement and exact replay passed in 8.48 seconds;\nsource restoration, disk GUID, destination archival/dataset removal and transfer\nslot release also passed. The full run failed later at ordinary cloned-guest\nrelocation with source_unavailable. A disposable read-only preflight now waits\nfor sixteen boolean source host/pool and reservation predicates before public\nrelocation and the initial faulted clone submission. One read-only database\nsnapshot and clock distinguish configured freshness from a stricter report-age\nmargin. Bounded polling inside the fixture avoids repeated release startup and\nages between separate reads. A failed earlier preflight showed only its tightened\nfreshness checks false; production staleness was not established. The atomic\nextension changes no admission authority. The final complete native cloning-fleet\npassed in 1539.61 seconds: repeated Start retained process identity; retry and\ncancellation measurement replay passed in 15.46 and 8.40 seconds; physical cleanup,\nboth cloned-guest relocations and audit after source deletion passed. Earlier\nfailures retain their historical scopes. Relocation destination retry/cancellation\naccounting and native foreign/corrupt boot refusal remain separate gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3953
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "After the user saves an origin, the extension requests optional browser access\nto that exact normalized origin and registers its packaged detector there. The\ndetector marks the current Overalls document with a local installed attribute.\nMarshall observes that attribute only to hide setup prompts on the home page; it\ndoes not establish login, machine, thread, terminal, editor or launch authority.\nMissing configuration, denied or withdrawn site access, registration failure and\ndetector unavailability keep setup visible. Registration is reconciled on startup\nand origin changes, while a failed change retains the last working configuration."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3957
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Age passed to nix-collect-garbage --delete-older-than. Generations\nyounger than this are preserved."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3961
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Agents rollout ([ADR-0171](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0171-windows-guest-agents.md)):\nthe first converged push carries the `windows-v1` agent set and capability\ntable, the vsock-capable firmware jail, the then-current `{ path; standby }`\nimage shape (with `standby = true` on the Linux entries; ADR-0177 later removed\nthe `standby` key), the 48 GiB template budget on both\nhosts and the Windows agents code with no image staged. Because the Windows\ninstallation is not byte-stable, the image is then built once, its closure\ncopied to both hosts with `nix copy`, and the same store path verified on each\n(and `disk.raw` verified sparse) before the second push stages it in\n`fleet/guest-images.nix` without standby metadata; hosts substitute the image\ninstead of each building a different one with a different identity. The\nprocedure is in [docs/operations/nixos.md](repo:docs/operations/nixos.md); acceptance is recorded in\nthe [agents review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-14-windows-guest-agents.md)\nand the [multi-OS review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-16-multi-os-guest-images.md).\n"
msgstr ""

