#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3972
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "All Elixir services share the reviewed Events catalog implementation and official\nOpenTelemetry SDK through the separate `elixir/diagnostics/` application. Diagnostic\nmetadata uses typed finite schemas, numeric measurements and validated identifiers;\ncredentials, arbitrary exception text, provider bodies, command arguments and\nterminal bytes are excluded. Host/service provenance comes from authenticated local\nproducer bindings. Routine export is bounded and asynchronous; physical outcomes\nand application commits remain independent of observability acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3976
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "All seven selected exact immutable images now have separate recorded successful\ncreate/readiness, strict personal-account CLI SSH, stop with an independent\ncurrent-owner stopped checkpoint, same-VM restart, repeated strict SSH and\ncompleted deletion. The matrix review's typed aggregate binds all 49 stage\nreceipts and four additional Arch/Alma read-only sudo/helper checks at distinct\ntimes and recorded revision contexts. Fresh OmniOS `122228` supplies the owner\ncheckpoint missing from its earlier `091638` journey. This scoped milestone\ndoes not establish a simultaneous same-revision run, broader enabled-capability\nacceptance, revocation, native isolation, interrupted growth or physical recovery."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3980
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "All seven selected image identities now bind separately recorded strict\npersonal-account SSH and current-owner create/readiness, stop, independent\nstopped checkpoint, same-VM restart, repeated SSH and completed deletion. The\nfresh OmniOS checkpoint is an owner-authorized control-plane observation,\nseparate from independent physical absence. Those 49 stage receipts establish\nthe scoped lifecycle journeys at their recorded revisions; they do not establish\nevery enabled guest capability, revocation, physical isolation or recovery."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3984
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "All signed-in users may read the Control room's bounded, redacted projections.\nThe former fleet diagnostic log reader is retired from Marshall under ADR-0149;\nGrafana has separate operator authentication and query-only store authority.\nAdministrative mutations require current administrator membership and passkey\nelevation; ADR-0160 defines the new fifteen-minute receipt and inline retry above.\nThe historical results below exercise the prior five-minute flow.\nControl-room visibility does not grant access to\nanother user's VM, terminal, guest web service, or SSH account."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3988
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "All twelve Elixir applications declare Covenant as a development/test dependency\nwith `runtime: false`; production releases gain no contract service or runtime\ndependency. Each application's `contracts/` tree names obligations, and tagged\ntests under `test/contract/` provide executable evidence. Precommit runs\n`mix covenant.check --no-run`, while the ordinary ExUnit run retains its existing\nformatters and adds `Covenant.Formatter` for runtime results."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3992
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Also bind fleet TLS to loopback for colocated clients when the main fleet bind uses a private interface."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3996
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An Ash domain groups resource actions and their code interfaces. It is a business\nboundary inside an application. It does not create a service, database or process.\nThe diagrams and resource inventory below are extracted from literal declarations."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4000
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An Inception deployment generates its own persistent SSH CA beside its existing\nprivate instance identities. It never receives the parent's CA private key.\nIts public policy follows the accepted nested namespace, and inner gateways use\nthe shared certificate installer and renewal units. Each deployment is a separate\nSSH trust domain."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4004
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An active web request retains exact execution, endpoint policy revision and app\nport. Ordinary web and SSH stream grants last at most thirty seconds from each\ncontrol request start; nested streams remain bounded by their five-second\nenvironment publication. A delayed reply cannot restart the deadline. Catalog\nand DNS snapshots last at most five seconds. Loss of current login or sharing,\na changed policy/execution, expiry or control failure closes traffic. A refused\nMarshall renewal need not immediately mark the durable row closed; the gateway\ncloses its transport and the previous lease still has its bounded deadline.\nRe-addition may authorize a fresh request. Closed or expired streams never revive.\nGenerated Audi guard checks permute seven independent local TCP streams, echo\nbytes before each lease fence, then verify owner death and socket closure for\nexpiry, delayed expired renewal, changed binding, revocation, guard loss and\nsuspension. A second generated history retains one live TCP owner across an\naccepted renewal and reordered stale renewal, obsolete expiry and later\naccepted renewal, checks its deadline and continued echo, then closes the same\nsocket after revocation, expired reply or changed binding. These checks do not\nexercise owner survival past the former deadline after renewal, the SSH\nchannel's frame gates or a partitioned Marshall renewal.\nThe [private browser verification](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-private-web-verification.md)\nrecords generated histories and the execution status of the dedicated native\nteam withdrawal journey. Existing public-policy, browser-code, SSH, outage and\nintegration renewal evidence retains its original scope."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4008
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An additional controlled schedule runs opposite-source relocations and clone\nactivation on three independent peers. Before release, every tagged backend\nblocking chain reaches a separate holder, with a direct transaction-ID wait.\nExact committed endpoints, durable activation, accounting and fixture restoration\npassed the focused property (seed219491,51.6seconds,exit0). This does not establish\nnative transfer, hosted fault search or untested cross-resource lock cycles."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4012
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An administrator using a non-Customer machine through an override returns to\nFleet workloads when verification ends. A terminal/detail page explains the\nexpiry before returning; selecting that machine starts a fresh privileged\nopening. Resize hides its mutation controls but keeps the draft in its URL and\noffers the same recovery link. Owner and sharing rights continue without\nelevation, and foreign Customer refusal never offers verification as recovery."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4016
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An administrator with no passkey is sent to `/settings?return_to=…#security`,\nthe sign-in section of the account page, with an allowlisted return path. First-key setup uses email authentication completed within five\nminutes; missing freshness requires a new email sign-in. The administrator then\nreturns to the original page and explicitly retries the action. No administrative\narguments survive setup navigation and enrollment alone does not elevate the\nlogin. Further passkey changes require an existing key verified within fifteen\nminutes; a key cannot prove its own\nincomplete enrollment. Removal of the proving key ends elevation immediately,\nand an administrator cannot remove the last key. Current Cedar ownership,\nsharing and profile checks still govern machine access: even elevated\nadministrators are refused foreign Customer resources. See\n[security boundaries](#security) and [workflow continuation](#workflows)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4024
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An archived owning team refuses fresh admission, renewal, configuration reads\nand management even when membership and attachment rows survive. Pending peer\ntokens also refuse without consumption. The generated\n[archival property](repo:marshall/test/marshall/galileo/renewal_history_test.exs)\nrecords passing direct/peer and attached/unattached refusal histories using actual\ninternal Ash archival. There is no public team archival journey; production\narchival at two-host rollout `b96443ff` refused real guest forwarding with 503,\nCLI show/attachment/removal with forbidden, and an unexpired pending token\nwithout consumption. A live-team bearer control passed immediately beforehand.\nNative stalled-stream cancellation timing after team archival remains unmeasured."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4028
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An authenticated exchange also rolls back a valid capacity report when a\npending command cannot be reconciled. Generated retries with a corrupted\ndurable command snapshot leave the host's report stale and the operation\npending. A current owner stop cancels that ordinary operation without requiring\nfresh host telemetry, after which the next exchange accepts a new report and\nstop command. This local test does not cover Lilly's retry delay, retained\nrelocation-cleanup obligations or native host effects. Whether one bad command\nshould withhold all host reports remains a recovery-policy gap.\nLilly classifies transport and temporary exchange failures as retryable, keeps\nits durable commands and session identity, and reports not ready while backing\noff. The retry delay starts at one second, doubles, and is capped at four\nseconds (plus jitter). A longer delay would barely reduce load on Marshall,\nsince hosts normally report every second, but after Marshall recovers it would\nstretch a healthy host's report gap past the host authority window\n(ADR-0140). A generated [Runtime history](repo:lilly/test/lilly/control/historical_fence_test.exs)\nchecks bounded backoff and restored status readiness after a completed exchange\nwith a new report timestamp. It injects handler results locally; a real network\npartition, client retry and Marshall host-freshness recovery still need a\ncross-service fault test.\nSince ADR-0142 these exchanges travel over Lilly's control WebSocket. A\ndropped socket resolves an in-flight exchange as unproven, which Lilly treats\nas a transport error with the same backoff; the socket itself reconnects with\nfull jitter capped at four seconds, so a restarted Marshall is reached inside\nthe report windows. Marshall's refusal names map\nto the same error classes the HTTPS statuses produced.\nTerminal exchange errors fence Lilly's actor supervisor instead of retrying.\nGenerated [actor-roster histories](repo:lilly/test/lilly/control/historical_fence_test.exs)\ndrive one to four actors across the six terminal classes, then require every\nactor to stop, every durable command to remain and a later tick to stay fenced.\nThis local control test does not establish native VMM survival, Marshall hold\nretention or external-restart outcome drain.\nA generated [readiness boundary property](repo:lilly/test/lilly/control/readiness_test.exs)\nvaries report age at the fifteen-second limit and one to four durable actor\nauthorities. A missing or stale actor denies readiness even with a fresh report.\nThis direct predicate test does not establish a new runtime incarnation or\nstatus-socket behavior after restart.\nA generated [terminal version history](repo:lilly/test/lilly/control/historical_fence_test.exs)\nvaries transient errors before an `unsupported_version` result. It checks that\nLilly fences, retains Store intent and refuses another tick; HTTP decoding and\nthe terminal WebSocket's separate 404 retry path remain outside that test.\nImage identities, storage GUIDs, placement identity, and execution generations\ntravel with commands. Marshall rejects observations that no longer match durable\nownership. Lilly retains physical receipts independently of the control connection.\nTransactional business and security audit rows remain in Marshall and commit\nwith the action they describe. Lilly lifecycle transitions and transfer byte\nprogress do not enter Marshall's audit or diagnostic tables. Physical outcomes,\nreadiness facts, operational receipts, billing and live authorization stay on\nthe control protocol because they establish durable domain facts."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4032
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An earlier instrumented native clone rerun failed before retry/cancellation at\nthe published copy's exact `transfer_busy` relocation refusal. Running guest\nand retained-slot checks passed; the actual differing refusal was not recorded.\nFinite refusal diagnostics now preserve that assertion. Earlier scoped retry\nevidence remains valid; the full matrix and cancellation remain unproven.\nThe next run passed that refusal and retry replay in 9.11 seconds, then failed\nthe OSS copied guest's start; its console diagnostic failed before connection.\nClosed terminal-stage labels and thirty early host boot-state snapshots now\ndistinguish those gates without exposing boot challenges or granting authority.\nThese diagnostic snapshots remain pending native execution."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4036
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An earlier scoped FreeBSD nested-KVM service gate passed eight\nbootstrap/network, current-boot identity, withheld\nreadiness, trust, flush, workspace-refusal and terminal HELLO/PING checks in\n197 seconds. It used a historical candidate before the final kernel/account\npayload, and does not establish checkout, SSH, execution, PTY, isolation or\nrecovery acceptance. A separate FreeBSD transport gate passed with\ntoken/CID/credit-window and ABI refusal assertions. A stock\nOmniOS probe passed native PTY shell/controlling-terminal,\nresize and inherited-descriptor checks; it does not execute the full terminal\nsession protocol. The current source-qualified OmniOS image then passed the\ncomplete native service fixture over two clean boots: current-boot identity,\nreadiness, trust, flush, workspace, terminal, SSH, executor fencing, retained\nhome and clean shutdown all passed. The runner requires status zero and the\nbounded `syncing file systems... done` serial marker before recording a clean\nillumos boot. Policy, supervised daemon recovery, physical isolation and image\nqualification remain pending. The separate OmniOS abrupt-crash receipt\ncovers process SIGKILL and same-disk recovery; neither it, the capability table\nnor these\nservice receipts establish fleet acceptance. See the\n[native kernel attestation review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4040
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An elevated administrator can send an invitation from **Users**. The\nrecipient becomes an ordinary account only after explicitly consuming a valid\nemail link. Delivery uses an encrypted outbox; requesting an invitation does not\nprove that a mailbox received it."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4044
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An exactly owned ready ZFS child can retain storage identity even when its boot\nbundle fails the current launch codec. The allocation audit still requires the\ndurable claim/spec, native host/pool/VM nonce and GUID, owned mounts, complete\nclosed file set, drive UID/type/length and matching `disk.json` plus\n`disk-ready.json`. Any failure there, or an unknown child, still withholds the\npool. A retained invalid marker must remain a safely contained private\nsingle-link file bounded to 16 KiB; boot artifacts must be nonempty root-owned\nsingle-link regular files with mode 0444, and total marker/artifact sizes must fit\nthe protocol's 1 GiB bundle reservation. If only the bundle contents are invalid,\nthe child is recognized with no allocation credit while otherwise valid\nneighbors remain measurable. No invalid marker content is decoded."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4048
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An expired/revoked personal cookie or its stored login requires authentication\nagain and redirects a safe browser visit into the fixed approval/sign-in flow.\nA fresh real sign-in can replace that host cookie; it never revives the old cookie\nor lease. Current write/account/Customer denial returns forbidden. Missing route or\nexecution or unanswered stored-login lookup remains unavailable, preserving the\ndifference between lost browser identity and infrastructure authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4052
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An explicit version refusal stops automatic DNS refresh, SSH key publication\nand wildcard certificate polling/readiness work. Over the control WebSocket\n(ADR-0142) the refusal is HTTP 426 at upgrade, close 4001, or a request\nanswered `unsupported_version`. Polling and readiness stop until an operator repairs compatibility and\nrestarts the service. Transient failures retain normal retries. Existing DNS\nsnapshots, local key files and installed certificates keep their original bytes\nand expiry; refusal does not renew authority. Fleet retires its temporary\nreadiness scheduler without waiting for a reply and its active jobs die even\nwhen the scheduler is suspended."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4056
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An identical prompt request key retains the original turn. A user who chooses to\nretry must submit a new invocation/request identity with current write access.\nAn old approved CLI session cannot bypass withdrawn sharing. Inspect effects in\nthe guest before choosing to retry an uncertain operation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4060
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An interrupted native property change can leave an owned template unmounted.\nRecovery remounts only after its owner matches the recorded template shape. Property changes, remount, rename and destruction use a 120-second native\nbound; timeout preserves uncertainty rather than granting capacity. Terminal\nmetadata is removed from Lilly's private catalog without waiting for a\nCollector ACK."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4064
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An interrupted owned template create may leave its child unmounted. Recovery\nremounts it under the exclusive image lease and pool lock before ordinary native\nvalidation and build continuation. Startup first sweeps nondeleted template\nincarnations whose images are no longer configured, re-reading each unchanged\nrecord under those locks. It mounts an owned interrupted child and restores its\nprivate root when needed before ordinary ownership-checked retirement; an\nalready-private sealed root needs no chmod. Configured templates\nand independent VM disks are unaffected; one unconfirmed retirement does not\nprevent attempts on the others. Unconfirmed ownership still cannot grant\ncapacity or forced deletion."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4068
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An interrupted run is reconciled by the cleanup unit (boot and every five\nminutes): a run that did not complete is recorded `failed(interrupted)` with\nits cleanup retried, and its already-uploaded component snapshots remain as\nunreferenced orphans retained for a one-day grace before retention may forget\nthem. If the run was stopped between manifest upload and completion, the\npublished host-manifest point stays listable, inspectable, restorable and\nretention-counted; the local journal still records the run as\n`failed(interrupted)`. An uncatchably killed writer leaves its Restic\nrepository lock behind: exclusive retention and integrity checks refuse closed\n(no deletion) until\nan operator removes the stale lock with `restic unlock`. Recovery never mutates\nrepository contents or a pool."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4072
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An omitted option keeps the current size; a request with no size option is\nrefused. A running machine stops, applies the sizes and restarts; a stopped\nmachine stays stopped and grows its filesystem on the next boot. The receipt\nfollows the request's phases. `request cancel grow-1` is accepted only while the\nmachine is still stopping: the original sizes and holds are kept, and a running\nmachine restarts unchanged. `request retry grow-1` resumes a request that needs\nattention from its recorded phase.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4076
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Any other delivery withdraws the marker, replaces the roots and runs\n`update-ca-certificates --fresh`, which rebuilds the bundle, the hash links and\nthe hooks. The marker is written only after that rebuild verifies. Trust still\ncompletes before guest networking, DNS, roster sync and sshd on every boot\n(ADR-0113)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4080
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Append-refusal diagnostics now use the reviewed `brady.cache_write_refused`\ncatalog event: a finite cause and bounded freshness durations, with no paths,\npayloads or raw errors. This adds diagnosis without changing capacity or privacy\nauthority. Acceptance GETs retry transient failures at most three times; TLS\ncertificate refusal remains immediate, all attempts are retained and trust\nvalidation is unchanged. These retries do not establish backend availability."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4084
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Application diagnostics use the independent observability path described in\n[observability](#monitoring), under\n[ADR-0149](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0149-independent-observability.md).\nThe earlier fleet envelope corpus was baseline evidence for the retired routes;\nit was retained as\n`marshall/test/marshall_web/fleet_version_history_test.exs` at overalls revision `a99f74f0` (repository deleted).\nIt does not verify the version-4 rollout."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4088
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Application logs pass reviewed event catalogs. Origin, unit and source routing\nderive from trusted journal fields. Nonzero lowercase exact-width `trace_id` and\n`span_id` identifiers support log-to-Tempo and Tempo-to-log navigation. Catalog\nmetadata excludes credentials, terminal contents, raw arguments and payloads.\nCorrelation does not add authorization or control authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4092
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Application release source now includes `protocol/priv` alongside Protocol's\nlibrary and Mix files so its compile-time exact native registry input enters\nthe release closure. A fresh application release build remains pending; source\ninclusion alone grants no native capability or runtime readiness."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4096
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Application trace intake authenticates the producer account and exact systemd\ncgroup before replacing service, host and application-origin attributes. The\nindependent spool durably accepts validated bounded spans before acknowledgment,\nretains unacknowledged delivery and reports saturation, storage failures and\npoisoned state numerically. A full or unavailable spool refuses diagnostics without\nchanging the application outcome. Collector application and guest trace delivery\nuse separate 64-entry persistent exporter queues, with `fsync` enabled for every\nstorage write, unlimited elapsed retry and no asynchronous batch ahead of queue\nacknowledgment. Saturation remains an explicit refusal; unlimited retry does not\nenlarge the queue. These process/restart guarantees do not establish physical\nhost power-loss durability.\nTrace storage and delivery remain bounded; traces are sampled diagnostics.\nEach producer defaults to a two-GiB logical archive and 256-MiB pending admission\nbudget with ninety-day retention, including batches acknowledged upstream. The\naggregate archive allocation must fit the configured 32-GiB host ceiling. These\nlogical budgets require additional disk headroom for SQLite/index overhead and do\nnot reserve physical storage or guarantee ninety days at an unmeasured input rate."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4104
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Approve a new key through Porsche's interactive browser flow while keeping that\nSSH connection open. Closing it invalidates the approval link. A one-shot command\nmust be retried interactively; browser identity alone does not prove key custody.\nApproval and manual key addition hold current account admission through the outer\ncommit. If account retirement wins, the registration is refused without consuming\napproval or adding a key. A fresh identity explicitly registers a released key\nafter old-account cleanup; old sessions retain their original registration ID."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4108
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Arch Linux and AlmaLinux remain Linux guests for authorization and isolation:\ntheir catalog marker changes image identity, not the kernel guest agent, trust,\nnetwork guard, storage ownership or recovery boundary. The builder evaluation\ndoes not establish runtime isolation or distribution-native security behavior."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4112
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Arch/Alma's `overalls-pam-helpers.service` is a root oneshot inside each guest,\nnot a fleet service. It creates the fixed pinned PAM account-helper copy on\nvolatile runtime storage before the existing owned SSH listener, which requires\nits success. Unsafe path custody or installer failure withholds SSH startup;\naccount expiry, current roster and private login receipt remain independent\nrefusal boundaries. No host, listener, domain or placement is added. The\nisolated VM helper check establishes root account behavior on nosuid storage;\nfresh guest SSH/sudo and fleet lifecycle remain separate."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4116
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Architecture impact is verification evidence under ADR-0135 only. Accepted\nrationale, decision status, production behavior and authority are unchanged.\nLocal properties do not establish native custody, interception, TLS, ZFS failure,\nFirecracker attribution or hosted faults. Mid-sync/rename interruption, client\ndisconnect, eventual custody recovery and native storage failures remain open.\nPinned all-file static checks and evaluated Nix HLDD passed; evidence\nsummary corrections were followed by another passing all-file check. Existing native/live acceptance\nrecords retain their original revisions and scopes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4120
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Archived threads retain their objective and current transcript while their machine\nis gone; these reads recheck current creator/team/grant visibility and the bound\nagent identities, and prompt or\nterminal mutations remain unavailable. Current thread managers can reopen\nan archived thread. Reopen provisions a fresh machine and agent binding while\nPaperTrail retains the retired identities. The workspace currently reads only\nthe current transcript binding by default. Authorized readers can select a\nretained generation from the detail URL and read its transcript through the\ngeneration's immutable machine/root/agent binding. Retired generations remain\nread-only and do not expose prompt, terminal or editor controls. Native\narchive/reopen continuity and cross-node recovery remain unverified."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4124
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Arrow keys move the selection, Enter activates it, Tab completes it and Escape\ndismisses the palette and restores focus. Touch interaction and IME composition\nremain supported. Unknown commands preserve the draft and display a refusal;\na leading space submits slash-looking text literally. New-thread mode selection\ndoes not create the machine. Plan/Work and reasoning are separate controls, and\nchanging collaboration mode preserves reasoning."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4128
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Arrows identify authority inputs and coordination paths; they are not a complete\nfunction call graph. The policy/coordinator box is not an Ash domain. Marshall\ndomains share PostgreSQL and may compose actions in one transaction. For example,\n[team mutations](repo:marshall/lib/marshall/teams.ex) use\n[Compute.Ledger](repo:marshall/lib/marshall/compute/ledger.ex).\n[Authorization](repo:marshall/lib/marshall/authorization/cedar.ex) checks current facts;\nprocess identity or a domain name alone grants no permission."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4132
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Arrows mean application ownership, not calls or deployment units. Resources below are literal declarations, deduplicated; extension-generated versions are excluded."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4136
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Arrows mean configured service placement. Configuration: `dungarees`. Marshall instances: none. Fleet address: `10.90.0.2`. Fleet peers: `overalls`. Administrative SSH ports: 2222."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4140
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "At least two independent authoritative nameservers."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4141
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "At the Porsche prompt, enter:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4142
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Atomically published PEM key and full certificate chain, readable by the haproxy group."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4146
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Audi DNS publishes current placement routes. Public gateways acquire leases and\nverify local Lilly execution before forwarding. Stable names do not permit the\nretired source to serve after relocation. Browser authentication, WebSocket\nforwarding, SSH, and private services retain separate authorization checks.\nGenerated local snapshot histories now compare accepted route and proof\nwithdrawals, stale and conflicting revisions, expired publication attempts,\nindependently expired routes and invalid snapshots with exact real UDP and TCP\nA/TXT payloads and authority flags from one Audi replica. They check local publication authority; live\nreplica expiry, cross-host refresh and deployed delegation remain separate gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4150
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Audi handles the guest SSH connection. It resolves the current placement, checks\nCedar and the registered key, and connects under a fresh execution binding. The\nUnix login is the account's guest name, not a shared root account. Old disks can\nlack the required reconciler or listener; inspect image provenance before treating\nthat failure as a key-registration problem."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4154
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Audi private verifies TLS service identity and Lilly's current local VM binding\nbefore forwarding guest requests. When fleet OpenTelemetry is enabled, it counts\ncompleted bound requests to Ziggy, Galileo and private SSH as a candidate\ntransport SLI. An upstream response below 500 is a completed transport; a 5xx\nresponse or stream loss is a failure. Pre-binding denials and guest OTLP uploads\nstay outside this denominator. A private numeric snapshot feeds a Rust exporter\nthrough an Audi-private-only collector socket. It carries no account, VM,\nservice path or payload labels. Collection never grants or extends guest\nauthority, and process restart can lose counts before export."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4158
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Audi rejects invalid gateway, DNS and private-service startup configuration\nbefore its named supervisor or reviewed listener startup entry points are\ncalled. Generated local OTP histories cover 126 refusals across 42 role/case\npairs, with a catalogued rejection, unchanged fixture hashes/modes/link counts\nand no credential, private-key or fixture-path diagnostics. Unset configuration\nstarts only the no-listener supervisor/proof registry. The focused suite passed\ntwo checks, including one property. Packaged startup, successful configured\nserving, file-replacement races, native networking and hosted faults remain open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4162
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Audi's certificate principal contains the SHA256 digest of its current published\nkey. The proxy derives that alias from the exact route's HTTPS lookup and carries\nknown-host revocations into its isolated SSH process. System public trust may use\nconfiguration symlinks; managed user trust and private key reads reject symlinks.\nAll these reads are bounded and require regular files. Guest certificates contain\nonly the authoritative VM hostname. Host certificates never grant user access."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4170
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Audi's hot read paths take no locks (ADR-0140):\n- **TLS selection.** The TLS store is the single writer of the validated fleet\n  wildcard and publishes each accepted generation to a read view. Every\n  handshake's SNI selection reads that view and never waits behind the store.\n- **DNS answers.** The DNS directory publishes each accepted complete snapshot\n  the same way, so queries never wait behind a publish. Every entry carries its\n  own expiry deadline; a snapshot with any undated entry is refused whole.\n- **Failing closed.** A restarted store or directory publishes nothing until it\n  is refreshed. Handshakes are then unrecognized, and queries answer SERVFAIL.\n- **Readiness.** The fleet worker's verified local handshake proves each\n  installed generation once. Per-VM route readiness reuses that proof instead\n  of repeating a handshake per VM per second, and still reports each route to\n  Marshall."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4174
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Authenticate the installed public host key from the receipt. Publish it in the\nhost inventory. Prepare encrypted Git custody, publish the enrolled configuration,\nthen activate the exact commit:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4178
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Authenticated SSH account discovery can create this durable allocation before\nthe user owns a VM. It returns the stored name and repeats do not create another\nidentity. Installer configuration and browser personal terminals share that\nidentity. The prior email-derived fresh-NixOS journey passed SSH/browser identity,\nshared-home preservation and managed Lyra SSH; it remains historical evidence in\nthe [fresh identity review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fresh-guest-identity-verification.md).\nOn base `63a1443c` plus the durable feature, before stopped-only relocation\nintegration, the complete NixOS SSH journey and the completed Ubuntu email-change\nsubtest preserve canonical login/home, numeric ownership, running boot and client\nconfiguration. Current database/property and migration checks also passed.\nThe complete NixOS and Ubuntu generated-identity retirement journeys passed old-home\nreservation, fresh same-email isolation, physical cleanup and explicit fresh\nsharing. Current merged component/native validation, complete Ubuntu SSH and\nretained-disk/restore acceptance remain\nseparate in the\n[durable identity review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-durable-guest-identities.md).\nThe\n[account lifecycle review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-account-lifecycle-verification.md)\nseparates generated identity histories from native cleanup execution and the\nremaining transfer/retirement race and external delivery boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4182
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Authenticated users can open `/threads`, create work at `/threads/new`, and\nreturn to `/threads/:id` from any device. The new-thread page centers an objective\ncomposer with a mode selector and a short mode explanation. Machine settings sit\ninside a closed disclosure, summarize the selected machine size and use the\nconfigured defaults unless changed. The thread index lists titles, status, mode,\nupdated date and an objective preview. Search matches titles and objectives\nwithout case sensitivity, and a status selector shows all, active or archived\nthreads. These filters apply to the current authorized keyset page of 50\nthreads; First page and Next page controls walk older authorized results, and\nactive includes every state except archived. A detail page keeps recent\nthreads in a secondary rail on wide screens; narrow screens return to the list\nthrough the Threads tab."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4186
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Authoritative Audi DNS replicas checked before challenge acknowledgement."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4190
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Automatic compaction evaluates the complete projected request before inference\nand between tool iterations. It begins at 90% of a configured model input\nallowance or 75% of the byte/item limits. The known-limit estimate rounds encoded\nrequest bytes divided by four upward; it is not a provider tokenizer count.\nUnknown token limits remain visibly\nunknown and use the byte/item limits. `/compact` requests compaction explicitly.\nHistorical context can be folded through bounded batches; current required\ninstructions and input that cannot fit return an explicit size refusal.\nCompaction consumes ordinary billed model usage. Current context estimates and\ncumulative usage describe different quantities."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4194
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Automation"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4199
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Backend HTTPS port."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4200
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Backend IPv4 address or hostname."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4201
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Backup subprocess retirement now keeps direct-leader identity unreaped until\nits same-group readers and threads have stopped. Unavailable proc inspection\nwithholds cleanup; a zombie leader alone does not prove thread death.\nThe [reader-group review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-backup-reader-group-retirement.md)\nrecords regression witnesses, pinned runtime8s and packaged cleanup121s passes. Command timeout does not\nbound uninterruptible kernel shutdown; the inherited strict elapsed-time\nrequirement remains unverified for that boundary. Escaped reader groups and durable\ndeferred cleanup need separate containment and recovery evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4205
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Because the bundle declares `guest_agents = none`, the\n[driver](repo:lilly/lib/lilly/vm/driver.ex) records trust as `skipped` for the\nexact boot instead of delivering it, the executor commits the terminal\n`unattested` provisioning phase and reports the VM running with no `guest_ready`\nfact, and readiness, terminals, workspace sources and the Inception profile are\nrefused. Restart and adoption decide from the same durable bundle."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4209
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Because the console is quiet, routine `Starting`/`Started` lines no longer\nappear in `boot.log`. Unit failures still print, and the boot report timeline\ncovers ordering. Existing writable disks keep their old image layout; the first\nboot after an image change takes the full trust path."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4213
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Before a schema or protocol rollout, verify compatibility with every serving\nreplica and retained host journal. Never downgrade by deleting journals or undoing\na migration whose rows establish ownership. See [deployment](#deployment) and\n[recovery](#recovery)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4217
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Before the machine is running, the workspace waits without querying guest\nsessions. Failed boots remain visible; stopped machines require Start. Temporary\nterminal-service failures show preparation during initial opening or reconnection\nfor an existing workspace. Definitive opening failures remain visible until a\nretry or a new execution. An unsuccessful listing never proves a shell exited.\nAutomatic opening runs in a supervised task, so the workspace never blocks on\nguest shell creation. A guest-account refusal is usually roster lag after boot\nor a grant change. It shows \"Preparing your guest account…\" and retries up to\nfive times per execution before it becomes a definitive failure."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4221
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Before the reader starts, a read-only preflight checks each existing shard\ncursor: it must be a private, singly linked regular file that passes SQLite\n`PRAGMA quick_check`. A missing shard cursor starts fresh. No other checkpoint\nformat is read or converted (ADR-0159). Unsafe or corrupt cursors refuse startup\nwith `logging.cursor_check_refused`; operators must inspect custody rather than\ndeleting state to clear the refusal."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4225
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Both clients verify `/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt`. Their client approval\nprompts and command sandboxes are intentionally disabled by the managed defaults;\nguest OS/VM/network/Marshall boundaries remain in force. NixOS exports native CA\nvariables globally; Ubuntu supplies them through profile/Bash startup and PAM's\n`/etc/environment` for browser terminal and SSH accounts. Homes and saved model\nchoices are not seeded or rewritten. Users keep ordinary guest permissions and\nroot capability; native configuration defaults are not a new enforcement layer."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4229
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Both guest builders use an uncompressed kernel with debug sections removed.\nThe build verifies its entry point, load addresses, permissions and loaded bytes\nagainst the original kernel. Debug symbols are retained in a separate output.\nThe manifest hashes the resulting smaller artifact; existing disks retain their\nportable boot bundle. This changes image identity without removing guest tools\nor kernel features. Real-kernel load-image comparison has passed; native boot\nacceptance for this change is still pending."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4233
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Both hosts activated the published coding-client images, but the first NixOS\nproduction canary timed out without inference admission and was fully cleaned\nup; Ubuntu creation was not issued. Separate strict public-chain validation and\nisolated client tests expose the legacy leaf's rejected extra SAN. Same-root\npreparation and independent encrypted replacements preserve offline issuer\ncustody and all nonleaf host values; they do not establish commit/push,\nlive replacement or renewed client\nacceptance. TLS verification and native client configuration remain unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4237
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Both hosts converged healthy on the machine-key expansion at\n`d5e03c080204a33a11b8c136e983593630e4fccf` on 2026-10-15. That expansion left the\ncolumn nullable. The dependent contraction backfills any late null keys, enforces\n`NOT NULL`, and requires the explicit machine key in the resource and workers,\nremoving the temporary row-key fallback under\n[ADR-0159](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0159-remove-legacy-compatibility.md).\nProvisioning and archive jobs must carry the matching key; malformed unkeyed jobs\nare cancelled, and authorized public retry queues a current keyed job. Create,\nreplacement retry and reopen always write the required key. Both hosts subsequently\nconverged healthy on contraction revision\n`32624e1bf80df120beb69b923eee4362427aee23`; read-only SQL confirmed the column\nrequires a value and no null keys remain. See the\n[thread review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-15-user-threads.md) for the\nseparate expansion, contraction and database observations. This rollout does not\nestablish native archive/reopen or worker-loss recovery.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4241
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Both hosts later settled healthy at `50021c04`, which contains the editor merge\n`058f13d8`, with zero updater failures. Dungarees was separately observed healthy\nat `058f13d8`; no intermediate Overalls activation of that revision was\nindependently recorded. Exact generation/system tuples are in the review. These\nread-only rollout observations do not establish a production workbench or upgrade\nretained disks. Both fresh native guest-family checks of `058f13d8` failed;\ncomplete current guest/browser acceptance remains required.\nCurrent Overalls closure inspection at `50021c04` found the exact specialized\npackage and matching protocol/source/release tuples in both installed guest\nmanifests, plus the four expected builtin extension manifests and policy defaults.\nPublic readiness returned200 with verified TLS. The four private recurring\nfixture/session files were absent, leaving supervisor/browser execution unproved;\nrunning recorders/exporters do not supply those credentials or healthy journeys."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4245
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Both hosts subsequently activated exact 63a1443c/release 73ad, independently\nobserved healthy at 13:00 UTC on 2026-10-10. Installed product/defaults and both\nnew manifest-v3 guest images match the same protocol/source/release tuple.\nThe review records exact host-system and image artifacts. This activation does\nnot establish a new authenticated production editor journey or upgrade retained\nguest disks. The recurring fixture absence above belongs to the earlier 12:01\ninspection at 50021c04. A separately authorized current existence-only check at\n13:06:33 confirmed all four fixture/session files absent on 63a1443c, with both\nbrowser supervisors restarting and request exporters running. Production\nbrowser and recurring history remain unestablished."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4249
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Both image builders use\n[one pinned package/settings source](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/coding-clis.nix).\nCodex reads `/etc/codex/config.toml`: `model_provider = \"ziggy\"`, provider\n`base_url = \"https://llm.internal/openai/v1\"`, `wire_api = \"responses\"`,\n`requires_openai_auth = false`, `supports_websockets = false`,\n`approval_policy = \"never\"`, `sandbox_mode = \"danger-full-access\"` and\n`check_for_update_on_startup = false`. Model selection remains native client\nbehavior; native user/CLI settings may override Codex system defaults. No per-user\nconfiguration is generated."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4253
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Both native terminal daemons also cross-link with native interpreters and\nverified manifests. The integrated closure remains incomplete: OS-native\nSSH/service execution and the full boot/recovery scenarios\nare missing. The rc.d/SMF supervisor, readiness PID checks and linked binaries\nprovide packaging evidence only; they cannot confer fleet admission.\nThe new nested-KVM `native-freebsd-transport` gate and its separate test-only\nlistener bind credit-window exchanges to the executing token and exact\ndisk/firmware/VMM hashes. A scoped 139-second run passed; subsequent candidate\ninputs require a fresh recorded execution. It does not enable the production\nservices or catalog."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4257
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Both standard images install pinned Codex 0.149.0 (`codex`) and Claude Code\n2.1.238 (`claude`) using their native system configuration. The\n[shared package/settings source](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/coding-clis.nix) selects\nZiggy's verified private endpoint without provider credentials or custom\nlaunchers. Automatic client updates are disabled. No model catalog synchronizer\nis installed; ordinary native model choices/catalogs may differ from Ziggy's\navailable models."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4261
