msgid "Boundary: A pool-locked native allocation audit independently binds durable claim/spec, host/pool/VM nonce, GUID, mounts, closed file set, drive UID/type/length and ready-disk metadata. A safely contained private single-link marker is bounded to 16 KiB; boot artifacts must be nonempty root-owned single-link regular files with mode 0444 and combined marker/artifact sizes within the protocol's 1 GiB reservation. Only then may invalid bundle contents leave that child recognized without allocation credit, without decoding those contents. Measured ZFS free space still includes its bytes and any outstanding startup hold remains unoffset. Current launch/readiness codecs, authenticated capacity reports, startup settlement, cleanup authority and ADR-0159's no-legacy policy remain unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4309
