msgid "Boundary: ADR-0192. Editor and nested HTTPS take ADR-0187's detached path (record, op 14, keeper, re-adoption, ending through hostd). Lilly derives the stage from the validated binding: a PROXY v2 header naming the Audi-attested client for nested HTTPS, the framed editor binding and the exact framed ready document for the editor. hostd writes the preface to the guest and byte-compares exactly the expected frame's length, reading no guest byte past it, before starting the bridge; it interprets neither string. TLS, HTTP and per-request editor grants stay with the client, the nested guest, Audi and Marshall."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4333
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Actual managed SSH observes the root-owned flush marker, executable mode/hash and live PID. Within one boot the oracle kills/reaps that process while executable permission prevents restart, then restores exact mode and requires a different supervised PID with the same bytes and boot identity."
