#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4341
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Arch Linux and AlmaLinux use the version-4 kernel image shape with distinct pinned distribution roots and identities. Owned key-only SSH policy, pinned PAM modules and a requisite private login receipt preserve the existing Audi authority. Collision-checked locked sshd/overalls-ssh identities, files-only account lookup and pinned account command paths preserve roster custody. Root-owned regular setuid sudo uses only reconciler-managed per-user grants; vendor sshd enablement resolves to the readiness-gated listener. The root-only argument-free helper oneshot installs exact pinned immutable unix_chkpwd bytes at its compiled path before SSH, requiring regular root-owned source/destination and safe root-owned parents. Existing nosuid mounts remain; the pinned root PAM caller sets real UID 0 before helper execution. Marshall authorization, current-boot readiness, host isolation and native storage remain independent existing boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4345
