msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4617
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Marshall checks current Cedar VM read, unique current placement and fresh authenticated protocol-2 host stream independently of guest terminal capability. Lilly checks its assigned stream caller and newest runnable command, then binds a private single-link host log inode to unchanged boot, intent and launch-attempt evidence. Only a bounded page and cursor leave the host; no guest manager, dial, boot challenge, path or input authority is returned."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4621
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Marshall counts endpoint responses only after the privacy, health and public machine-API prefilters; a mode-0640 cumulative snapshot in a dynamic-user-owned, mode-0750 directory feeds a static Rust exporter using the Marshall-only collector socket with a Nix-configured replica identity."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4625
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Marshall owns executor fences and transitions; the guest uses only verified private HTTPS. Native exec_command forwards the existing lease/stop callback before spawn and during authority polling. A separate scoped collector owns the child, concurrently bounds both output streams and enforces the 20-second deadline independently of a blocking lease RPC."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4629
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Marshall serves /bin/install.ps1 templated with the deployment's SSH host trust (503 without it) and the windows-amd64 artifact with its SHA-256 digest from the same manifest as the Unix targets. The installer validates origin, zone and host against the issued values, requires an OpenSSH client with hostname protection (9.6+), installs Microsoft.OpenSSH.Preview with winget without asking when %ProgramFiles%\\OpenSSH lacks one, and with one administrator approval places %ProgramFiles%\\OpenSSH before the in-box 9.5 directory in the machine PATH (resolved in the elevated process; declined elevation leaves the machine PATH unchanged and points to overalls ssh) so the machine page shows one ssh HOST command, verifies the digest, runs config-ssh --staged-installer with the downloaded binary before installing it, and connects with overalls ssh through the recorded client. The managed SSH block quotes ProxyCommand as one double-quoted absolute path because Win32-OpenSSH runs it without a shell. Updates use the same digest manifest and activate by renaming the running executable aside."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4633
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Marshall.Threads owns the durable objective, mode, team visibility and thread-to-machine binding. Compute owns VM admission/lifecycle and Agents owns turns, model calls and tools. PostgreSQL transactions, row locks, generation keys and Oban jobs coordinate durable thread changes. The authenticated LiveView is a client of these domains."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4637
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: MarshallWeb.SecurityHeaders sets one Content-Security-Policy (script-src 'self' alone; style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' for the vendored xterm.js and Mermaid renderers), Permissions-Policy, same-origin opener and resource policies, nosniff, SAMEORIGIN framing and no cross-domain policies before health, static files, the early /api refusals and the router. MarshallWeb.NoIndex adds X-Robots-Tag on the same surfaces and the root layout repeats it as a robots meta tag beside the disallow-all robots.txt. Production sends HSTS max-age=63072000 with includeSubDomains and no preload. The production session cookie is __Host-marshall (Secure, HttpOnly, Path=/, no Domain, SameSite=Lax, signed and encrypted) and the remembered credential is __Host-remember_me; MarshallWeb.BrowserSession owns the options for Plug.Session, the LiveView socket and every forged-session test or release probe, and expires legacy cookie names carried by a request. Headers and cookies grant nothing: stored-login checks, Cedar and CSRF tokens decide access, and user applications on *.apps.ghuntley.dev remain same-site with Marshall."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4641
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Native helpers retain completion custody (the source-export lock; the transfer-stream hostd lease) across descendant process groups/sessions; direct leader exit does not prove cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4645
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Native state journals, ownership fences and physical readiness receipts remain authoritative; observer ACKs cannot gate v2 actor progress."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4649
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Native user-run client configuration and guest-local state remain separate from Marshall's platform agent loop; Lilly derives the VM binding and Marshall grants current inference authority. Codex starts with no approvals and danger-full-access; Claude starts with bypassPermissions and no Bash sandbox. Guest OS, VM, network and Marshall boundaries remain independent. Ubuntu retains the pinned offline application closure through its registered GC root."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4653
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Nix configuration trusts only the pinned Overalls Cachix signing key for the additional read substituter. The NixOS host catalog, NixOS guests, kexec installer and Ubuntu nix-daemon share the declaration; fleet publication uses a separately scoped SOPS token under ADR-0189, and guests receive no publication credentials."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4657
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Nix provisions Grafana on Overalls loopback for operators. Application candidates repeat source lifetime and sampling-clock guards; ingress additionally requires fresh direct localhost source health. Guest claims cannot enter those series."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4661
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Nix provisions stable dashboards and datasources; Grafana authenticates the operator while its server-side datasource holds only reader-scoped log-store authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4665
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Nix-owned measurement rosters and numeric diagnostic states; operator Grafana and signed-in Marshall reads; independent read-only loopback storage probe and one 15-bound Underclass duration histogram."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4669
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Official-source Nix package and broker bind exact boot address/gateway, execution/release/account preface and reconciled UID. Systemd worker/socket ownership is independent of the root broker."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4673
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Official-source patch routes Open VSX gallery, dependencies and WEB-targeted installs through the native signature verifier before extraction; package identity includes the reviewed key ring."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4681
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Only the current connection owns a heartbeat schedule; retired timer messages cannot service its replacement."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4685
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Operator-owned private configuration is validated before Lilly creates runtime authority or status listeners."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4689
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Overalls supervisors use private real operator session/guest fixtures and own browser deadlines; distinct durable recorders, numeric readers/exporters and collector sockets preserve outcome authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4693
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: OverallsProtocol.GuestAgents names the closed agent set (linux, none, windows-v1) and a pure capability table; Lilly's jail, driver and executor and Marshall's per-capability image facts branch on the table, never on the set's name, so the agentless none row reproduces ADR-0170 exactly. The firmware jail gets the jail-local vsock endpoint only for an agent set that speaks the Lilly protocols. The readiness budget is the agent set's (600 s for windows-v1) and is recorded once per boot. The image ships the virtio-win viosock driver and, until the real agents exist, a SYSTEM probe that discovers the provider's address family at runtime, listens on vsock port 1099 and answers the host's CONNECT with one JSON line, publishing only its own log on the EFI system partition. Windows binaries are cross-built from the shared Lyra crate with the pinned zig toolchain; the Lyra gate type-checks the library and the Windows bins for x86_64-pc-windows-gnu. Images are configured as { path } objects; a size check decides template cacheability and every root disk is copied on demand (ADR-0177); both hosts' template budget is 96 GiB."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4697
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Owner-only access, no sharing or web exposure, and denied outbound/lateral traffic."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4701
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Peer activity renews a fifteen-second silence budget; outgoing ping cadence must not postpone retirement beyond that budget."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4705
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Per-producer Unix UID/cgroup identity and private SQLite FULL-WAL archive determine diagnostic custody; the observer holds no application or guest authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4709
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Persisted Cedar role governs each action and live capability renewal."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4713
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Persisted Plan/Work collaboration is trusted application state separate from reasoning. Root Plan turns own durable questions and the first current authorized answer. A completed proposal binds one Work turn on the same thread and machine. Plan is instructional and does not create a read-only filesystem boundary."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4717
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Personal account allocation, boot-bound opening receipt, current creator/read-only attachment authority and PTY ownership."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4721
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Pinned transfer, probe-gated source stop and quiescence, one full stream of the stopped disk, atomic placement handoff and destination readiness before source cleanup (ADR-0155)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4725
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Porsche counts terminal SSH command dispatch results in fixed cumulative outcomes and duration; a private numeric file feeds a Rust exporter through a Porsche-only collector intake with Nix-owned service identity."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4729
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Post-backup revocations, epochs, generations and physical survivors must be reconciled."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4733
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Presentation changes never alter authorization, terminal transport, element identifiers or hook names; every stylesheet, script and font is served from the application origin."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4737
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Private file ownership, global recovery membership, selected host recipients, retained rekey identity, per-document publication, staged compatibility and old-key retention."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4741
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Private stable intent lock, exact current-generation payload and trusted absolute exec target; shared custody must precede intent validation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4745
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Production Lilly Driver and independent systemd VM tree, durable launch authority and authenticated Marshall physical outcome settlement in a disposable fleet."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4749
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Public CSRF capture grants no authority and stores only canonical source2, visit and expiry in the signed cookie. A current ordinary stored login or registered-key Porsche identity admits through Compute and a matching manifest4 source capability; ordinary browser provisioning requires no passkey. The postcommit receipt rechecks login and VM ownership before matched clear. Lilly carries inert source2 bound to current placement, epoch and boot; only the guest contacts providers and runs git. Existing immutable snapshots/receiver records are never rewritten during cutover. Every validated new provision/start snapshot derives source from the durable VM, including supplied resize snapshots. Recovery preflights durable image eligibility without discarding valid crash/resize proof or fresh host reports."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4753
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Public and signed-in navigation and Overview link to the canonical public /docs/browser-extension guide. Guidance grants no identity or compute authority. Marshall serves a closed artifact allowlist from a canonical immutable Nix-store package over its existing public HTTPS boundary without login state; operators may disable downloads while the guide remains public. Strict native modules transmit only provider origin/path after removing source queries/fragments, only after an explicit provider toolbar click to an explicitly configured origin. The configured extension requests optional access only for that exact Overalls origin and marks the open page with a local installed signal; Marshall uses that signal only to hide setup affordances. Public package possession and the marker grant no compute authority; the repository-launch scenario owns authenticated capture and admission."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4757
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Pure guest-terminal Ring retention allocation; actual PTY growth, viewer queues and authenticated upstream authority remain separate."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4761
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Registered SSH key, current Cedar decision, CA-authenticated gateway and guest, boot-bound roster, permanently reserved username/UID and durable account discovery."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4765
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Required operator fields, IPv4 bind, port, absolute paths, token limits and regular certificate/key references are validated before worker or listener authority starts."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4769
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Reviewed finite producer-health events use trusted journal service/unit, module host identity and the native journal clock; the loopback numeric bridge retains independent application log routing."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4773
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Role-specific operator configuration and private credentials/keys are validated before Audi creates listener authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4777
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Runtime schema and file custody are validated before named supervision and SSH or status listeners."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4781
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Saved self-only locale override takes precedence over validated session/browser negotiation and English fallback. Arabic and Urdu use RTL; locale does not grant authority or change machine output."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4785
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Schema is validated before named supervision; private matching CA signer material is validated by the first supervised child before cache and transparent listeners."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4789
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Shared account admission through the outer manual/approval transaction, exclusive retirement and completed old-UUID credential cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4793
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Shared client owns volatile request correlation and at most eight pending callers; disconnect is unproven domain completion and cannot authorize replay."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4797
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Signed-in bounded redacted projections; current elevated administrator, installation/account/raw-job locks and actor/request-bound retry receipt."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4801
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Signed-in read access is separate from administrator membership plus fresh elevation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4805
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Snapshot ownership, audit and current requester authority, serialized publication/cancellation, immutable snapshot, source restoration and independently proven cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4809
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Stored browser login, current direct/team Cedar rights, exact app cookie and execution/policy-bound five-second request-start lease."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4813
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Strict operator configuration, private service/provider credentials, fixed upstream origins and runtime paths are validated before serving or provider worker authority starts."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4817
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Strict operator schema, control origin, private credential and local socket are validated before Galileo creates serving authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4821
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The BEAM holds only sockets it created (ADR-0184). lilly-hostd connects Lilly's own socket to api.sock or v.sock beneath pool roots, or, as a fallback only, bridges it to a namespace connection through lilly-ingress-bridge running as lilly (op 13); every ingress service instead sends Audi's accepted connection to a detached bridge (ADR-0187, ADR-0192). hostd sends no descriptor and Lilly closes each socket after its gen_tcp port is down."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4825
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The SSH channel captures request start before backend authorization; StreamGuard must refuse expired admission before invoking the locally configured guest connector."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4829
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The disposable native guest uses actual packaged Lilly router and TAP source-guard rules under validated synthetic identity. Every fixed TCP target is proven reachable before rules. Real guard drop counters distinguish source refusal from an unrelated connection failure."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4833
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The encrypted outbox row controls whether a mail attempt may start; each retry carries one stable Message-ID and token payload, while token consumption remains single-use."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4837
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The exact source-built package supplies immutable policy and signed hash-pinned Open VSX builtins; native workers use current personal UID and all-folder trust. Installed extensions/server data belong to guest-account directories, while disablement follows upstream browser-profile storage on the separate account origin without cross-device synchronization. Language tools come from project environments and direnv requires separate explicit approval."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4841
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The first supervised listener validates certificate signature leaf binding current time and a single principal before the SSH daemon or later serving children."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4845
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The fixture flushes and reads back exact home bytes, requires actual Firecracker SIGKILL, then boots the same disk with fresh MMDS authority. Native filesystem verification and retained bytes are required after recovery; final shutdown must be observed cleanly."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4849
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The host boot-log writer stamps console lines without interpreting payloads under its 1 MiB cap; the guest boot report is observation only. Ubuntu skips update-ca-certificates only when the marker, managed root bytes, bundle PEM blocks and per-root links prove the store already reflects the exact delivered set; every boot still delivers and verifies the current host set before networking (ADR-0113, ADR-0154)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4853
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The image is installed inside a KVM Nix sandbox from Microsoft's hash-pinned evaluation ISO with restricted user networking and pinned virtio-win drivers; Firecracker boots the edk2 CloudHv firmware as a PVH payload over the opt-in virtio-pci transport. The patched VMM keeps its 1.16.1 identity and static linking; its seccomp surface widens by exactly one vCPU-thread ioctl (KVM_IOEVENTFD) for BAR relocation. This scenario covers the operator launcher only (no jailer, no host network guard); the Lilly launch path is the separate windows-lilly-guest-launch scenario."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4857
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The immutable image binds the pinned editor/broker closure and exact descriptor; Marshall retains current write/profile/Customer-owner authority, Audi retains the account origin, Lilly fences TCP 4444 to the current boot, and the guest broker reconciles the current personal UID before launching a systemd worker."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4861
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The native helper owns stable command slots and repository writer locks; inherited descriptors retain uncertain descendant authority. Marshall retains durable intent."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4865
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The opt-in private runner requires explicit distinct catalog IDs for all seven OS keys, with null marking unavailable images. Selected IDs must match exact catalog names and the intended account. New lifecycle mutations and guest probes bind durable create receipts to canonical UUID, current owner, name, image, profile and SSH endpoint. Personal-account probes use the installed Overalls CLI with strict guest trust; this client-side ledger does not replace Marshall authorization, current-boot attestation, Lilly fencing, guest/host isolation or native storage ownership."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4869
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The pinned Rust proxy validates its bearer and parsed model request before durable admission; an independent exporter reads only a restricted numeric snapshot and a separate collector intake assigns fixed source provenance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4873
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The pinned Underclass proxy refuses with 429 and a relative Retry-After only when a fresh selection after the automatic reset attempt still finds no healthy eligible account; requests skip the reset lock while any Codex account is healthy."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4877
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The pinned Underclass proxy stores sanitized stream outcomes and aggregate statistics in its host-local database; the stats API, event import route and CLI require the host administrator bearer token."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4881
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The protocol admits exactly the eight-key version-5 manifest and the seven-key version-2 firmware bundle beside the unchanged version-4 and version-1 shapes; artifact names come from the protocol only. Lilly keeps rootfs.ext4 as the pool-side root slot, bind-mounts the firmware read-only, seeds the boot identity (placement, execution epoch, boot challenge, /32, gateway, MAC; never the generation) into Firecracker's MMDS from a root-owned jail-local metadata.json before launch, boots /firmware with the Hyper-V CPU template and --enable-pci, and runs the guest under the jailer, seccomp observation and the per-tap guard. The guest's SYSTEM bootstrap task reads MMDS with a V2 session token, validates every field including the adapter MAC and applies exactly the delivered /32. Marshall projects per-capability guest facts (guest_capabilities) from the immutable image, all false for the agentless set."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4885
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The reset route, page button and underclass reset command require the host's admin bearer token; a remote --url call must carry UNDERCLASS_UI_TOKEN and never sends a database token."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4889
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The shared client owns socket retirement; public satellite adapters must preserve its stopped unsupported-version reason when pending calls resolve as unproven."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4893
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The shared client owns volatile pending requests under the current welcome's validated capacity; service admission and domain authority remain separate."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4897
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The shared client owns volatile reconnect scheduling; durable host freshness and domain authority remain independent."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4901
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The v6 image and v3 workload bundle carry immutable kernel provenance. Lilly uses the caller-owned jail-local /v.sock and a fixed probe port to compare the native OS, placement, execution epoch, boot challenge and kernel digest, requiring a canonical boot ID before credentials or readiness. Readiness must return the same boot ID. Native source receipts and placeholder kernels remain outside fleet admission; unqualified native capabilities remain false. Separate complete exact-image qualification enables only the reviewed sealed FreeBSD and exact OmniOS native subsets; changed or unreviewed candidates remain closed."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4905
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: The zone is a nullable display preference on the user's own row, written only through the self-only set_time_zone action and validated against the compiled tz database; storage, ledger time, CSV export and SSH wire views stay UTC. The viewer zone resolves saved, then validated browser connect param, then UTC; other people's local time renders only from a saved zone."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4909
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Threads owns canonical viewer/operator/manager grants and immutable sharing results. Current thread grants contribute to the current matching-owner VM binding through existing Cedar authority; no VM grant is copied. Independent VM/team grants remain additive. Terminal, editor, SSH and personal guest-account authorities remain separate."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4913
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Trusted absolute utility argv, private export lock and all-adopted-child kernel custody; source permit and SSH authority remain separate."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4917
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Unsupported-version close is a terminal transport refusal, and disconnect cannot prove domain completion."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4921
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Verified HTTPS policy and one dedicated host CA; issuance requires locked service or physical boot authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4925
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Verified TLS control upgrade, correlated error and pending-close classes plus local DNS, SSH publisher, Fleet and readiness ownership; Marshall remains publication authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4929
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Verified email identity, current elevated administrator, immediate account revocation and old-UUID cleanup through physical lifecycle fences."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4933
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Verified origin and current profile admission precede shared-cache policy; explicit-public or reviewed anonymous full-commit GitHub classification, complete payloads, exact variants, freshness and process-owned leases govern reuse."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4937
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Version-6 manifests and version-3 bundles explicitly bind FreeBSD or illumos (the OmniOS wire family) to its matching agent set, firmware boot kind, raw-GPT root and bounded artifacts. Unqualified native capability rows remain all-false. Complete exact identity qualification enables readiness, trust, terminal, workspace, flush, SSH and agents only for the sealed reviewed FreeBSD image. OmniOS and changed candidates remain refused; editor and Inception remain disabled. Lilly keeps the Windows Hyper-V CPU template off native guests."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4941
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Versioned authenticated control transport, durable generation, owned physical process and GUID-bound drives."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4945
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Volatile proof binds the exact currently verified VMM; one native observer may outlive proof withdrawal to report its actual terminal outcome, without granting authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4949
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Write permission, profile tool allowlist, model claim and boot-bound executor fence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4953
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Ziggy counts a newly durable terminal spool completion, excludes caller cancellation and exports only fixed cumulative numbers through a private file, Rust exporter and Ziggy-only collector intake."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4957
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Ziggy's closed native route type validates the exact beta query separately from the query-free accounting path, forwards native bytes and allowed Anthropic headers, and retains current admission and provider-secret custody."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4961
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: lilly-hostd holds each lease's flock on the existing lock inode, grants waiters in arrival order and runs leased utilities from a closed table with the lease descriptor inherited, each in its own command cgroup in production."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4965
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Brady attribution, Audi ingress and private-service lookups read that view\nwithout calling the runtime or the actor. A request therefore needs a connected\nruntime, a live command identical to the durable command, and an unexpired\nobservation:\n- A superseding command, a disconnected runtime or the actor's exit revokes at\n  once.\n- A slow or retried observation does not, and neither does placement-lock\n  contention while gathering boot proof: the proof lapses only when its\n  deadline passes. Definite negative evidence does revoke.\n- A Lilly restart starts with no rows, so authority waits for the next running\n  observation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4969
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Brady intercepts guest TCP 80/443 with nftables tproxy inside Lilly's router\nnamespace: a mark selects a local-delivery table so Brady's transparent sockets\nreceive the connection. The namespace keeps strict reverse-path filtering and\npins `src_valid_mark=0` itself. A host value of 1 (Tailscale exit nodes set it)\nwould make the reverse-path check follow the tproxy mark into that local table\nand silently drop every intercepted SYN, leaving OSS guests without web egress.\nThe Brady fleet journey runs with the host setting enabled to cover this.\nFor HTTPS, Brady pins the original IP and verifies the upstream certificate for\nthe handshake SNI there; it does not require its own DNS answer for that name to\nequal the guest's, because rotating names such as github.com resolve differently\nthrough different public resolvers. Plain HTTP `Host` and operator TLS-exception\ntunnels, which Brady cannot verify, still must resolve to the original address."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4973
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Brady intercepts permitted guest web TCP before NAT. It verifies the HTTP authority\nor TLS name and connects to the pinned original destination with independent\nupstream TLS verification. Guest identity comes from kernel connection attribution\nand a current execution proof, not guest headers."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4977
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Brady validates operator schema before supervision, emitting the catalogued\nconfiguration rejection for invalid input. Signer material is validated later\nby the first supervised child; invalid private certificate/key files stop that\nchild before cache or listener startup. Generated local properties pass 120\nschema refusals across 40 cases and 51 signer-child refusals across 17 cases.\nTwenty immutable-store issuer-key paths receive loader-only checks, with no\noutside-fixture signer startup. Recursive fixture bytes, modes, ownership,\ntypes and link counts remain unchanged, and diagnostics exclude original and\nmutated signer material and fixture paths. Unset starts only Metrics, with fleet\nmonitor exports disabled in the disposable process. These are test-build checks;\npackaged invalid startup, configured serving, native interception/trust/isolation,\nconcurrent file replacement and hosted config faults remain open for this property."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4981
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Browser extension"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4982
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Browser extension presence detection is outside Ash domain ownership. The browser\nrequests optional exact-origin access and emits a local document marker; Marshall\nonly uses that marker for setup presentation. It creates no resource, listener,\nidentity, machine grant or durable authority, so no new domain or resource enters\nthe ownership inventory."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4986
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Browser login uses the persisted account and login token. Ordinary signed-in\nworkspace and Control room reads do not require a passkey; passkey verification\nstarts at the privileged mutation or passkey-change boundary. LiveViews\nrecheck the stored login before mount and on navigation, events, and refresh;\nkeeping a page open does not preserve revoked authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4990
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Build hosts need the repository's pinned toolchain and, for native image creation,\nworking KVM. Inspect the resulting `manifest.json`; use its canonical image\nidentity rather than inventing an ID from a filename. Fleet image declarations\nselect installed artifacts and Marshall's default image."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4994
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Build the selected source-built context exports, stage them with\n`antithesis/build/prepare-contexts.sh`, then validate\n`antithesis/config/docker-compose.yaml`. A meaningful local baseline requires\nthe full Compose build and startup: PostgreSQL migration, both verified HTTPS\nMarshall readiness endpoints, actual operator enrollment, authenticated Lilly\nControl and a fresh committed host report, then the workload's single\n`setup_complete`. Preserve named state volumes only when testing retained-state\nrestarts; use a fresh Compose project and volumes for an independent baseline.\n`antithesis/README.md` gives the local commands and the\n[foundation review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-13-antithesis-harness-foundation.md)\ntracks their present execution state. A local base control-core setup completed;\nits selected manifest has four stale runtime-dependency hashes, so it is not a\nfrozen hosted baseline. The earlier clean local Compose diagnostic started PostgreSQL migration, both\nMarshall HTTPS replicas, enrollment and Lilly health. The non-serving operator\ncompleted three synthetic accounts and three passkeys; read-only SQL found\nexactly three of each, and `ss -lnt` found no enrollment listener. The workload\nremained at `host_connection_or_report`: its connected v4 host had\n`report_sequence` 0 and no `reported_at`. A later fresh diagnostic4 project\nreached a connected, fresh v4 report at sequence 44 and logged\n`INFO Antithesis setup complete` at 14:33:49 UTC. Six packaged serial Control\ncommands exited zero and emitted 13 true SDK assertion records; a later SQL\nread found fresh report sequence 392. That sequence counts reports, not commands\nor physical capacity. See the [foundation review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-13-antithesis-harness-foundation.md)\nfor the local result and identity limits."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4998
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Build with `nix build .#marvin`; check with `nix build .#checks.x86_64-linux.marvin`.\nIn devenv, `marvin-build`, `marvin-check` and `marvin-watch` use the same maintained\nnative module/build source and lockfile-pinned tools. Release version comes from\n`marvin/package.json`; archive timestamps default to the fixed ZIP epoch through\n`SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`. No signing credential or provider credential enters the build.\nSee [installation](#interactive) and [verification](#reference)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5002
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Built-in formatting, language diagnostics, search, Git, Markdown preview and PTYs\nrun through the native guest extension host. Open VSX gallery VSIXs are checked\nagainst the packaged Ed25519 keys before extraction, including dependency and\nWEB-targeted installs. User settings cannot disable that gate. An explicitly\nimported local VSIX remains a user trust decision. Webviews use separate hash\norigins and immutable Audi-served bootstrap files, without a CDN fallback."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5006
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "CA bundle authenticating Marshall backend certificates."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5007
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "CA bundle authenticating the PostgreSQL endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5008
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "CA bundle authenticating the control-plane endpoint. Lilly reads it through systemd LoadCredential, so the file may be readable by root only."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5012
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "CA certificates authenticating the Marshall HTTPS endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5013
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "CA roots authenticating the ACME directory."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5014
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "CA roots validating issued certificate chains."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5015
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "CI metadata reads enabled `config.requiredFeatures` from a lazy NixOS tester when\nits wrapper lacks `requiredSystemFeatures`, preserving explicit metadata and\navoiding evaluation of the driver/derivation/image merely to select a builder.\nThe throw-on-forcing regression and actual metadata checks passed. Native\nservice/transport/reset tests remain enabled nested-KVM machine checks; the host\nfixture remains nonmachine. This corrects test scheduling without changing the\nactual nested-KVM requirement or adding runtime acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5019
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Cancellation and publication serialize in PostgreSQL. Cancellation before\npublication retains both transfer revocations, destination discard, snapshot prune\nand source restoration as separate obligations. Unknown physical results retain\nholds. An offered incomplete preparation, capture, copy, adoption or cleanup\neffect may report an unconfirmed progress label and retry with its retained\nidentity and commitments. A successful matching receipt clears that label.\nCancellation can abandon forward copy/adoption, but still requires every cleanup\nreceipt and clears the final diagnostic. A completed capture receipt can coexist\nwith independently pending copy work; uncertainty cannot fabricate the snapshot\nor authorize publication. Once restoration\ncompletes, later clone work cannot overwrite subsequent\nsource start/stop intent. After publication, use ordinary destination lifecycle\ncontrols. The [verification review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-clone-cancellation-verification.md)\nrecords generated actual-action histories, observed three-replica schedules and\nthe exact native execution scope; synthetic receipts are not native disk evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5023
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Cancellation and supersession exclude the original completion intent; their own\ncommands have separate confirmed outcomes. Replays cannot reset source identity,\nrewrite finished measurements or add repeated totals. Exporters drain overdue\npending accounting before publishing fresh clocks. PaperTrail, authenticated\noperation history and public command receipts remain available through Marshall.\nDiagnostic collection does not replace them."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5031
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Candidate activation stages secret bundles privately and binds them to the\ncomplete descriptor by content digest in `/run/overalls-auto-update/handoff.json`.\nThe new generation's preparation services publish exactly the staged bytes\nwithout re-decrypting, so a concurrent document replacement landing between\nstaging and the switch cannot change what consumers receive. Stale handoffs\nfrom earlier attempts are retired at staging entry and on refusal cleanup.\nThe [updater custody histories](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-custody-updater.md)\nexecute this handoff against the real SecretSpec/SOPS pipeline and pin the\ncapped backoff, the verify-only post-rotation recovery and the wedge label."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5035
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Candidates must carry the complete current manifest: diagnostic preflight,\nsocket units and the Lilly transfer state directory. A host's reviewed resource\npolicy may raise CPU, RAM and quota ceilings and may lower the RAM ceiling\nlive only while the guest slice's current use plus two GiB fits under the new\nceiling, read just before the change; otherwise the update is refused\n`resource_decrease_unsafe` and nothing changes (ADR-0164). CPU and quota\ndecreases, and introducing or removing a policy, like any other\ninstallation-binding change, require maintenance. The policy also writes and\nverifies the ZFS ARC dnode limit at a quarter of the ARC maximum beside the\nmaximum itself. No reader tolerates manifests from before these fields existed\n(ADR-0159)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5039
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Canonical mounted pool path."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5040
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Canonical runtime directory containing the complete published bundle."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5044
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Canonical source and fleet deployment continue using `antithesishq/overalls` on\n`main`. Host clone/ancestry checks, enrollment probes and updater defaults agree\non this branch. ADR-0147 accepts the Standard profile for fresh state. The\nretained-state extension,\n[ADR-0151](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0151-existing-state-standard-profile-migration.md),\ncompleted on both hosts and is superseded by ADR-0159: the one-way database\nmigration was applied and its file then pruned, and Lilly no longer renames\nprivate state at startup.\nDo not treat a previous system generation as a database rollback."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5048
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Capacity alerts warn at seventy percent, critically at eighty-five percent, or\nprojected exhaustion within the retention horizon. Low root headroom, missing\ncapacity probes and ingestion refusals have separate alerts. Increasing retention\ncannot restore deleted observations. Resolve volume or allocation pressure without\nsilently shortening the declared horizon; see [operations](#operations)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5052
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Central Grafana loads reader-only log-store credentials through systemd and queries\nthe verified fleet TLS entry. Store insert and reader credentials retain separate\ncustody. Changing the reader credential requires restarting Grafana to reload it;\nnever place secret contents in Nix options, application environments or dashboards.\nSee [monitoring](#monitoring) and the evaluated [option reference](#options)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5056
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Central metrics/traces/Grafana store or worker collector."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5057
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Certificate-specific verification includes\n`nix build .#checks.x86_64-linux.ssh-host-certificates`, the NixOS and Ubuntu\n`user-ssh-journey` fleet checks, protocol certificate properties and Marshall\nissuance tests. The current decision is\n[unified host CA](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0124-unified-ssh-host-ca.md);\n[operations](repo:docs/operations/porsche-operations.md) describes trust and renewal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5061
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Changes to implementation, configuration, protocols, architecture, operations or\nverification must use the repository's `hldd-maintenance` skill. Update affected\nchapters and diagrams in the same change. When no reader-visible fact changes,\nrecord the specific reason. Never mark a review complete by refreshing hashes\nwithout inspecting the source change."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5065
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Check reports drift without modifying documents. Rekey validates every changed\ncandidate before publishing any; preparation refusal preserves all originals.\nPublication is atomic per document. If interrupted, retain the reported completed\nand possibly updated names, resolve the failure and explicitly rerun rekey.\nCompleted documents with current recipients remain byte-identical on retry.\nVerify independent recovery before retiring old custody. Recipient removal\ncannot erase plaintext or application credentials already learned by a recipient."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5069
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Choose a stable, unique request ID for each intended mutation. Reuse it when\nretrying that same mutation after losing a reply. Request IDs contain 1–128 ASCII\nletters, digits, underscores, dots, colons or hyphens, and start with a letter or\ndigit. Do not reuse one ID for different operations."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5073
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Chromium configuration/cache lives in private writable temporary directories.\nThe shared native/recurring helper preserves HOME and inherited data paths,\nincluding the native tester's actual NSS certificate trust. Pinned headless fonts\nestablish reproducible browser startup, not authentication. The separate Nix\npackage startup fixture uses its own temporary trust bypass; its passing installed\nworkbench check does not establish verified native TLS or a Marshall login."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5077
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Claude reads `/etc/claude-code/managed-settings.json`. Its `env` sets\n`ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://llm.internal/anthropic`, nonsecret\n`ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=ziggy`, `DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER=1` and\n`CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC=1`. The package's forced plugin-update\ndefault is removed and native managed settings disable plugin auto-updates. No\nreal provider key or login token is an image input. Its managed settings also set\n`permissions.defaultMode = \"bypassPermissions\"` and `sandbox.enabled = false`,\nand `skipDangerousModePermissionPrompt = true`, using native dangerous-mode\nprecedence. This removes client prompts and client\ncommand sandboxing while retaining guest/VM/network/Marshall boundaries.\nProduction Anthropic remains disabled and these requests return\n`provider_unavailable`; this configuration is not provider enablement."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5081
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Clone and relocation exports send compressed ZFS streams (`zfs send -c`), with the\nsnapshot name last so resumed exports bind the same snapshot. Same-host clone\nstreams use `services.lilly.localTransferBytesPerSecond` (default 1 GiB/s), while\npeer transfers keep `transferBytesPerSecond` (default 64 MiB/s). On the\ndestination and for same-host clones, lilly-hostd runs the stream from typed\nfields, since the BEAM holds no ZFS permission: a local send or resume, or an\nSSH pull, into a policy-fixed receive\n([ADR-0183](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0183-guest-dataset-streams-in-hostd.md)).\nThe source host's root export worker keeps its own sender. Receive-side\nlineage, nonce and ownership verification is unchanged. Before this change, a\nmeasured same-host clone spent 46.9 of 71 seconds sending about 3 GB of\nuncompressed logical data at 64 MiB/s. Lilly reports newly offered clone effects on\nan immediate follow-up exchange instead of the next one-second poll, while\ndeliberately re-offered capture renewals keep the one-second cadence; the\nprepare, probe and connect steps stay ordered because later commands carry the\ndestination key from `prepare`. Native and post-deploy timings are pending."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5085
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Clones queue per source. Distinct requests create distinct private machines and\nindependent disks. Capture may stop the source; restoration and destination cleanup\nremain separate obligations when copying fails or the request is cancelled."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5089
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Cloning is currently unavailable for the Inception multi-disk profile."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5093
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Closed trusted request-source name; physical measurements stay in PostgreSQL."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5101
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Codex and Claude Code are ordinary guest processes, separate from Marshall's\nplatform executor. System provider settings choose Ziggy and verified public CA\ntrust. Their native approval prompts and command sandboxes are deliberately\ndisabled for this isolated guest-image use; the guest OS/VM/network/Marshall\nboundaries remain the authority boundary. A client configuration or nonsecret\nsentinel is not inference authority.\nGuest writers retain existing sudo/root capability. The pinned offline image\nclosure contains no provider secret and opens no additional listener."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5105
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Command reference"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5106
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Compaction is durable model work with its own completion validation. Publication\ncompares the context generation and eligible event frontier; failure leaves the\nprior checkpoint. A root Plan turn may wait on persisted human questions, and\none current authorized answer resumes its existing turn. A completed proposal\ncan admit one exact Work turn without changing the thread's machine. Archival,\ncancellation and authority loss invalidate unanswered requests. These states\nare execution progress, not proof of VM physical readiness."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5110
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Compute additionally owns `ServiceLevelAttempt`, `WorkflowServiceLevelAttempt`\nand `ServiceLevelTotal` under\n[ADR-0133](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0133-durable-physical-service-level-accounting.md).\nAdmissions commit with operations or accepted operation-linked SSH receipts.\nTheir immutable deadline results and permanent numeric aggregates are reliability\nevidence only. The reconciler reads retained physical and exact-execution\nreadiness evidence, and never changes execution, reservations or receipt status.\nTimers can classify a measurement failure while the guest continues to run.\nWorkflow attempts commit with their canonical SSH mutation receipts. They retain\nclone sequence and retry operation binding, terminal exclusions for cancelled or\nsuperseded original intents, and independent cancellation-command outcomes.\nThese measurements provide no workflow, reservation or execution authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5114
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Configure `services.brady`, its private signer custody, roots, dataset, and limits.\nInspect readiness and bounded cache counters. Cache data is disposable; signing\nidentity is not. See [Brady design](repo:docs/services/brady-design.md).\nWhen fleet OpenTelemetry is enabled, Brady also writes a mode-0600 numeric SLO\nsnapshot. Only resolved requests with terminal outcomes enter its denominator;\nmalformed requests and policy refusals stay outside it. A separate Rust process\nvalidates and exports the snapshot from the host network namespace. Collection\nloss never changes proxy results. The local collector socket is group-restricted;\na native request-to-metric check and measured target remain required before\ntreating the series as a fleet SLO."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5118
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Configured editor zones must contain at least two canonical lowercase DNS labels\nand at most 189 bytes, matching the shared protocol and native broker. Marshall's\nmodule/runtime guard and editor authority refuse a single-label zone; Audi's\nmodule and startup guard also refuse it when immutable editor assets are configured. Generic ingress with\neditor capability disabled retains its existing zone rules."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5122
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Confirmed, pending and form disk values preserve every supported 4096-byte-aligned\nfractional GiB value. The machine's identity, image, placement, addresses and data\nremain unchanged. A running request holds target CPU/RAM before stopping; unknown\nphysical effects retain holds. Matching target-size evidence commits growth.\nA measured capacity shortfall can leave the resized machine stopped, and an\nuncertain restart must be fenced before retry. A capacity report that is merely\nlate is not a shortfall. The request keeps its holds with the disk change\nconfirmed, and the host's next accepted report decides the restart (ADR-0140).\nProvisioner lock contention during the disk step is retried, never reported as an\nidentity conflict. Originally stopped machines remain stopped without\ncompute admission. Disk shrinking stays outside the accepted interface."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5126
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Conservative per-pool artifact budget for sealed image templates (ADR-0130); images larger than the budget use fresh verification for every provision."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5130
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Consult current ADRs and their linked reviews for feature-specific acceptance.\nSeveral decisions remain partial. Known boundaries include historical database\nreconciliation, pre-existing guest image migrations, provider-specific behavior,\nphysical failure domains, and unmeasured scale. A newer test count is not a broader\nguarantee. This handbook's own checks validate documentation and presentation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5134
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Control requests expire after five seconds. Their reply addresses expire when\nthe request completes, so late replies cannot crash the workspace or satisfy\nanother request. Caller identity still governs peer ownership. Retries reuse the\ndurable opening identity and cannot automatically resurrect a closed shell.\nThe [startup recovery review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-terminal-startup-recovery.md)\nrecords generated reply-order and opening-history tests, connected workspace\nregressions, and loopback TLS peer checks; native deployment acceptance is separate."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5138
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Control-room workload, job, operation, access, audit, Git and usage views are\nbounded business projections with timestamps. Job retries retain original attempt\nhistory and require current authorization; expected denials, replay and pruning\nremain separate from diagnostic traces. Use the canonical receipt and committed\noperation state to reconcile an uncertain reply. A diagnostic event may help find\nthe transaction, but absence of one does not authorize a replacement mutation."
msgstr ""

