#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5780
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Failed browser journeys may emit only closed document categories and validated\nbootstrap/error/connection booleans. Browser messages, URLs, headers, cookies,\ndocument text and WebSocket payloads remain private. The native fixture may\nadditionally observe fixed broker/worker/socket/refusal booleans after proving\nthe authenticated current boot and executed root UID, sharing one 30-second\nconsole deadline. Native unit metadata, journal bodies, worker arguments and\nterminal bytes are withheld; the only personal Node execution is `--version`.\nThese read-only observations do not launch editors or retry assertions, and\ndiagnostic refusal preserves the original failed acceptance. Their source\npresence does not prove runtime execution or identify the Ubuntu cause."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5784
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Failure and supersession can also terminate earlier phases. The execution and\ndataset journals retain launch and cleanup authority. The deadline starts at\nlaunch, allowing materialization its separate utility bounds. The original deadline\nsurvives retries; a cached receipt is reusable only for the same execution and\nboot challenge after physical confinement is rechecked. State and revision\npublish atomically in lifecycle envelope version 2; duplicate polling changes\nneither. After fsync, at most 128 reviewed UUID/state/time diagnostics per caller defer\nuntil the exact native writer releases. Confirmed release admits them to the\nbounded SDK queue and structured logs; spool handoff runs independently. Queue\nrefusal or uncertain lock release may drop diagnostics without undoing state.\nTemplate diagnostics retain closed host/pool identity; these\nobservations never authorize a copy, physical seal or execution."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5788
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Fenced guest deletion inventories both inhabited mount namespaces and process-held\nmount-namespace descriptors. A descriptor can preserve a sandbox's ZFS mount after\nits last process exits. Cleanup pins and rechecks these namespaces, unmounting only\nthe exact owned root at its canonical path. Aliases, live file holders, unreadable\nor oversized inventories and races retain the fence and disk reservation.\nCleanup pins the host proc directory before entering a foreign namespace, then\nopens that namespace's current self/mountinfo through it. A hidden or absent proc\nmount cannot substitute stale host inventory; open or classification failure\nstill retains the fence. The new proc-less descriptor subtest reproduced refusal\nbefore repair. The repaired full native check passed in 563 seconds including\nbuild time, retaining busy-file refusal and the surviving guest/process snapshot.\nAfter healthy `b9790a5c` activation, the original blocked Galileo source deletion\ncompleted. Independent exact-two SQL/ZFS/systemd checks confirmed source and\ntarget deletion, released reservation holds, absent datasets and inactive units;\nsee the [production review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-02-galileo-production.md).\nThis records observed recovery without arbitrary namespace churn. The\n[native scenario](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/zfs-guest/namespace-cleanup.py) includes\nan empty descriptor-held namespace, an active file holder and a surviving guest;\nthe native check passed on `5c623418`. After healthy production activation of\n`99f13b26`, the original blocked deletion completed through its existing request.\nIndependent SQL/ZFS/systemd checks confirmed the six original acceptance VMs\nwere deleted, reservations released, datasets absent and units inactive. A fresh\npost-repair three-guest campaign was also deleted; a second bounded proof covered\nall nine exact fixtures. The\n[acceptance review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-02-https-egress-production.md)\nkeeps this live evidence separate from native busy-file and neighbor preservation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5792
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Fifteen generated/fixed native full-commit archive histories use actual upstream\nTLS on port 443, packaged proxy/ZFS storage and two veth clients. Independent\npayload digests and origin counts distinguish complete anonymous reuse from\nprivate, trailer and truncated refusal. Fixed small truncation witnesses require\nterminal omission. The first native run failed in the inherited 64 MiB reuse\nmatrix before these histories. The final native capture\n`1790971037510-767403-0.jsonl` passed the full test in 300.02 seconds,\nincluding all fifteen archive histories, restart, concurrent readers and reduced\nquota. Earlier intermittent abandonments remain unexplained and retained as\nfailed evidence. This fixture establishes packaged TLS/ZFS and veth scope only."
msgstr ""

