#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5950
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Generated Marshall admission checks inject insert failures at twelve VM,\naudit, agent, ingress, placement, reservation, address, operation and\ndispatch-job stages. Each refusal leaves the complete committed public-table\ninventory unchanged; a later admission creates one linked set of the checked\nrows, and exact replay or changed-shape refusal adds no rows. These local\nchecks do not exercise optional source or Inception environment writes,\nprocess death at commit ambiguity or native job execution.\nGenerated [archived replay histories](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/admission_test.exs)\nreturn the original VM after one to four same-key retries, reject changed shape,\nand preserve the local VM, placement, reservation, address, operation, audit\nversion and dispatch-job inventory after each prefix. Lost HTTP replies,\nsimultaneous callers and cross-node replay at an uncertain commit remain open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5954
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Generated [Lilly channel histories](repo:lilly/test/terminal/channel_history_test.exs)\nexercise real local sockets and Stream callbacks: replay/live bytes retain exact\norder, byte and frame credit block excess output, duplicate input has no socket\neffect, exact cumulative ACKs release credit, malformed receipts fence channels,\nand EOF drains only after consumption. Transport loss stops channels synchronously;\na new attachment rejects old process output/ACKs even with the same channel ID.\nGuest managers are retained, but these tests do not establish native PTY lifetime\nor authenticate a reconnect. Each new attachment resets its local sequence space;\nuncertain input must not be replayed into that new incarnation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5958
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Generated [approval and expiry histories](repo:marshall/test/marshall/agents/agent_revocation_history_test.exs)\nalso compare exact CLI session and refusal receipts for repeated, fresh and\nowner/member digests after sharing withdrawal. They check that expiry removes\nonly old sessions with one receipt each and that a second sweep is idempotent.\nThese are SQL-backed checks, not browser or native CLI transport acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5962
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Generated [shared-ring histories](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/terminald/src/budget_property_tests.rs)\ncreate actual Linux PTYs at the configured 64 MiB aggregate reservation boundary.\nFixed 1 MiB/8 MiB and generated 2/4/8 MiB initial capacities isolate memory\nadmission from the session-count limit. Contending final reservations refuse\nwithout changing survivors; explicit retirement returns exact capacity for\nreplacement sessions. Complete retirement returns the counter to zero.\nThe [recorded native scope](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-terminald-shared-ring-budget.md)\npassed all 47 tests and Clippy. This is local admission/retirement evidence:\ndynamic growth, interleaved create/retirement, child-exit/idle release,\nauthenticated vsock, aggregate growth/admission with mixed viewer pressure and VM/browser composition remain\nseparate. Reservation capacity is not measured resident memory or throughput."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5966
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Generated [spool receipt histories](repo:ziggy/test/spool_test.exs) verify that\ncompleted usage receipts occupy bounded durable slots until exact acknowledgement,\nsurvive Ziggy process restart and free only acknowledged capacity. The focused\nsuite passed six checks, including one property, after correcting generated IDs\nto satisfy the protocol's canonical UUID requirement. This local property does\nnot measure delivery timing during a Marshall outage.\nAn exact Marshall 409 `completion_conflict` now stays distinct in Ziggy's control\nclient and reporter diagnostic reason; the disputed receipt remains in the spool\nfor operator recovery. A generated reply-class property checks the local mapping.\nIt does not prove lost-response replay or reporter recovery against a live\nMarshall service.\nGenerated [reporter histories](repo:ziggy/test/reporter_history_test.exs) additionally\ncheck fixed 2/127/128/129 receipt counts, transient/conflict/wrong-ACK retries,\nexact immutable bytes and per-batch attempt sets. Healthy neighbors drain around\none persistent conflict; spool restart retains that receipt and lifetime totals.\nThe focused property passed seed203368 in7.6seconds. Full Ziggy precommit passed 64\nchecks (15 properties, 49 tests), seed 521050, in 61.7 seconds. Forced Dialyzer passed\nin 5.33 seconds with zero errors, skips or unnecessary skips; terminal exit0.\nControlled initial batches do not establish timer cadence, HTTP lost-reply\nrecovery, Marshall commit durability or native disk fault recovery.\nZiggy sends its control requests over the verified-TLS shared control WebSocket.\nHTTP426 at upgrade, close4001 and an unsupported_version response retain a distinct\nversion refusal. Pending calls retired as unproven consult the owning stopped\nclient so close4001 cannot become an outage result.\n- **While fenced:** the accounting reporter stops normal-cadence retries without\n  acknowledging the durable spool, and the model-call poller stops claiming new\n  work.\n- **Recovery:** the fence is recoverable (ADR-0140). Only a backed-off probe may\n  run, after 30 seconds and doubling to ten minutes, and an accepted probe\n  resumes normal operation for response-level refusals on a live socket. An\n  upgrade426 or close4001 stops the shared socket until its owner is replaced\n  or auto-update restarts the application; the probe cannot revive that owner.\n  Generated [version histories](repo:ziggy/test/version_refusal_test.exs)\nand verified local TLS replies cover these local boundaries. Marshall's\n[closed satellite version property](repo:marshall/test/marshall/control/satellite_version_test.exs)\nchecks that every Ziggy control op answers an explicit wrong body version with\n`unsupported_version`; absent versions still receive `invalid_request`. Galileo\ncarries no body version: its version refusal is the control socket's 426 at\nupgrade or 4001 after hello. A process restart\nresets this local fence and can retry the retained receipt before an upgrade;\nhosted mixed versions, restart pacing and active provider tasks remain separate\ntests."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5970
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Generated admission histories withhold the reply after a real commit, then kill\nthe exact caller or its owned BEAM before nine concurrent retries across three\nsurviving nodes. Live and archived results retain the original VM and complete\nallocation inventory; changed-shape retries refuse. The\n[lost admission reply review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-admission-lost-reply.md)\nrecords passing distributed-file evidence and full1452-check Marshall precommit\nwith zero-error forced Dialyzer. HTTP reply loss, pre-commit ambiguity\nand native dispatch remain separate verification gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5978
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Generated certificate histories call production activation with delayed issued\njobs and newer pending, failed or issued generations. Stale jobs preserve the\nactive row, encrypted chain, timestamps and audit inventory; active-job replay\nis unchanged. Only the latest issued generation activates. The focused file\npassed seven checks, including one property. Independent-worker races, hosted\nissuer faults and recovery from a failed newer generation remain open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5982
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Generated cleanup histories compare complete public-table row digests before and\nafter both successful and deliberately failed assertions, while preserving an\nunrelated fixture's automatic histories and unused image catalog entries.\nFailures report changed tables and row hashes without payloads. If teardown also\nfails, the original\nfailure remains reported. Historical rows in older verification partitions and\nbaseline reproduction rows remain available; a clean fixture restores the prior\ninventory rather than assuming the database began empty. The\n[fixture review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-committed-fixture-history.md)\nrecords exact execution and remaining scope; the\n[authority fixture review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-authority-fixture-history.md)\nreproduces and repairs the retained catalog/retirement job histories. This is\ntest database hygiene, with\nno new native isolation or user-scenario acceptance claim."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5986
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Generated control/readiness histories and independent-process ordering checks\ncover these control-plane boundaries. The bounded native browser/two-Lilly campaign\npassed preview/refusal, elevated request/pause/continue, running/stopped moves,\nsource cleanup, retained data/ingress identity and fresh-elevation admission resume.\nIt uses real pinned SSH transfer endpoints and ordinary guests. Native full-stop\nconsent, cancellation/replan permutations, independent hosts and broader recovery\nacceptance remain tracked in [scenario coverage](#coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5990
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Generated coordinator histories and the native browser/guest journey are described\nin the [resize verification review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-resize-verification.md).\nSynthetic receipt tests do not establish filesystem preservation. Native evidence\nretains its exact platform and execution scope in [scenario coverage](#coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5994
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Generated local Linux PTY/socket histories and fixed configured-watermark and\nquiet-slave cases exercise this boundary. They do not prove authenticated vsock,\nFirecracker/browser composition, aggregate 64 MiB admission or escaped descendant\ncleanup. See the [review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-terminald-credit-retirement.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5998
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Generated public-action histories and six three-process schedules pass for these\ndatabase boundaries. The packaged ordinary-browser journey passed on captured\n`f4de549a`-based source with virtual passkey elevation, ordinary tree/blob/history\nand raw reads, refresh through a source outage, stale-page/raw refusal, audit\nattribution and actual cache deletion. Its cache uses an ordinary VM filesystem;\nit does not establish ZFS quota behavior. Existing service machine evidence covers\nlocal HTTPS Git clone, update, force-push retention and source outage. Physical\ntunnel, cache pressure and large-repository capacity remain separate; see the\n[scoped verification review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-git-mirror-verification.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6002
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Generated three-node capacity histories reject retained structured SQL deadlocks\nand accept clone activation only as success or a documented atom refusal. A\nrolled-back opaque activation error cannot count as a safe capacity refusal.\nThe focused race and wrapper properties passed seed202304 in60.2seconds. Full Marshall\nprecommit passed 1,423 checks (222 properties, 1,201 tests), two exclusions,\nseed59328,1465.7seconds; forced Dialyzer44.48seconds, zero errors/skips/unnecessary\nskips, exit0. Opaque errors in other step families and ungenerated lock\nschedules remain gaps. Fixture cleanup retries provide no mutation evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6006
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6011
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Global **Threads** is the primary task entry point; the machine navigation no\nlonger includes an Agents tab. The machine-scoped routes\n`/machines/:id/threads` and `/machines/:id/threads/:thread_id` remain available\ndirectly for selecting the root thread, creating a child or submitting a prompt\nunder existing machine authority. The CLI supports one browser-approved invocation:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6015
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Grafana adds operations and log dashboards alongside the existing baseline.\nOperations show numeric resource/state observations and independent queue health.\nThe operations dashboard provisions fifteen stable panels covering fleet and\nbackup/updater measurements, log queues/retries/refusals, trace custody,\nSDK availability/age/refusals/export failures and fresh BEAM memory/run queues.\nLogs select explicit application/platform sources and expose trace correlation.\nGrafana access and reader credential custody remain independent of Marshall\nsessions. Optional burn delivery uses private runtime webhook/credential files,\nHTTPS-only startup validation and notification health; delivery failure does not\nchange objective arithmetic. Receiver receipt still requires separate evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6019
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Grafana operators use `https://ghuntley.dev:3443/` with the separate `operator`\naccount. Its generated password is held in `/var/lib/grafana/admin-password`;\nhandle it privately and never put it in command arguments, logs or Nix options.\n`services.overallsOtelFleet.publicGrafana.enable = false` removes the dedicated\nHTTPS frontend and its firewall grant on the next configuration activation,\nwhile retaining local Grafana state and credentials. Certificate issuance and\nvalidated reload use the existing Marshall proxy certificate owner. Inspect\npublic TLS, login refusal and `/api/health` after deployment; a healthy collector\ndoes not establish public Grafana availability.\nCertificate publication and cached startup validate both certificate references\nwhen Grafana is enabled, replacing both with the candidate during HAProxy\nconfiguration validation. Zero or more than two references are refused. An\ninitial production rollout refused the second reference and stopped HAProxy;\nthe corrected validator preserves trust, hostname, lifetime and key checks."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6023
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Grafana reads fleet diagnostics from Prometheus, Tempo and VictoriaLogs. Marshall\nowns desired state, command receipts, authorization, PaperTrail versions and durable\nservice-level accounting. It no longer accepts a telemetry upload, lifecycle audit\noutbox or relocation progress stream through the control protocol. Its retired\n`/admin/fleet`, `/admin/logs` and `/admin/slos` views do not provide diagnostic readers.\nProtocol v4 retains the bounded host/pool evidence required for admission,\nreconciliation and current readiness; those facts remain control authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6027
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Grafana uses the log-store reader identity through verified fleet TLS. After reader\ncredential rotation restart `grafana.service` to refresh its systemd credentials,\nthen verify read success and insert refusal with synthetic isolated evidence.\nAn unavailable Grafana reader does not stop store ingestion. Store or Tempo quotas\nand archive/output budgets need separate review; retention alone cannot prove\noutage tolerance or successful backfill."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6031
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Grafana's baseline opens ninety days. Its source-status/evidence tables describe\nmissing or stale sources, warmup, coverage gaps, inactivity, incomplete seven-day\nhistory or volume, incomplete duration accounting and histogram overflow. Missing\nand stale sources precede inactivity. Empty or ineligible ratios remain unknown.\nFive-minute candidates require every declared source host and the source's own\nsampling clock. Retained Collector values cannot establish a live producer."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6035
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Grafana's pinned VictoriaLogs plugin uses `https://logs.fleet.internal:8443`, the\ncommitted CA and reader-only credentials delivered by systemd. Insert identity can\nwrite only `/insert/*`; reader identity can query `/select/*` and health, never\ninsert. Runtime credential paths enter configuration, their contents do not enter\nthe Nix store or browser. The store is not a general fleet HTTP proxy."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6039
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Grant this login user passwordless sudo."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6040
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Group under which Audiobookshelf runs."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6041
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Guest OTLP is a separate untrusted path. Audi supplies the current Lilly binding;\nthe receiver authenticates the Audi peer, replaces resource provenance, applies\nper-VM and host budgets and permits only reviewed guest metric names. Guest claims\ncannot enter authoritative fleet SLO arithmetic. Customer guests remain outside\nthe private integration zone. The guest path cannot impersonate an application\ntrace producer or fleet resource exporter."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6045
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Guest SSH and browser terminals use an automatically allocated Linux login such\nas `u200001`, with `/home/u200001` as its home. The login comes from a durable\naccount UID rather than your email address. It stays the same across machines and\nsame-account email changes. A new account registered after retirement receives a\ndifferent identity and does not inherit the former account's home or access.\nMarshall continues showing your email address; there is no username setting."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6049
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Guest identity discovery may durably allocate before the user owns a VM. Repeated\ndiscovery reuses that identity; it grants no VM access. Fresh UUIDs require new\ncredentials and explicit grants. A distinct username, UID and home prevents\nautomatic inheritance, while authorized guest writers retain passwordless sudo.\nHistorical homes are not confidential from newly authorized guest administrators.\nSame-User email changes are labels at this boundary and preserve its guest\nUUID/UID/name/home. Historical database restore remains unsupported until all\nretained reservation and sequence state is reconciled; see [recovery](#recovery)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6053
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Guest output remains bytes; terminal escape sequences do not authorize browser\nactions.\nThe host stream ignores repeated output sequence numbers. If an output frame\nskips the next expected sequence, it closes that viewer channel and signals the\nviewer to reattach with a scrollback cursor; it does not leave the channel\nsilently stalled. Generated local frame histories check this boundary, while\nnative interruption and browser reattachment remain separate evidence.\nGenerated [mailbox pressure histories](repo:marshall/test/marshall/terminal/host_stream_test.exs)\nfill one stalled viewer to the 64-message output bound and shed only that\nchannel. One to three other channels continue advancing after the close. This\nlocal host-stream test does not cover peer forwarding, browser WebSockets or\nproduction load."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6057
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "HSTS `includeSubDomains` commits every `ghuntley.dev` name to HTTPS in browsers\nthat have visited the apex. The names this repository serves: the apex (proxy\nTLS, HTTP-01 challenge and permanent redirect on port 80), `*.apps.ghuntley.dev`\n(Audi wildcard certificate; HTTP answers `308` to HTTPS for recognised hosts and\n`421` otherwise) and `ns1`/`ns2.ghuntley.dev` (DNS only at Audi's address; TLS\nfails closed and HTTP answers `421`, so no browser service exists). Ports 4443\nand 5443 on the apex serve service-CA TLS to non-browser clients. The apex DNS\nzone lives outside the repository; an HTTP-only name created there would stop\nworking in browsers that visited the apex."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6061
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "HTTP forwarding failures emit `audi.http_proxy_failed` with a fixed forwarding\nphase, timeout/closed/protocol/other category, response state and bounded event\ncount. Errors, URLs, headers and request or response bytes never enter that\nevent. Failure before response headers returns 502; an interrupted response\nstill terminates the stream without a successful final chunk. These categories\nlocate a failed hop; they do not prove the guest's cause or retry a request."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6065
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Hegel tests exercise the Rust boundary; the disposable `image-template` NixOS\ntest exercises production Ash journals, actual ZFS seals, leases, independent VM\ndisks, retirement, interrupted effects and the catalog bound. Its synthetic\nartifacts do not establish guest boot or\nfleet performance. The [execution review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md)\nrecords results and outstanding guest/deployment acceptance.\nThe extended disposable ZFS probe now checks that a validated warm callback\ncarries the ready record and incarnation UUIDs while the verified uncached\ncallback carries neither. The revised native `image-template` VM run passed\non reader revision `153db737` (205.65s script, 0.39s cleanup), including both\ncallbacks, independent disks, interrupted effects and bounded retirement.\nIt uses synthetic artifacts; no production template hit or real guest SSH\nfollows from this result."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6069
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Hints never bypass that fence: a halted DNS replica ignores `dns_snapshot`\nhints and a halted gateway worker ignores `fleet_certificate` hints. Before a\nrefusal, a `dns_snapshot` hint reads a fresh snapshot at once (a burst\ncoalesces into one read) and a `fleet_certificate` hint fetches the activated\ngeneration at once; the periodic refreshes stay as backstops."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6073
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Historical `wz4r` disk SHA256\n`e7fc0c04bccb4b443dd4bea2edcdabfa2d1481fee6b683891f4338b399625a41`\npassed native nine-module/764-payload assembly, all three SMF validations, the\nsafe native SSH executable check, read-only receipt extraction/export and clean\nshutdown. Its read-only baseline is\n`/tmp/overalls-omnios-native-ssh-config-final-artifact/`; clone it before booting.\nThe [native admission review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-image-admission.md)\nrecords exact kit/receipt hashes. The historical `wz4r` baseline remains outside\nruntime qualification and admission; current source-qualified service, growth and\nprocess-crash receipts are recorded separately. Exact-image lease withdrawal,\ntransport/reset, isolation and image qualification remain pending."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6077
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Historical backups can resurrect revoked credentials and obsolete commands.\nAutomatic historical fleet reconciliation is not available. This manual therefore\ndoes not prescribe a generic final activation command. Preserve uncertain capacity\nuntil physical obligations are settled."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6081
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Historical executions remain scoped to the revisions recorded in the\n[physical SLO review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-02-durable-physical-slos.md),\n[request/backlog review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-02-relocation-and-workflow-backlog-histories.md),\n[retention review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-telemetry-retention-and-diagnostics.md),\n[uncertain acknowledgment review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-producer-uncertain-ack.md),\n[recorder commit/reply review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-recorder-commit-reply-loss.md),\n[job-history review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-job-history-verification.md),\n[structured logging review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-19-structured-logging-fleet.md)\nand [public Grafana review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-public-grafana.md).\nThey do not establish activation or runtime acceptance of ADR-0149's replacement\npaths. The [decoupling review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md)\nand [scenario ledger](#coverage) record current checks and remaining boundaries.\nProduction rollout, physical multi-host recovery, sustained outage capacity,\ncomplete seven-day source history and notification receiver receipt require their\nown recorded acceptance.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6085
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Host attribute under nixosConfigurations."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6086
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Host backups use separate encrypted Restic repositories and independent passwords\nper hostname. The default schedule is thirty minutes with a bounded per-host\ndelay; retention keeps twelve complete recovery points. Defaults are policy, not\nproof that a deployment has configured or successfully restored backups."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6090
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Host credential rotation immediately invalidates previous host authority. Prepare\nprivate output custody, rotate, verify the result, publish encrypted material and\nrestart the consuming service promptly. Preserve guest journals and reservations.\nA timeout after issuance requires verification, not blind reissuance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6094
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Host firewall activation must preserve Lilly's owned nftables tables. Do not use\na global ruleset flush. The fleet perimeter separately declares public listeners\nand allowed source networks. Review both provider firewall and host rules when\nchanging a listener.\nThe public listener refuses every `/api` path except the agent CLI routes and\nknown-host discovery before reading request bodies;\nthe fleet listener has no browser routes. Generated path, method and host-header\nprobes verify both local plug chains return uncached 404 without browser cookies\nor redirects. Live TLS listener separation and purpose credentials require\nseparate transport evidence.\nSince 2026-10-16 the shared source registry contains only the Overalls and\nDungarees fleet host addresses; every personal and office address was removed at\nthe user's request. Operators reach fleet listeners through the Tailscale overlay\n(accepted on `tailscale0`). Anonymous reachability remains limited to the typed\npublic listeners (Audi, the proxy's HTTP-01 port and public Grafana). Network\nreachability never replaces SSH or application authentication."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6098
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Host liveness has one classification (`HostLiveness`, ADR-0140), derived from\nthe shared host row.\n- **States:**\n  - `disconnected`: no session;\n  - `live`: report no older than `capacity_freshness_ms`, five seconds;\n  - `late`: no older than `host_authority_ms`, sixty seconds;\n  - `lost`: older, missing or future-dated.\n- **Capacity decisions** (admission, start, resize, clone, relocation, drains\n  and evacuation) require `live`.\n- **Authority decisions** (terminal viewers and tickets, ingress, DNS\n  publication, inference, Galileo and SSH guest access) accept `live` or `late`,\n  so a slow report no longer disconnects viewers or drops DNS records.\n  The sixty-second window covers a Marshall-side outage: while Marshall cannot\n  write to its database it rejects every host's report, so a shorter window\n  would mark healthy hosts lost. A reset or replaced connection session still\n  ends authority at once.\n- A new or reset session, a credential change or retirement still ends\n  authority immediately.\n- Ingest accepts a sample up to the authority window, keeping its sample time,\n  instead of rolling back the whole exchange and losing its outcomes. A late\n  sample therefore keeps the host authoritative but never makes its capacity\n  fresh."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6102
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Host queue budget; selected per-source output limits must fit. Size from measured rate for 24 hours plus 50% headroom."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6106
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Host snapshot cleanup compares the durable dataset GUID and local nonce before\nunmounting or destroying. Foreign or inherited markers, changed GUIDs, conflicting\nmounts and unavailable inspection retain the descriptor without destructive work.\nAn unrecorded snapshot GUID does not prevent cleanup when the remaining native\nproofs match. Confirmed absence removes intent; an absent snapshot with a claiming\nmount refuses. Uncertain inspection after destruction retains intent for retry."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6110
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Host uplink carrying routed guest egress."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6111
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Host-lock, transfer-stream (under its hostd lease, ADR-0183) and source-export\nhelpers retain completion custody until every\nadopted child is reaped across process groups/sessions. Direct leader retirement\ndoes not permit a reply or successor mutation. Native completion and failure\nhistories, scoped selector mutations and source identity after integration are\nrecorded in the [host-lock review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-host-lock-descendant-custody.md)\nand [transfer review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-transfer-stream-adopted-children.md).\nThe wait remains blocking: explicit escaped-child death is part of these fixtures,\nnot proof of bounded cgroup confinement or physical ZFS/SSH recovery. Full Lilly\nwith the exact verified helpers passed506checks and forced test Dialyzer with\nzero errors/skips. Integrated publication and physical/hosted acceptance remain pending."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6115
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Host-tool receipt required before polling."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6116
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Host-wide native log file budget."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6117
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "If a mounted machine or terminal depended on an administrator override and that\nverification ends, the operation is refused and the UI returns to Fleet workloads\nwith an expiry explanation. Selecting the machine there opens a fresh passkey\nstep-up. Resize keeps its draft URL, removes mutation controls and offers a\nFleet workloads recovery link. Current owner and sharing permissions continue\nnormally. Foreign Customer access remains refused without a verification hint."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6121
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "If a new administrator has no key, the sign-in section of the account page\n(`/settings#security`) first requires fresh email authentication for enrollment. The user returns to the original page and\nexplicitly submits the action again; setup retains only an allowlisted return\npath, never administrative arguments or a pending continuation.\nCancelled, expired, replayed or substituted continuations, stale targets and\nwithdrawn authority leave no mutation. New input requires a new explicit action.\nAlready committed durable workflows retain their own recovery authority after\nelevation expires or the requester is demoted. Customer owner-only refusals\nremain effective during retry. This accepted continuation is not established by\nthe historical workflow checks below. Focused receipt properties and packaged\naccount-action browser evidence are recorded in [scenario coverage](#coverage);\nbroader native workflow continuation and timed-expiry acceptance remain gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6125
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "If a turn stalls, inspect machine readiness, durable turn/model state, Ziggy\nreadiness, profile capability policy, and the guest executor. Do not replay a tool\nby editing receipt rows. A provider timeout can leave an uncertain remote effect;\nrecovery follows the recorded command identity.\nZiggy's model poller fences after a classified control-version refusal. Its\nbacked-off probe may recover a response-level refusal on a live socket; upgrade426\nand close4001 leave the owning shared client stopped until replacement or update. A generated\n[poll history](repo:ziggy/test/version_refusal_test.exs) varies transient errors\nbefore that refusal and verifies that later poll messages start no model task.\nThe local test does not prove a hosted version-skew rollout or the fate of an\nalready-active provider task."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6129
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "If set, merge all definitions that don't have an associated option\ntogether using this type. The result then gets combined with the\nvalues of all declared options to produce the final `\nconfig` value."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6133
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "If this is `null`, definitions without an option\nwill throw an error unless {option}`_module.check` is\nturned off."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6137
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Illumos activated queue/interrupt/DMA storage now has static lifetime until VM\ndisposal. Fallible allocations precede `DRIVER_OK`; runtime detach refuses and\nunavoidable later activation failures fence readiness, drain workers and retain\nthe bounded unavailable attachment. A refused VMM device reset cannot authorize\nresource reclamation. Independent source review confirms this control flow;\nnative DMA/reset acceptance remains separate from the correction and from the\nunexplained initial ZFS I/O errors.\nSource-extracted host fault injection and three rejected lifetime mutants cover\n236 preactivation failures and both retained late failures. Separately, direct\nblock requests are bounded by each request's worst-case data plus two metadata\ndescriptors, with scatter clamped before DMA attributes; 265,596 extracted-helper\narithmetic/sanitizer vectors passed. These do not establish native DMA safety\nor prove the initial disk failure's cause."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6145
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Immutable image bound exclusively to the Inception development profile; native host eligibility is also required."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6149
