#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Loopback-only VictoriaLogs HTTP port."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6431
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "MSI-X reset state must agree between guest-visible PCI capability and internal\ninterrupt routing: MSI-X disabled, function mask clear, individual vectors\nmasked. A pre-enabled capability previously made illumos skip the enable write\nwhile internal routing remained disabled/masked, so completed block requests\nnever interrupted. The correction retains ordinary enable/mask semantics and\nrefuses interrupt delivery while MSI-X is disabled. Disposable numeric tracing\nand polling identified this fault; neither diagnostic variant belongs in an\naccepted guest or VMM artifact."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6435
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Machine references accept names or UUIDs. Names are lowercase, begin with a letter,\nand contain letters, digits and single separating hyphens, up to 63 characters.\nUUID-shaped names are reserved for machine identifiers.\nCreation without a name generates one. Creation without an image selects the\noperator's default image. Creation without `--profile` selects OSS; use\n`--profile customer` for the restricted Customer environment. Omitted CPU,\nmemory and disk requests use defaults raised to the image minimum; explicitly\nundersized requests fail."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6439
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Machine-page editor eligibility reuses the validated image/release authority\ncheck and exposes only a finite status after current VM read authorization. A\nhidden button or upgrade explanation is presentation; direct opening still\nrequires fresh stored-login/write/account/execution authority. The active link\nrequires both desired and observed running state. Valid legacy/noncurrent images\nshow current-image guidance; missing, malformed or wrong-identity data and invalid\nrelease configuration show temporary unavailability and refuse opening. Catalog\ndisabling prevents new launches without adding revocation of an already running\nmatching image.\nCreating another machine and copying chosen files preserves the original data;\nthis operation does not rewrite an old disk's immutable image identity."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6443
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Machine/creator/project instruction precedence, bounded file reads, managed\nskill storage and explicit upgrade-required failures are described in\n[agent context](#agents). Linux/Windows native execution and rollout evidence\nremain separate in the [context review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-16-agent-context-and-planning.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6447
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Magic links use an encrypted outbox and retryable mail jobs. Configure verified\nremote SMTP or explicitly selected loopback relay mode. Check sender identity,\nprovider TLS and delivery; an accepted SMTP transaction is not inbox evidence.\nNever print the token-bearing message to diagnose delivery."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6451
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Magic-link email proves mailbox access only when its single-use token reaches\nthe authenticated POST action. The browser now posts automatically after the\nlink page connects and requests a remembered credential. A GET-only visitor\ndoes not consume the token; an automated visitor that runs JavaScript may do so.\nStored login, MFA, remembered-login revocation and sign-out remain separate\nauthority checks. The automatic browser flow has focused HTTP and a recorded\nthree-replica native browser run; physical-host and real inbox behavior remain\nseparate acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6455
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Magic-link requests queue an encrypted outbox record and a private delivery\njob. The mail action locks and rechecks the row before submission; a delivered\nor expired record cannot start another submission. Each retry uses the same\nMessage-ID and token payload. Message-ID now uses the delivery UUID in a fixed\n`overalls.invalid` identifier namespace; the configured sender still supplies\nFrom, and sender rotation cannot change the corrected implementation's retry\nidentity. The namespace is not a delivery destination or DNS/TLS endpoint.\nThe older implementation derived this identifier from the live sender domain;\nan uncertain delivery spanning that format transition may have a different first\nupgraded ID because the old emitted identifier was not stored. That transition,\nprovider deduplication and body stability across endpoint rotation remain gaps.\nAn actual post-ACK transaction-loss history preserves independently committed\npending ciphertext until retry commits. A sender-rotation history reproduced the\nold identity mismatch and passed its repaired selection. Combined mail execution\npassed19checks (9properties,10tests),seed0,266.0seconds. Forced test-environment\nDialyzer passed with zero errors/skips on the mail worktree. Integrated Marshall\nprecommit on the b6496b73 merge passed1479checks (245properties,1234tests),\n2excluded,seed755639,1598.9seconds, with zero-error/skips forced test Dialyzer.\nNewer-main integration and native/inbox acceptance remain separate in the\n[mail review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-auth-mail-post-ack-runtime.md).\nSMTP acceptance with a lost result can still\nproduce a duplicate submission, so the link remains single-use and receipt\nis not proof of inbox placement. A generated local\n[retry property](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/auth_emails_test.exs)\nchecks the stable identity and terminal recheck through an adapter that loses\nthe result after acceptance. Generated implicit-TLS and STARTTLS\n[post-DATA histories](repo:marshall/test/marshall/mailer/smtp_test.exs) additionally\ncheck the real ten-second owner deadline, client socket closure, unchanged pending\nciphertext, stable decoded token payload and terminal no-connection replay.\nThe postmerge focused file passed eight checks in 114.6 seconds, as recorded in the\n[SMTP review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-mail-smtp-timeout-histories.md).\nThe [committed worker histories](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/auth_email_distributed_property_test.exs)\nadd three independent Marshall peers, real row-lock blocking, post-DATA abrupt\npeer death and replacement-peer terminal reads. The final focused file passed both\nproperties in63.7seconds; forced Dialyzer passed in74.84seconds and full precommit passed1,432checks,seed612345,1525.2seconds with forced Dialyzer50.9seconds as recorded in\ntheir [review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-mail-committed-worker-histories.md).\nThe [waiting-token properties](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/auth_email_waiting_authority_property_test.exs)\nremove or expire the captured stored token through a third committed peer while\na second worker is blocked on the outbox lock. After the first attempt receives\nan explicit SMTP rejection, the waiter must erase and expire the outbox without\na second connection. The combined four-property run passed in 80.8 seconds,\nseed63342, as recorded in the\n[authority review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-mail-waiting-token-authority.md).\nStored-row removal does not establish complete sign-in consumption or session issuance.\nOban duplicate-job scheduling, exact natural expiry, token changes after validation, the post-acknowledgment\ncommit window, host relay composition and inbox placement remain separate gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6459
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Manage integrations through `/integrations`, `/teams`, or Porsche. Secret values\nare write-only and redacted on read. Configure the independent service credentials\nand private frontend before attaching workloads. See [Galileo](repo:docs/services/galileo.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6463
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Managed operations share a host lock. Do not run independent Restic mutations\nconcurrently. Failed cleanup retains ownership evidence and prevents publication\nof a complete point. Never erase a journal to make backup status healthy."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6467
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Managed skill configuration changes affect later snapshots. Guest operations\npublish pinned immutable revisions and report their original operation identity;\nan uncertain reply is resolved by a status read. Failed updates keep the active\nrevision, admitted turns retain their referenced versions, and reopening\nrestores recorded commits/digests instead of following branch heads. The\nrestoration coordinator uses a bounded round-robin cursor so one blocked thread\ncannot monopolize the scan. Active receipts continue through their existing\nturn, terminal failures are not replayed automatically for the same machine\ngeneration, and rejected restorations emit a bounded reason event before the\nscan advances. A fresh machine key makes the pinned revision eligible again."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6471
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Management-only AWS credentials. Null uses explicit EC2 role mode."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6475
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Manual SSH key registration and browser key approval serialize with retirement\nthrough the account admission fence. A registration committed first is included\nin old-UUID cleanup. If retirement wins, registration is refused without adding\nkey or approval records. Completed cleanup leaves no active key for that retired\nUUID. A fresh identity must explicitly register the released fingerprint and gets\na new registration ID; existing sessions stay bound to the old ID.\nGenerated same-email histories and three independent Marshall processes verify\nboth registration orders and exact committed inventories. This is database\nworkflow evidence; native concurrent browser/SSH delivery remains separate.\nSee the [credential review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-credential-lifecycle-verification.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6479
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Marshall TLS endpoints, keyed by backend identity."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6480
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Marshall checks every configured authoritative DNS replica for the exact live\nACME TXT proof before acknowledging a challenge. A negative check retains a\nclosed cause class (`invalid_request`, `transport`, `absent`, `malformed_reply`,\n`ttl_out_of_window`, `value_mismatch` or `local_defect`) in the catalogued\n`ingress.fleet_certificate_propagation_waiting` event, without the DNS packet,\nname or proof. The selected issuer still retries the challenging generation;\nthe event does not itself quarantine or escalate it. Generated loopback TCP\nproperties cover the local checker and two-replica refusal, not production\ndelegation or minute-tick issuer progress."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6484
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Marshall instances share PostgreSQL. Local processes and PubSub improve delivery;\nthey do not replace durable authority. Ash resources define domain actions and\npolicy boundaries. Oban performs retryable background work."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6488
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Marshall is a private control plane at the apex `https://ghuntley.dev`; nothing it\nserves is meant to appear in a search index. Two independent mechanisms say so:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6492
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Marshall owns per-VM thread history, prompts, model calls, child-agent joins, and\nrecovery. A user with write access can prompt a stopped VM; the request starts it\nthrough the normal admission path. Deleted or unrunnable machines return an\nunavailable result."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6496
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Marshall projects per-capability guest facts (`guest_capabilities`: available,\nreadiness, trust, terminal, workspace, flush, SSH, agents, editor, Inception)\nfrom the immutable image\n([image](repo:marshall/lib/marshall/compute/image.ex),\n[views](repo:marshall/lib/marshall/compute/views.ex)), each derived from the\nprotocol's capability table for the row-bound validated manifest and all false\nwhen the manifest is missing, corrupt or mismatched: presentation hides\nTerminal, Agents, the editor control and the SSH connection commands when the\ncorresponding capability is false and explains why, while terminal authority,\nagent model calls, the agent executor binding and web search refuse on their own\ncapability; admission refuses the Inception profile unless the image's agent set\nhas it, and provisioning admits the creation-to-ready service level only for an\nimage whose agent set has `readiness` (an unknown snapshot image keeps the\nmeasurement). An image change in the creation form resets the size defaults to\nthe selected image's minima. The image stays out of `fleet/guest-images.nix`;\nstaging and registration are operator actions after every host runs a release\nthat understands the shapes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6504
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Marshall renders The Monospace Web (ADR-0161). Every page sits on a character\ngrid one `ch` wide and one line height (1.2rem) tall; borders are 2px and are\nsubtracted from padding so boxes stay on the grid. The stylesheet is\nhand-written in `marshall/assets/css` and bundled by esbuild beside the\napplication JavaScript; no CSS framework, component generator or icon set is\ninvolved. Icons are text glyphs and diagrams are box drawing or Mermaid."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6508
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Marshall's Control room audit accepts `kind=editor` and exposes bounded redacted\nlogin, credential and lease transitions under the existing current-user\n`admin_read` policy. It carries identifiers and closed action/status projections,\nnever raw approval proofs, cookies, paths, commands or terminal bytes. Revoked\nstored-login readers refuse. PaperTrail audit versions follow the global ninety-day\nretention inventory; bounded operational cleanup expires old authority separately."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6512
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Marshall's SSH domain stores public certificate generations in pending, issued,\nfailed and superseded states. Issuance holds service or VM authority locks and an\nadvisory subject lock through local signing and commit. A partial unique index\npermits one current generation per subject. Matching valid retries reuse it;\nfailed signing publishes no certificate. Principals come from server policy and\nVM endpoints, never caller-supplied names. The CA private key stays in a Marshall\nsystemd credential, outside PostgreSQL and release artifacts.\nSubjects retain stable service or VM identities across credential rotations and\nboots. New keys supersede earlier generations. Hourly cleanup retains seven days\nof superseded or expired public history, deletes at most 500 rows per transaction,\nand queues continuation batches. Deleting history does not revoke certificates."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6520
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Marshall's existing HTTPS deployment closure also includes its selected immutable\nbrowser launcher package. Null disables downloads; enabling it creates no new host,\nlistener, service identity or external signing service. Public archive availability\ndoes not establish a successful authenticated guest launch."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6524
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Marshall's public proxy terminates TLS and verifies backend TLS identities. ACME\nsupports HTTP-01 peer routing and optional Route 53 DNS-01. All frontends sharing\na public name must route challenges correctly. Explicitly select the CA and accept\nits terms before issuance. Never use staging roots as production public trust.\nThe fleet perimeter normally hides the proxy's HTTP-01 ingress from the public\nCA. A host opts in with `services.marshallProxy.acme.http01.publicIngress`\n(ADR-0181), which admits only TCP 80 on the proxy address, sharing the proxy's\nsingle `marshall-proxy` public entry with Grafana's port. Overalls opts in so\n`ghuntley.dev` renews unattended; HTTPS on 443 stays source-restricted. Without\na valid certificate the publication validator keeps HAProxy stopped, so failed\nissuance takes the browser origin down rather than serving an untrusted name."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6532
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Maximum receive stream bytes per second, with a 64 KiB burst allowance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6536
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Maximum same-host clone stream bytes per second; these never cross the network."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6540
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Maximum space in GiB a single collection run may delete."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6541
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Measured ZFS free bytes still account for all retained data. With no matching\nallocation credit, that child's outstanding startup disk hold cannot be offset;\nsettled virtual promises do not consume the physical admission budget. The\ncurrent launch/readiness decoder still refuses the child. Recognition neither\nrewrites metadata nor grants launch, admission, readiness or deletion authority,\nand adds no legacy decoder or conversion under ADR-0159."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6545
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Measured and reverted, with no gain on a 1-vCPU guest:\n- starting the trust receiver before `basic.target`;\n- replacing udev-settle with an `eth0` device dependency;\n- skipping root fsck."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6549
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Measured or configured IOPS limit; null means unknown. ZFS uses logical whole-pool operations. This is monitoring metadata, not admission capacity."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6553
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Measurement diagnostics expose only fixed roster identities, numeric counts,\nages and closed status codes. Grafana requires its own operator authentication;\nMarshall retains current-session checks for control and security views. Diagnostic\nroutes and readers are retired from Marshall. Missing/stale source states precede\ninactivity, and neither diagnostics nor guest claims authorize execution.\nThe loopback storage probe uses a separate read-only namespace with only the two\ntelemetry stores exposed under `/var/lib`; private runtime and configuration are\nhidden. It exports aggregate sizes, never names, contents or credentials. Its\nroot read capability does not confer provider or measurement-writer authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6561
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Merging Lilly's pending and delivering trust journal writes (about 6 ms each)\nwas not worth the change."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6565
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Minimum free Lilly pool space before capture and during upload."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6569
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Minimum free space in GiB on the filesystem holding /nix. Falling\nbelow it triggers a collection run."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6573
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Minimum remaining lifetime before a certificate can be published."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6577
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Multi-GiB acceptance retains the original per-guest request window on replay.\nCompleted bounded receipts must match the script fingerprint and resume only\nowned-path cleanup, with at most five unconfirmed-channel retries. Missing legacy\nfingerprints fail closed; forwarding, transport failure and later unrelated hits\ndo not establish success. Production readiness failures and an earlier unexplained\nnative fill abandonment remain separate gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6585
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Named IPv4 sources allowed to reach every fleet host over TCP and UDP."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6589
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Named destination-scoped listeners admitted from any IPv4 source; each needs an explicit local address, at least one TCP or UDP port, and a reviewed comment."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6593
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Named integrations forward to reviewed HTTP targets or peer VMs. Marshall owns\nattachments, team access, encrypted injected credentials, and renewable admission.\nGalileo strips/injects configured headers and cancels forwarding when renewal fails.\nPersonal integrations require explicit source VM attachments, including owner\nmachines. Current members of live owning teams retain automatic access. Existing\npersonal configurations receive no backfill or compatibility exemption.\nA verified Marshall `unauthorized` answer is an authorization refusal: Galileo returns guest403\nbefore reading an upload or contacting the origin and emits the reviewed\nrequest-denied event. Invalid/outage exchanges remain guest503;426 retains its\nversion-refusal class. Response bytes cannot turn a403 into admission or an\noutage. A refused renewal still cancels the existing request without retry.\nThe private HTTP/1 frontend retains Bandit body reads in the stream owner;\nthe lease guardian closes the ThousandIsland frontend socket when authority\nfails, interrupting blocked uploads and response writes while owner cleanup\ndecrements counters. Idle deadlines do not replace revocation deadlines.\nGenerated partial-response prefixes pass through lease failure and consumer halt\nwithout late delivery. The packaged fault fixture passed blocked uploads and\npartial responses after a successful silent renewal, then refusal, invalid TTL\nor renewal stalled beyond expiry. It measures origin EOF/reset, frontend return\nand zero active requests within five seconds and independently counts accepted\nTLS connections and dispatches. This is isolated Galileo/Bandit evidence with a\nsynthetic control authority. The corrected real-policy fleet withdrawal and\nseparate cross-host Galileo fleet checks also passed in one physical KVM failure\ndomain. Both production hosts activated `7fda1272`, including the subsequent\n403 classification correction. Real NixOS direct/peer sources passed unattached\n403 without origin traffic, explicit attachment, detach and restoration. One\nstalled request survived renewal, then closed its origin and reached zero active\nrequests within 1.81 seconds after observed fresh refusal. Direct/peer 1 MiB upload\ndigests and method/query checks passed. Production invalid-TTL/control-timeout,\nblocked-upload and partial-response fault permutations remain native-only.\nThe campaign used verified persistent SSH observations after a separate fresh\nSSH admission refusal; it does not establish arbitrary SSH availability.\nBoth original VM deletion receipts succeeded, both integrations were removed,\nall compute/disk holds were released and no matching native datasets/units remain.\nGenerated 600–700 ms lease histories allow zero or one valid renewal before a\nrefusal, invalid TTL or renewal delayed past expiry. The verified local TLS\norigin sees one stalled request handler, while Galileo cancels without\ndelivering response bytes. The [lease property](repo:galileo/test/upstream_test.exs)\ndoes not exercise Marshall withdrawal, Audi forwarding, physical dial counts\nor hosted network faults.\nGenerated local TLS uploads now vary source chunk sizes and pull failure points;\nthe fixture origin counts handler dispatches by unique guest path during a\nbounded quiet window. Physical TLS dials, late retries, origin receipt of\npartial bytes, response faults and external origins remain unverified.\nPeer requests carry bound provenance; a guest cannot assert another VM's identity.\nAuthorized attempts now feed a fixed cumulative outcome and duration snapshot.\nThe private host-only `/slo` read and Rust exporter use a Galileo-specific local\ncollector socket. Guest identities and integration names never become SLO labels;\nthe packaged and full Firecracker source-to-collector journeys passed, while\nlive production collection and a measured baseline remain open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6597
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native Linux/Windows path handling, authenticated continuation, live revocation\nand independent-host recovery need their own execution evidence. A parser test,\nsynthetic provider result or browser fixture cannot establish those boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6601
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native SSH helpers obtain fresh MMDS authority per invocation and keep host keys,\nlocks and readiness volatile. Separate managed sshd configuration refuses root\nand password login and forces the current-authorization session helper. Exact\npinned sudo bytes alone may regain setuid mode during image assembly; extraction\ndoes not activate package privilege. Periodic roster/certificate refresh removes\nreadiness on failure. Actual authorized SSH, expiry, retained-home and current\nsession refusal still require target-native journeys."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6605
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native `exec_command` passes the executor's existing lease/stop callback into\nthe bounded process runner. It checks before spawning and during every polling\nturn; the callback checks host stop requests immediately and renews the lease\nat its five-second cadence. A refusal kills the command's process group, reaps\nthe direct child and discards its result. A scoped collector enforces the child\ndeadline independently of a blocking lease RPC. Output remains bounded to 4 KiB\nper stream and command duration to 20 seconds. This enforces\n[ADR-0100](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0100-pulled-agent-work-over-ziggy-control.md)'s\nfenced execution on the native path; a fresh image replay must still prove\nlease withdrawal during a running native command. Descendants that deliberately\nleave the process group are outside this cleanup guarantee.\nAll six local process regression tests and the pinned Rust/type/link gates\npassed for this collector, including callback refusal and a blocked lease RPC.\nThose Linux process tests remain separate from native guest lease withdrawal."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6609
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native boot diagnostics also exposed a UART transmit-empty interrupt boundary.\nFreeBSD fills the16-byte FIFO before enabling transmit interrupts; the pinned\nUART previously failed to signal when THR was already empty. The reviewed patch\nsets pending THRE and signals only on the disabled-to-enabled transition,\nincluding re-enabling a pending interrupt; an unchanged enable bit and DLAB\ndivisor writes preserve their existing semantics. A regression through the\nproduction UART API fails on the original dependency and passes the patch.\nThe production VMM, identity and selected patch gates passed in173seconds;\nthat source/build evidence requires separate native guest boot and transport\nreplays. Console silence alone does not identify a blocked guest kernel stack."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6613
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native boot now includes a root-only mounted-root growth helper before MMDS\nidentity and network. It verifies both GPT copies/CRCs, exact disk/partition\nidentities and actual capacity before native resize commands, then requires a\nfresh volatile success receipt. OmniOS read-only pool discovery searches fixed\ndevice labels with its userland cache disabled; no persisted early-boot cache is\nrequired. Assembly pool GUID, one canonical whole-disk vdev and raw-device\ncustody remain mandatory. A disposable missing-cache diagnostic passed the\nrevised helper's preflight, expansion, post-GPT preservation and success receipt\nwhere the old query refused. This same-boot fault case is separate from new-image\ngrowth/recovery qualification. Twelve pure checks and three native FreeBSD\nQEMU boots passed one unchanged root and two expansions, retaining home bytes,\nnonroot GPT entries and a foreign disk. The later exact canonical-roots/SSH\nFreeBSD image passed 334-second Firecracker composition through three clean\nboots/two expansions with complete service oracles, preserved data and strict\nEFI inventories (only bounded root `NvVars` mutable). The final reviewed\nblocking-flush image passed all five services/growth/policy/daemon-recovery/\nsame-disk SIGKILL-recovery variants, with exact image and immutable receipt paths\nin the native review. The recorded source-qualified OmniOS growth replay separately covers three clean boots and two expansions; interrupted expansion remains open.\nThis adds a tenth production executable\nper OS beyond the recorded eighteen-executable package. OmniOS's offline SMF\nprofile disables all four stock cloud-init instances and stock SSH; only\nOveralls bootstrap and the roster supervisor own those startup authorities.\nSeed-fixed native assembly and fresh-boot resolver/disabled-service checks\npassed. A diagnostic Firecracker boot also passed the complete AF40/file\nverifier and nine transport echo sizes through 1 MiB after a debugger-only stock\n`pseudo_isa` override. The assembler now preserves stock files and binds\npersistent pseudo ISA plus loader/kernel serial settings; final exact-image\nreplay remains required. No diagnostic override grants production authority.\nThe first formal persistent-console boot reached ordinary login but refused\nservices: the remaining plumb-only stock vioif0 file blocked physical networking,\nand all three Overalls manifests used an invalid stability enum. The correction\nremoves only the four fixed stock vioif0 address/DHCP files, preserves unrelated\ninterfaces and binds their absence into assembly and boot verification.\nThe corrected manifests pass actual native `svccfg validate`; the old-enum mutant\nis rejected. Assembly and verification now require that native schema check.\nActual service import/methods and the separate ZFS I/O failure require replay;\ndecoded FMD errors precede the later reset attempts.\nThe final corrected token `985301b4` kit passed native clean-export assembly\nwith nine linked modules, 764 exact payload entries, all three native manifest\nvalidations and the four recorded network removals. A read-only receipt import\nand clean administration shutdown sealed disk `24318238`; its exact hashes and\ntest-only artifact are in the native review. Normal boot and complete services\nfor that disk remain separate machine gates. Native assembly is recorded manual\nexecution, not a reproducibly Nix-built disk or admitted fleet artifact.\nIts first service, ordinary-transport and reset attempts all failed early with\nblank serial and Firecracker `Shutdown(GenericError)` before fixtures or probes.\nThe cause remains under investigation; none establishes native runtime success.\nThe later completion-corrected `76b8c1ad` kit passed a separate pristine native\nassembly with the same nine-module/764-entry/schema/network checks, read-only\nreceipt extraction and clean shutdown. Sealed disk `a49255bd` and its exact\nreceipt are recorded in the native review. A paired direct-only QEMU diagnostic\nreaches console login on `76b8` under the same no-vsock settings where `9853`\npanics mounting root. Its growth service enters maintenance; corrected\nFirecracker service/transport/reset acceptance remains a separate gate. The\nearlier failed `9853` disk remains preserved. The first corrected-image\nFirecracker service run stays alive and reaches login but misses its 240-second\nfirst-boot deadline because growth enters maintenance and bootstrap withholds\nnetwork/identity. Retained serial corrects an earlier wrapper-rendered\nblank-output impression; the sliced expansion operand is separately diagnosed.\nThe corrected growth-operand kit `d0rd` passed a fresh native assembly with\nnine modules, 764 payload entries, native schema checks, clean export and\nshutdown. Sealed disk `bea32fe6` retains token `76b8c1ad`; that historical kit remains separate from the later source-qualified service and growth receipts. Transport/reset replay and supervised daemon recovery remain open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6617
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native bootstrap canonicalizes only local `ifconfig` MAC output: exactly six\none- or two-digit ASCII hexadecimal octets become lowercase two-digit octets\nbefore comparison. External MMDS remains strictly canonical, and malformed or\nforeign values refuse. The regression/type/build gates and corrected `sis8`\nnative clean-export assembly passed, sealing disk `1e095659`. Complete service\nreplay remains pending and grants no admission. Later executor lease/stop\ncallback changes require another kit and exact-image replay."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6621
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native growth runs only `overalls-native-grow-root` without arguments. It derives\nthe mounted root, checks pinned dual-GPT identity/capacity, applies native grow\ncommands and writes `/var/run/overalls/root-growth.json` before bootstrap may\npublish identity. Twelve pure checks and three native FreeBSD QEMU boots passed\none unchanged root plus two expansions with retained home/GPT/foreign-disk checks;\nthe later exact canonical-roots/SSH image passed 334-second Firecracker growth\nwith three clean boots, two expansions and full service oracles. A host-direct\nFirecracker diagnostic on a disposable OmniOS `76b8` clone reproduced the `s1`\nexpansion-operand refusal and unsliced whole-disk success. The corrected helper\nretains validated `s1` authority and raw `p0` GPT preflight, using the unsliced\ndisk only for expansion. The typed Rust/Clippy/native build and fresh corrected\nkit `d0rd` assembly passed; read-only disk `bea32fe6` has its exact receipt in\nthe native review. Corrected-helper OmniOS replay and interrupted\nexpansion remain pending; final blocking-flush FreeBSD replay\npassed the same three-boot/two-expansion boundary. The\nOmniOS kit's offline SMF profile disables stock cloud-init's four instances and\nstock SSH; exact-profile database-copy validation passed without touching the\nlive repository. Assembly removes the fixed four stock vioif0 address/DHCP files\nand binds continued absence into verification. Assembly and booted verification\nvalidate all three exact manifests with native `svccfg validate` before receipts.\nThe corrected `Unstable` manifests pass actual native validation; the old-enum\nmutant refuses. Schema validity does not establish methods or service readiness.\nA new assembled image must pass fresh-boot disabled-state and immutable payload\nchecks. The native isolation fixture's composed driver and\nLinux nft smoke pass; the exact canonical-roots/SSH FreeBSD image also passed\ntwo clean native policy boots with sink controls, actual guard drops and source\nrecovery. OmniOS process-crash recovery is recorded separately; direct native peer-VM,\njail, host isolation and fleet admission remain gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6625
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native guest SSH refusal checks distinguish recognized users denied by VM or\nmembership policy from missing identity. Foreign users, Customer members and\nwithdrawn members require fresh Audi `forbidden` control evidence, recognized-key\nguidance and unchanged ingress/guest-login receipts. A generic SSH transport\nfailure does not establish an authorization refusal."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6629
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native manifests and workload bundles bind kernel bytes, digest, source\nrevision, patch/configuration hashes and compiler. Lilly's jail-local probe\ncompares the native OS, placement, execution epoch, boot challenge and digest,\nand requires a canonical boot ID before credentials or readiness. Missing,\nstale, malformed, oversized or mismatched responses refuse. Lyra compares a\nread-only loaded transport build token with a bounded root-owned expected-token\nfile, then separately hashes the configured kernel file. Symlinks, group/world-writable or\nforeign-owned expected files, malformed tokens and module-token mismatch refuse.\nA compiled-input token and a file digest do not substitute for native evidence\nthat the intended kernel/module set booted. The readiness boot ID must equal the\nearlier kernel response's boot ID. A scoped FreeBSD nested-KVM run binds actual\nhost-CID transport to the executing token, checks native ABI refusals, and crosses\nthe credit window with exact synthetic-data comparisons. Wrong-CID injection,\nmalformed DMA, reset, native crash durability and broader isolation evidence\nremain gaps; scoped growth/recovery and IPv4/router/TAP results are recorded\nseparately below. The\n[native kernel attestation review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md)\nrecords these limits."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6633
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native preset's compiled-in output plugin."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6634
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native provider compaction is disabled unless\n`MARSHALL_AGENT_NATIVE_COMPACTION_CAPABILITIES` contains a JSON array of exact\nOpenAI provider/model records. Each record requires `provider`, `model` and a\nlowercase 64-character `evidence_digest`; Marshall validates the shape at\nstartup and rechecks the complete provider/model pair when queuing and claiming\nmaintenance. `MARSHALL_AGENT_NATIVE_COMPACTION_VERIFIED=true` is rejected as a\nglobal switch. The digest is an operator receipt reference and does not replace\nlive provider acceptance evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6638
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native root growth is an automatic no-argument service before identity/network\nbootstrap on every boot. A failed preflight or native command withholds the\nvolatile root-growth receipt, preventing bootstrap even if rcorder continues.\nDo not bypass the receipt or select another disk to repair a refusal. Preserve\nthe disposable disk and compare its mounted root, assembly pool identity,\nphysical capacity and both GPT copies before another experiment. Twelve pure\nchecks and cross-target Clippy passed. Three native FreeBSD QEMU boots passed one\nunchanged root followed by two expansions with retained-data, GPT and foreign-disk\nverification. The exact canonical-roots/SSH FreeBSD image later passed full\nFirecracker service/growth composition over three clean boots and two expansions.\nThe final reviewed blocking-flush image passed that boundary and all five scoped\nservices/growth/policy/daemon-recovery/SIGKILL-recovery variants. The current\nsource-qualified OmniOS service fixture passed two clean boots with the same\ncurrent-boot, trust, flush, workspace, terminal, SSH and executor-fencing\noracles. For illumos, a clean result additionally requires process status zero\nand the bounded serial marker `syncing file systems... done`; the patched VMM\nobserves that marker before exiting. The source-qualified OmniOS growth replay is recorded separately; interrupted\nexpansion remains unexecuted."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6642
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native root mutation is confined to the actual mounted root and pinned GPT\nidentities, after read-only dual-header/CRC/capacity validation. OmniOS additionally\nbinds the assembly dataset/pool GUID and single whole-disk vdev. Growth keeps\nthat vdev's validated `s1` authority identity and raw `p0` GPT preflight separate\nfrom the unsliced operand required by libzfs expansion. The scoped native\noperand diagnostic does not establish corrected-helper or interrupted-growth\nacceptance. Root-only\nno-argument invocation, an exclusive root-owned lock, bounded utility output and\npostflight precede the volatile success receipt required by bootstrap. Pure\nparser tests do not establish filesystem growth or interruption recovery."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6646
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native trust composes the current host roots with the separate pinned vendor\nsnapshot `/etc/overalls/system-ca.pem`, then durably replaces the effective\nbundle at the standard FreeBSD/OmniOS trust path. Reusing that managed path as\nthe next boot's vendor base is refused by the reviewed contract: previous host\nroots must be removable. A real second boot exposed the earlier accumulation;\nthe corrected filesystem regressions are separate from final two-boot service\nacceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6650
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Native trust keeps pinned vendor roots in the separate regular\n`/etc/overalls/system-ca.pem` and composes only those bytes plus the current\nboot-authorized host set. Its managed system destination is never the vendor\nbase on later boots. Missing or conflicting base/staged bytes and stale\nauthority refuse before changing the effective bundle; root replacement/removal\nmust remain idempotent across boots under ADR-0113."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6654
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Natural EOF drops the retired ring backing before returning its reservation, even while a stalled viewer retains the session. Independent queued output remains intact and drains when the peer resumes. Generated local Linux PTY/socket histories require zero backing allocation, exact finite NUL drain counts and final viewer permit release. The [native repair review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-terminald-retired-ring.md) records the pre-fix1MiB retention failure and passing47-test/Clippy and static factory checks. Initial1/8MiB rings remain fixed; this does not establish dynamic growth, aggregate mixed-pressure admission, RSS, authenticated vsock or VM/browser composition."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6662
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "New editor windows default to no startup editor\n(`workbench.startupEditor = none`), and installing an extension does not open its\nwalkthrough automatically (`workbench.welcomePage.walkthroughs.openOnInstall = false`).\nUsers can override both preferences in Settings. These ordinary defaults are\nseparate from the permanently disabled bundled AI policy. Existing saved editors\nfollow upstream session restoration. The new package and a separate fresh-profile\nmanual browser smoke passed; the latter awaited actual workbench restoration and\nobserved no Getting Started panel or startup Welcome/Get Started/Walkthrough tab.\nIt does not establish saved-editor removal, actual extension-install walkthrough\nbehavior or user override execution."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6674
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "New production Repo connections check client disconnection during active SQL\nonce per second and request a 15-second TCP unacknowledged-data limit. They keep\nthe 15-second idle-transaction timeout and TCP keepalives after 15 seconds,\nevery 5 seconds, with three probes. Healthy SQL may run longer than the network\nlimit. A failed network connection can terminate sooner than under the previous\n30-second limit; callers must still resolve uncertain commits through durable\nidempotency. Existing connections keep their startup settings until reconnection."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6682
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Nix derives bounded recorder/exporter accounts and RPC/reader groups from a\nfixed hash of the configured instance name, keeping every Unix name below\nNixOS's 32-character boundary. Units and storage paths retain the readable\ninstance name. Nix assigns the recorder a separate unprivileged user and mode-0700 permanent\nstate. Its mode-2750 RPC directory uses a producer group inherited by socket\nchildren. A separate mode-0750 publication directory and primary reader group\npermit snapshot reading without directory write access. Producers receive only\nthe RPC group; exporters receive only the reader group and collector access.\nThe explicit Rust `--recorder-group-source` mode preserves that publication\ncustody without falling back to application status sockets. Kernel attribution still\ndistinguishes different application roles sharing a UID. Recorder restart does\nnot stop the producer, and producer loss does not grant guest execution authority.\nSource hooks and the source-local `Overalls.RequestAccounting.Producer` exist. The producer uses private\nquality state independently of recorder checkpoints and permanent source lifetime.\nThe pure aggregate model shares arithmetic and snapshot validation only; application\nstorage, concurrency and publication remain inside the configured source unit.\nProducer marker directories are mode 0700 beneath their systemd state directory;\nthe inner real directory also works with DynamicUser's private-storage symlink.\nApplication-owned exporter units no longer exist (ADR-0159); only the static\nrecorder-group exporters publish request accounting. Application telemetry\nhandlers and independent database measurements remain. Static\nexporters receive no application identity or database credentials. Recorder\nrestart leaves its producer running; neither requires the other to remain live.\nThe collector fixes host, source and origin provenance on each restricted\nintake. Native fixture execution does not establish actual application outcomes;\nthe declared application/collector rollout and production activation have\nseparate acceptance records."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6686
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Nix store reclamation is bounded and preserves configured generations. Guest\nstorage cleanup belongs to Lilly. Brady and Enrico caches have separate quotas.\nDo not reclaim a guest dataset with generic cache or Nix garbage-collection tools."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6694
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "NixOS installs the packages and system settings declaratively. Ubuntu copies\ntheir complete pinned runtime closure into its existing development-tools\nenvironment, registers it in the Nix database and retains a GC root; commands\nare exposed at `/usr/local/bin`. This is the scoped offline application exception\nin [ADR-0167](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0167-native-guest-coding-clis.md).\nThe ordinary authenticated Ubuntu package lock remains authoritative."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6698
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "NixOS machine integration tests and property-based tests are the preferred evidence. Unit tests establish narrower behavior. **Present** means a test exists and its assertion was inspected; **recorded** links a historical execution record, not a rerun of the current tree. Partial coverage does not mean the feature is broken. Gaps identify what the evidence cannot establish."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6702
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "NixOS test drivers and separately launched browser helpers have distinct type\nchecks. Teams, Control room, handbook, MFA login, administration, Git mirrors,\njob history, Inception and the fleet's default OSS, resize, account lifecycle,\nteam resources, terminal, maintenance evacuation, agent CLI, private web, clone\nand executor-loss journeys execute copied helper artifacts only after pinned\n`ty` passes against their actual Python/Playwright runtime; the fleet client\nlikewise executes typed Audi and Porsche browser artifacts. The repository's ordinary Python source discovery does not\ninclude machine helpers. Installer trust has no standalone browser script and\nretains composed driver typing. Every composed fleet variant driver passes the\nframework's `ty` check and ruff lint; no variant skips type checking."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6706
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "No Cachix write token is embedded. The evaluation check\n`nix-cache-configuration` covers host, guest and fleet fixture declarations; it\ndoes not establish live reachability, cache hit rate or physical rollout."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6710
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "No additional description is declared by the module."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6711
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "No migration changes guest disks or physical VM state. Publishing an image or\nupdating a host does not convert an existing writable disk. Recreate incompatible\nguests from current images and copy/verify selected data while retaining the old\ndisk unless deletion is separately authorized. No retained-disk conversion or\nfeature deployment has been performed. Refresh the\nOveralls installer/setup on old clients so their managed SSH block discovers the\ngenerated name. The complete development lifecycle journeys on base `63a1443c`\nplus the durable feature precede main integration and are scoped\nin the [durable identity review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-durable-guest-identities.md),\nseparately from deployment and the old\n[email-derived verification](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fresh-guest-identity-verification.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6715
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "No-key administrators are sent to the sign-in section of the account page\n(`/settings#security`) for fresh-email first enrollment, then return to the\noriginal page and explicitly retry the action. Cancel,\nceremony failure, continuation expiry, another\ntab's input, stale resource state or loss of login/role/key authority refuse the\nmutation and keep the page usable for permitted reads. Passkey changes require\nverification of an existing key; Customer guest access still requires its exact\nowner. Terminal, editor, SSH and service authority do not inherit this browser\ncontinuation. Marshall implements the enrolled-key modal, socket-local retry and\nno-key Security return path. Final merged packaged browser checks passed ordinary\naccess, no-key return/explicit retry, continuation/cancellation/focus restoration\nand colocated cross-replica revocation. Native machine-page recovery and timed\nreceipt expiry remain unexecuted. See\n[access](#access), [security](#security) and [scenario coverage](#coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6719
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Non-secret native output settings; routing and queue keys are reserved."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6723
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Nonempty set of providers enabled for discovery and inference; readiness requires all selected catalogs."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6727
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "OTLP hostname, without scheme, path or credentials."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6728
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "OTP supervisor progress reports, two per TLS connection, are dropped at the\nsource. Crash and supervisor-failure reports remain."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6732
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Observability is an independent deployment boundary under ADR-0149. Control\nreceipts carry readiness and accounting facts required for authority; they carry\nno diagnostic lifecycle outbox, progress stream or resource history. Marshall\npreserves transactional security/business audits and durable service-level totals.\nThe host trace spool, Collector and searchable backends cannot authorize effects,\nrelease reservations or delay local state publication. Grafana dashboards and\ndatasources are provisioned by NixOS. Historical database and private journal\narchives retain their original evidence scope; they do not prove current health.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6736
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Observe collector/spool failures through Grafana and service logs. Do not erase\nstate journals or physical outcomes to clear a diagnostic backlog.\nThe trace spool confirms delivery only after a bounded, completely framed HTTP\nsuccess contains a valid OTLP response with absent or zero rejected spans. The\nCollector's explicit empty `partial_success` is a valid success. Malformed,\ntruncated or nonzero-rejection replies retain pending data for retry; response\nwarning text stays private. Confirmed delivery clears pending work while retaining\nthe immutable archive until its configured expiry.\nSuccessful delivery advances immediately to the next pending batch. Idle or\nfailed attempts back off for 250 milliseconds; maintenance and numeric health\npublication use a separate cadence during continuous drain. Archive quotas and\nservice resource limits still apply, so production traffic and retention require\nseparate sizing evidence.\nExisting native process, boot, storage and lease fences determine recovery even\nwhile the observability backend is unavailable. Local properties cover this\nindependence. The [focused native recovery fixture](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/observability-recovery.py)\nconfigures the production collector and trace spool, stops them on the worker,\nreopens Lilly without replacing native VMMs, settles a fresh stop/start readiness\nreceipt, and recovers retained diagnostic custody. Its companion\n[submission recovery histories](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/submission-recovery.py)\nkeep the before/after native launch barrier and exact-generation outcome oracle.\nThe final typed packaged recovery capture passed in 707.93 seconds on its\npre-Starship/pre-profile runtime. Its observer-outage subtest passed in 113.51\nseconds, including the original 180-second drain bound\nand an exact fresh native execution/revision, host, placement and running-transition\nquery through real Tempo. Both-host and generated before/after native-submission\ndaemon-loss histories also pass. These disposable-machine results establish that\nscoped recovery journey. Earlier captures remain in the [verification ledger](#coverage);\nmerged guest execution, retained-state upgrade, physical host power loss,\nproduction archive sizing and rollout remain separate acceptance work."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6740
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Official parent/trace-ID ratio for routine spans; committed lifecycle diagnostics always sample and SLO accounting is independent."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6744
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "OmniOS assembly applies a stock cloud-init/SSH disabling profile to only the\ncloned root's offline SMF repository. The exact profile passed native validation\nagainst a scratch stock database, with five false enabled properties and no\nlive repository mutation. The previous full-kit fresh-boot verifier correctly\nrefused cloud-init's resolver changes; retain this failure. A newly assembled\nimage must verify both disabled service state and exact immutable payload before\nFirecracker service acceptance. Scoped FreeBSD native IPv4/router/TAP policy\npassed two clean boots after the native SSH `UseDNS no` fix; complete OmniOS,\ndirect peer-VM, jail, physical-host and multi-host isolation remain pending.\nThe seed-fixed image passed those checks and diagnostic Firecracker transport\nafter a debugger-only stock pseudo ISA setting restored late serial output.\nPersistent assembly now preserves `/etc/system` and `/boot/loader.conf.local`,\nappends reviewed pseudo ISA and loader/kernel serial settings, and binds both\ncomplete files/modes for second-boot verification. It removes only an inherited\nstandalone `-s` from `/boot/transient.conf`, preserving the ZFS root, boot path\nand console arguments; second boot rejects any remaining single-user token. The\nfirst formal normal boot\nreached ordinary login with persistent serial but\nstock physical networking entered maintenance and withheld the required\nbootstrap dependency because the remaining plumb-only stock vioif0 file conflicted\nwith interface initialization. All three Overalls manifests also failed import\non the invalid `Uncommitted` stability enum. Assembly now removes only the four\nfixed stock vioif0 address/DHCP files, preserves unrelated interfaces and requires\ncontinued absence in boot verification. The corrected `Unstable` manifests pass\nactual native `svccfg validate`; a deliberate old-enum mutant is rejected.\nThe same native check now gates assembly and booted verification before receipts.\nThis establishes schema validity, not imported methods or startup ordering.\nDecoded native FMD records show ZFS EIO before the later unsupported VMM resets;\nthe disk-I/O cause remains under investigation. No service receipt exists\nfor that attempt. Replay the corrected exact image; debugger changes and\ndiagnostic success cannot replace that evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6748
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "OmniOS runtime image verification permits the effective CA file to become only\nthe designated root-owned managed link, with a regular mode0644 target containing\nthe exact immutable vendor prefix and one to 32 bounded public PEM roots. Static\npayload hashes/modes and the regular vendor snapshot remain exact. The final 21\nhelper boundary tests include foreign/traversal links, writable or nested-link\ntargets, vendor substitution, unrelated payload changes and malformed/oversized\nroots. This structural verification grants no current-boot trust authority;\nthe trust protocol receipt must still match the current boot.\nThe assembler also removes an inherited standalone `-s` from the cloned\n`/boot/transient.conf` while preserving its ZFS root, boot path and console\narguments; second-boot verification rejects any remaining single-user token.\nThis fixes loader selection only. The current source-qualified OmniOS image\nlater passed two complete native service boots; the runner required status zero\nand the bounded `syncing file systems... done` serial marker before recording\nclean shutdown. The later exact disk `45983bb7` separately passed policy and\nsupervised daemon recovery; physical isolation remains open. The separate OmniOS\nabrupt-crash receipt covers process SIGKILL and same-disk recovery; physical stable-media and host recovery\nremain unverified."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6752
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "OmniOS vendor cloud-init and SSH are disabled in the clone's offline SMF\nrepository so runtime network/SSH authority remains with Overalls. Exact-profile\nvalidation on a scratch stock repository passed without changing the live\nrepository. Fresh-boot verification must observe those five instances disabled\nand every immutable payload unchanged; it continues to refuse resolver changes.\nFresh seed-image assembly and QEMU boot passed those file/service checks after\nbinding the offline repository environment and importing the exact clone\nmanifests. Diagnostic Firecracker AF40/file/token verification subsequently\npassed under a debugger-only pseudo ISA override. Final persistent-image service\nand storage replay remains required. Assembly now removes only the fixed four\nstock vioif0 address/DHCP files, preflights every destination and refuses any\nrestoration during verification. All three corrected manifests pass native\n`svccfg validate`, while the old-enum mutant refuses; the same native validator\nnow gates assembly and verification. These checks preserve MMDS-only network\nauthority and establish schema validity, not actual service method execution.\nNo profile validation or installation receipt enables native admission."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6756
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "On a failed journey the browser helper emits closed document-status categories\nand bootstrap/error/connection booleans, without URLs, cookies, messages or page\ncontents. The native fleet may additionally inspect its authenticated current\nboot and fixed worker-health/refusal booleans within one 30-second console bound.\nThese read-only probes do not start an editor, retry browser assertions or turn\nfailure into acceptance. Their presence is not a recorded diagnostic execution\nor an explanation of the Ubuntu failure."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6760
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "On a supported repository page, clicking an unconfigured toolbar button opens\nsettings. Unsupported hosts show an **Unsupported page** state and do not send a\nURL. Marshall checks the launch request again before staging it and may require\nyou to sign in."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6764
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "On base `63a1443c` plus the durable feature before main integration, the\ndurable-identity application gate and focused editor checks passed\nemail continuity through approval, exchange, credential reuse and renewal. The\nNixOS native run completed canonical personal editor/terminal, policy,\nbroker restart and worker recovery, then failed an edit assertion after physical\nstop/start. Ubuntu failed guest startup before personal editor login. Earlier\neditor package/family snapshots do not establish this feature or explain these\nfailures. The later incoming `d4499c4c` merged Marshall gate passed 1,429 checks,\nincluding application editor authority, with zero-error forced Dialyzer. That\ngate and both merged lifecycle passes do not establish native editor acceptance\nor later browser-launcher/shared-observability integration. Complete\ncurrent editor recovery and native email continuity remain open in the\n[durable identity review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-durable-guest-identities.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6768
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "On base `63a1443c` plus the durable feature before main integration, the complete\nNixOS SSH journey passed canonical account/home checks,\nsame-User email continuity, relocation, reboot and cloning. Ubuntu passed the\nemail-continuity subtest before a later agent-authentication failure. Complete\nUbuntu SSH and editor recovery remain gaps.\nBoth complete retirement journeys passed shared storage/process retention,\nold-home reservation and explicit fresh re-sharing. Separate integration with\nincoming `d4499c4c` passed Protocol/Lilly/Marshall gates and both eight-subtest\nlifecycles (NixOS 438.33 seconds, Ubuntu 574.18 seconds). Those captures do not\nestablish later browser-launcher/shared-observability source; see the scoped\n[execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-durable-guest-identities.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6772
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "On failure the driver disarms recording, synchronizes publication and copies rings\nto private directories outside the Nix output before teardown. Failed-build retention\nand private extraction are required to preserve them; successful runs discard rings.\nThe disposable executable checks cover exclusion, byte/status/signal preservation,\nbounds and persistence failure. They do not establish native accounting behavior,\nphysical isolation or cancellation acceptance. Existing readiness, ownership,\ncapacity and pool-lock authority remain mandatory."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6776
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Onboard provider accounts on each selected host. Use `systemctl status underclass\nunderclass-tailscale-serve`, `tailscale serve status`, and local `utop` for diagnosis.\nThe local monitor socket exposes bounded metadata without granting account controls.\nWhen fleet telemetry is enabled, a separate Rust probe reads this socket every\n15 seconds and exports a fixed 0/1 local monitor readiness gauge. It has no\nproxy or administrative credential. The private Grafana candidate requires\nfresh, complete observations from both enrolled hosts; it does not measure\ntailnet access, authorized proxy completion or provider success.\nThe separate proxy candidate admits only authorized parsed inference objects with\na nonempty model. A private SQLite journal commits admission before provider\neffects and commits one terminal aggregate when the response body finishes.\nThat journal, `slo-totals.sqlite`, holds one totals record whose single duration\nhistogram has fifteen finite bounds through twenty-four hours; the retired\nseven-bound `slo.sqlite` is never read.\nSSE success requires a dispatched completion marker and clean EOF; missing,\nmalformed or error frames and dropped bodies are failures. Restart turns pending\nadmissions into failures with unknown duration without repeating provider work.\nJournal uncertainty fences admission and publication. Saturated accounting\nrecords the eligible refusal as a failure and refuses provider effects.\nThe numeric snapshot lives in `/run/underclass/slo`, mode 0640 under a mode-0750\nsource directory. An independent Rust exporter UID has only the source group\nand its separate collector group. It cannot read provider state or credentials.\nThe monitor role and its public local socket retain their existing boundary.\nNative startup, provider TLS and exporter custody passed an isolated fixture; production\nactivation, power-loss recovery, throughput and complete seven-day history remain\nopen. This candidate does not establish guest or tailnet availability.\nThe pool database contains OAuth credentials and needs encrypted recovery custody.\nRevision `8c1a38c` retains the existing refresh-token rotation and rotates Codex\nrefresh tokens after 24 hours, checking at startup\nand every 15 minutes. Existing databases gain a rotation timestamp; legacy tokens\nare due on the first pass. Failed scheduled refreshes preserve account health and\ncooldowns. HTTP 401 and 403 receive one refresh/retry per account per request.\nAdministrators can enable `auth_error` accounts, while quota cooldowns remain\nintact. This pin update has source review only; native migration, provider recovery\nand rotation behavior were not tested. Older backups can contain invalidated tokens.\nRevision `d0cb274` added manual redemption of one banked Codex reset credit through\n`POST /admin/api/accounts/{id}/reset`, the admin page **Use reset** button and the\n`underclass reset` command. The route sits behind the admin token; the command\nreuses `utop` token resolution and with `--url` requires `UNDERCLASS_UI_TOKEN`.\nWithout `force` the proxy refuses (409) when upstream says the account is allowed or\na redeemed reset has not restored usage; no credit and non-Codex accounts are never\noverridable. The default catalog adds `gpt-6-sol`; usage accounting classifies\n`\"stream\": true` bodies as streaming. Revision `8c1a38c` also records bounded\nstream outcomes and sanitized error codes, retains daily statistics rollups for\n730 days, and serves administrator-only `/admin/api/stats` and event-import\nroutes. The `underclass stats` command uses the same token boundary. These\nstatistics contain no prompts, cache keys or credentials. Source review and an\noffline build only; tests were not run for this pin.\nRevision `469aff4` always reselects after the saturation reset attempt, so a\nthrottle cooldown that expires while a request waits on the reset lock no longer\nyields a stale 429; requests skip that lock while a Codex account is healthy.\n`request.saturated` logs a relative `retry_after_ms` and an absolute `until_ms`.\nUpstream Rust tests passed; no dedicated regression test covers the race.\nProvider egress can be pinned to a tailnet exit node (ADR-0185).\n`underclass-egress.service` runs a separate unprivileged userspace `tailscaled`\nwith its own state and socket, no TUN device and no routes. Its HTTP proxy\nlistens only on `127.0.0.1:1055`. The enrolled profile sets\n`services.underclass.egress.exitNode = \"mac-mini\"`. Each host's node starts\nlogged out, and an operator joins it once with `sudo underclass-egress up`.\nThe exit-node setting gives Underclass `HTTPS_PROXY`, confines\nthe unit to loopback through systemd IP filtering, and adds a privileged start\ngate. The gate selects the exit node with LAN access disabled and refuses to\nstart while the node is logged out. Losing the exit node fails provider\nrequests instead of falling back to the host's address. Underclass still\nrestarts while the exit node is offline, and resolves provider DNS at the exit\nnode. The `underclass-egress` machine check verifies these properties on a\nheadscale tailnet. Live login of both nodes and a request observed from the\nMac Mini remain open; root can clear the preference until the next start.\nSee [Underclass operations](repo:docs/services/underclass.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6780
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "One Marshall instance authorized to issue the public Audi wildcard."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6784
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "One reported failed production thread recovered through its authorized retry and\nremained ready after required-key deployment, with the same running VM and one\ncompleted initial objective turn. The final inspection was read-only and submitted\nno further prompt. This observation establishes that recovery and continuity;\nnative archive/reopen, fault recovery and cross-device acceptance remain separate\nfrom the focused tests and synthetic browser observations recorded in the\n[thread review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-15-user-threads.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6788
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only Overalls Marshall receives the dedicated SSH CA private key through an\nencrypted runtime bundle and systemd credential. Porsche, both Audi gateways\nand guests hold separate leaf keys and public certificates. Guests generate\nleaf keys under `/run` on each boot. New SSH readiness depends on issuance;\nexisting valid certificates permit renewal retries during a control-plane outage.\nThis signer is independent of physical administrative SSH host keys and TLS CAs.\nInception instances create an independent CA beside their own persistent identities."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6792
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only complete anonymous GET responses with explicit public freshness are cached.\nCredentials, cookies, query-bearing URLs, private/no-store responses, and unsupported\nvariation bypass storage. Cache failure can stream through the proxy; proxy failure\nmust not open a direct-web bypass. QUIC is not a bypass path. The cache lives in a\nseparate bounded ZFS dataset outside the managed guest parent."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6796
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only current thread managers install, update, enable, disable or remove managed\nskills; operators may invoke enabled skills. Installation accepts public\nGitHub, GitLab, Codeberg and Bitbucket repositories, an optional revision and a\nskill subdirectory. The guest resolves a full commit and records its content\ndigest. It performs bounded credential-free fetching with validated paths and\nwithout hooks, filters, submodules or install scripts. Immutable revisions live\noutside repository discovery paths. A failed update keeps the active version;\nlocally edited files are preserved. Ambiguous results are reconciled through the\noriginal operation's status rather than blindly executing again. Reopen restores\nthe pinned commit/digest, and admitted turns retain their selected revision.\nManaged removal leaves repository and personal files intact."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6800
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only the disposable clone-cancellation Marshall release contains the report-guard\ninstrumenter and private sink. Build-time hashes pin both the authenticated caller\nand guarded source; production releases remain unchanged. Original conditions,\nshort circuits, one evaluation per predicate, database time, rollback and public\nrefusal results remain intact. The sink records only one of eleven fixed stages\nand signed sample age; malformed shape has null age. No report body, host identity,\ncredential, raw state or committed-outcome event leaves the guard."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6804
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only the disposable clone-cancellation fixture can interpose the ZFS observation\nrecorder. Its literal argv allowlist contains the public properties used by Lilly's\nwhole-pool observer and the fixed `zroot/lilly` root. Ownership properties, receive\ntokens, other arguments and all mutation commands execute directly without capture.\nIt retains at most 128 completed samples per host, each with at most 64 KiB from\neach stream, explicit byte counts and truncation flags. Files are private beneath\na mode-0700 root, with one bounded staging file during atomic replacement. Native\noutput and status reach Lilly unchanged; no sample enters application events."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6808
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Open Settings → Resize as the current owner or manager (the Settings page shows\nthe current resources to everyone with machine access). CPU and memory may\nincrease or decrease; disk may only grow up to 500 GiB. Draft URLs retain their\noriginal generation and request identity across polling and reload. A stale draft\nrequires an explicit review of current state; that review retains its size inputs\nbut does not itself request work. Exact authorized replays return the original\nrequest. Manager revocation also blocks previously accepted request replays.\nThe page shows the confirmed resources, the form's current → requested sizes and\nthe stages the request will pass through (stop, apply, restart or remain stopped,\nconfirm). While a request is active the form is replaced by a stage ladder marking\nthe recorded phase (a fencing phase displays as restarting), the original → target\nsizes, and, when the request needs attention, a retry control that resumes from\nthe recorded phase. The ladder never marks a stage done ahead of the record."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6812
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Open `https://ghuntley.dev/launch/entry#https://github.com/OWNER/REPO`, or the\ncorresponding public GitLab, Codeberg or Bitbucket URL, to create an OSS machine\nafter complete sign-in. The root fragment form still reaches this capture page.\nThe browser launcher uses the same path. Ordinary sign-in and a magic link opened\nin another tab resume through the shared signed session cookie; passkeys do not\ngate ordinary provisioning. `overalls open\nURL [-- COMMAND]` uses Porsche `new --source URL`, then SSH into the checkout.\nOnly the guest contacts providers and runs git; Marshall and Lilly carry a closed\nsource2 identity ([ADR-0157](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0157-multi-provider-authenticated-repository-launch.md))."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6816
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Open a GitHub, GitLab, Codeberg or Bitbucket Cloud repository in Overalls with a\nsingle toolbar click. The extension carries only the provider origin and path to\nOveralls, so you can move from a repository page to a machine without copying a\nURL by hand."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6820
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Open backend TLS ports; unnecessary for a colocated proxy."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6821
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Open ports in the firewall for the Audiobookshelf web interface."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6825
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Open the public HTTPS port."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6826
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Opening a magic link in a JavaScript-enabled browser submits the token through\nthe CSRF-protected sign-in POST without another click and remembers the browser.\nThe initial GET does not consume the link. A browser without JavaScript can use\nthe fallback button. A successful sign-in returns to the requested destination\nor Overview. Pending first-key setup does not block ordinary reads; the account\npage's sign-in section is opened by an explicit credential action or by the\nprivileged step-up setup flow.\nInvalid, expired and replayed links leave no login or remembered credential.\nJavaScript-capable automated link visitors may consume a valid single-use link;\nGET-only scanners cannot. The updated three-replica native MFA browser journey\npassed automatic navigation and remembered-cookie checks in one NixOS VM; see\nthe [automatic sign-in review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-02-automatic-magic-link.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6830
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Operation cancellation does not erase a physical effect. A late outcome still\nrequires reconciliation against the current identity and generation. The\n[generated lifecycle history](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/lifecycle_history_test.exs)\nchecks one to four delayed physical receipts after confirmed archival. Their\nimmutable rows append while VM state and released reservations stay fixed; a\nchanged replay is refused. This uses synthetic outcomes in local PostgreSQL,\nnot native guest or cross-host evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6834
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Operational Login/Credential/Lease/asset-receipt cleanup uses bounded seven-day\nexpiry batches, retaining credentials still referenced by leases. Audit versions\nfollow the separate ninety-day inventory. Neither pruning nor process restart\ngrants identity or cleanup authority over another account. Old guest disks retain\ntheir immutable package capability; recreate from a matching image to acquire a\nnew release. Standalone native and full NixOS Marshall/Audi/Lilly/Firecracker\nbroker restart/worker loss passed with saved data. Actual NixOS stop/start preserved\nplacement/epoch, advanced logical generation, rotated challenge and guest boot UUID,\nand required exact current-generation physical running/Provisioning readiness.\nThat record precedes the observability cutover. The merged driver requires the\ncurrent-generation authenticated physical start outcome's `guest_ready: true`;\nthe guest helper still proves its confined boot and host-local Provisioning journal.\nNo lifecycle diagnostic delivery is required for current readiness.\nUbuntu failed before these recovery assertions; physical faults and recurring\nprobe histories remain gaps in [scenario coverage](#coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6838
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Operator RSA public key (at least 3072 bits). Keep its private key off-host."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6842
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Operator selected ACME directory."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6843
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Operator-owned JSON public Inception issuer, consent, DNS and trust settings, delivered through systemd credentials. Contains no parent credentials. Null leaves public bootstrap disabled."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6847
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Optional Compose overlays declare separate origin/SMTP fixtures, satellite\nroles, a guest VMM, a measured Lilly/ZFS TCG host and a recorder host. Closed\noperator requests and witness paths are source-defined; the workload has\nauthored browser, Control peer, admission, terminal and recovery callsites.\nTheir presence does not establish that selected images, migration, credentials,\nhealth, independent oracles and one setup owner ran together. The local guest\nand router TCG records each have their own artifact identity and never count as\nthe default control graph's hosted baseline."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6851
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Optional IPv4 recursive DNS resolver or hostname including its port."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6855
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Optional ZFS dataset mounted at /var/lib/tempo with a hard refquota."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6859
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Optional ZFS dataset mounted at the store state directory with a hard refquota. Uses a static service user (DynamicUser bind-mounts conflict with pre-mounted datasets)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6863
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Optional burn delivery places Alertmanager on the central telemetry host through\n`services.overallsOtelFleet.burnAlerts.enable`. Prometheus sends over loopback and\nAlertmanager sends to an approved HTTPS webhook using service-local runtime\ncredentials. No listener is public and clustering is disabled. The deployed hosts\ncurrently have this capability disabled; central-host failure also interrupts\nnotifications. The placement projection includes Alertmanager when enabled."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6867
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Optional central-host Alertmanager delivery requires an explicitly approved\nruntime HTTPS destination. Systemd owns URL and bearer credential loading; private\nsource files stay outside the Nix store and unprivileged readers must be refused.\nRouting requires the reviewed burn name, objective, window, provisional status\nand warning severity together. Foreign or mismatched labels select an empty\nreceiver. Transport verifies system TLS trust, refuses HTTP startup and disables\nredirects. Loopback-only HTTP is the local Prometheus-to-Alertmanager boundary;\nno cluster listener or public firewall port is opened."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6871
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Optional measured-host enrollment uses a private request and the reviewed\nMarshall CLI, binds the issued host/pool identity to the inner ZFS measurement,\nand leaves an ambiguous reissue uncertain. Its TCG-specific Lilly ownership\nretains root, machine-ID, reserved-UID, global lock and durable host/pool fences\nwhile omitting the native KVM probe. This is source-reviewed only: no composed\nControl/guest acceptance follows. The separate router smoke uses a boot-private\nrelease cookie and local ZFS/Brady effects; its loose fixture source filtering\nand synthetic peers do not prove production packet attribution.\nThe private host/guest variant retains no signing key for its public bootstrap\nCA; real private roots require same-boot GuestTrust delivery and an exact\ndurable receipt before private channels can become ready. This is source and\nfocused adapter-test evidence only. The current measured host sample is\ndisconnected and execution-unready, with no admitted guest, terminal accounts\nor QEMU crash recovery result.\nPhysical host readiness is measured before private role credentials are issued;\nprivate Ziggy/Audi readiness is checked immediately before a new guest\nlaunch/restart effect. Missing private readiness refuses that effect. Only an\nexact matching boot with positive current process proof may be re-observed\nwithout reopening the private readiness gate. This source-reviewed ordering\ndoes not establish a connected private host or a running guest.\nThe non-serving fixture operator retains the Endpoint only with `server: false`\nfor WebAuthn origin/RP identity and opened no listener in the recorded diagnostic.\nIt established three synthetic account/passkey pairs through reviewed Ash\nactions; a durable bootstrap marker refuses ambiguous reissue. These credentials\nremain private to the fixture and grant no live deployment authority. The\ncontrolled collector reads only its own validated unified cgroup subtree and\nancestors; an unavailable or ambiguous observation withholds the entire report.\nThe earlier connected host session with zero report sequence could not establish\nsuccessful setup. A later project committed a fresh report and emitted setup,\nbut its nil pool capacity and false execution readiness still refuse guest\nadmission. The committed effective CPU/memory fields were collector-derived;\nraw cgroup file values were not independently compared."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6875
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Optional operator-owned runtime default image identity, delivered through systemd credentials. Overrides defaultImageId; empty input disables the default and invalid input prevents startup."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6879
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Optional operator-owned runtime public hostname, delivered through systemd credentials. Overrides publicHost; invalid or missing input prevents startup."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6883
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Optional origin/SMTP, satellite, Enrico, guest/inner-host and recorder overlays\nhave separate private state and source-defined health probes. Select only the\nfixtures whose source-built images and matching workload/setup probes are ready;\nthe default bootstrap does not establish these extra services. The authored\nControl loopback peer checks pending-window frames and retired replies through\nthe real shared client, but has no hosted execution record. A peer receipt is\ntransport evidence, not a Marshall domain effect.\nThe optional inner host has a [recorded local TCG boot](repo:antithesis/verification/integrated-host-boot.json)\nwith measured ZFS/cgroup health on its third exact image and a fourth built\nprivate-service image. The fourth boot also completed runtime PKI preparation\nand a workspace-source-v2 guest image witness. Its host credential, pool ID\nand CA were issued, but Lilly rejected runtime configuration before Control;\nthe stopped-root journal recorded two invalid-configuration errors. It remained\ndisconnected and execution-unready. The first two health attempts failed and\nwere stopped. This record does not include an authenticated Control report,\nnested guest readiness or crash\nrecovery. Inner Audi/Ziggy/Galileo role configuration still awaits runtime\ncredentials; do not treat the built image or working 9p witness as service\nreadiness.\nThe private Docker variant is selected by adding\n`compose.inner-private.yaml` after the host-vmm overlay and staging the\n`private-host-vmm` context. Its Compose file renders, but no container startup\nor inner private-service readiness has been recorded."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6887
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Optional private CA bundle for terminal peer TLS; system roots otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6891
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Optional private runtime bearer credential for the approved webhook."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6895
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Optional verified HTTPS Route 53 endpoint for isolated fixtures or compatible services."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6899
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Ordinary documents need authenticated host recipients and recovery users.\nRecovery-only documents explicitly have no runtime host recipients. Nix contains\nciphertext and public keys; SecretSpec/SOPS materializes runtime files. Use string\npaths for private inputs, not Nix path literals that copy content into the store.\nAfter recipient changes, rekey affected documents and verify independent recovery.\nEvery inventoried document receives all recovery-enabled users and only its\nselected hosts; login alone grants no recovery access. Host and user key lists\npermit overlap during rotation. Reconciliation requires a retained recovery\nidentity and replaces the data key whenever the recipient set changes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6903
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Ordinary web and SSH stream grants last at most thirty seconds from control\nrequest start and renew with Marshall. Nested Inception grants remain bounded\nby five seconds and the parent environment publication's remaining lifetime.\nAudi accepts the generic thirty-second lease envelope; Marshall's nested\nissuer and nested response each apply the shorter bound.\n- **Definite refusal:** a denial or a changed binding revokes the stream at once.\n- **Inconclusive failure:** a transport error, a non-2xx response or a grant\n  that arrived after its own deadline keeps the current lease and retries. The\n  stream's guard still ends it at the deadline, so revocation latency is\n  unchanged.\n- **Push revocation:** Marshall-pushed revocation with a longer backstop remains\n  future work."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6907
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Other HTTP-01 issuers for the same hostname on a trusted private network. Configure every frontend with every other issuer."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6911
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Overalls admits TCP 80 on the proxy address from any source (ADR-0181) so the\npublic CA can validate `ghuntley.dev`. The listener answers only challenge\nlookups for that host and permanent HTTPS redirects; other hosts and paths get\nno Marshall route, and it holds no certificate key. HTTPS on 443 and all other\nproxy, Porsche and administrative listeners stay limited to reviewed sources,\nthe tailnet or the fleet tunnel. Expected refusal: a request for any other\n`Host` gets 421, and a non-GET challenge request gets 405. Evaluation cases in\n`public-grafana-configuration` assert the opt-in rule and built successfully;\nlive issuance and HAProxy start were observed on 2026-10-16. No machine test\nexercises public port 80 yet."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6915
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Overalls alone publishes shared-database creation-to-ready, physical lifecycle\nand operation-linked SSH completion totals. `marshallReadySloExporter`,\n`lillyPhysicalSloExporter` and `porschePhysicalSloExporter` are separate Rust\nexporter identities. Each reads one fixed numeric mode-0640 snapshot from the\nMarshall source group and can send only through its dedicated collector intake\ngroup. The publisher and database retain measurement authority; snapshots can be\nreconstructed after process restart. Exporters cannot write source files and\nreceive no database, host or provider credentials. Dungarees does not duplicate\nthese shared totals. Declared placement is distinct from recorded live activation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6919
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Overalls builds NixOS and Ubuntu guest images with Nix. Each immutable manifest\nbinds the kernel, initrd, drives, architecture, and minimum resources. Register the\nmanifest in Marshall and install matching artifacts on Lilly before admission.\nRebuilding an image changes future provisioning; existing writable disks remain.\nThe browser creation form and Porsche SSH `new` command select OSS when the\nprofile is omitted. Users may select Customer explicitly for its restricted\nnetwork and agent policy. Existing machines keep their persisted profile.\nCustomer owner lifecycle controls, their entry-specific refusals and receipt\npinning are verified through generated histories and a native journey; see\n[Machine lifecycle](#lifecycle) and [scenario coverage](#coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6923
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Overalls declares separate `vscode_browser_nixos` and `vscode_browser_ubuntu`\nsources. The shared typed Playwright helper uses private real operator storage\nstate, opens the VM from Marshall, checks its expected personal origin, edits and\nsaves a fixture Markdown file, closes/reopens it for readback, inspects its isolated\npreview and verifies terminal UID/name plus guest OS. It does not mint a synthetic\nbrowser success or bypass authentication. Before using preview/terminal features,\nit opens upstream's workspace-trust UI, grants trust to the dedicated reviewed\nprobe workspace and waits for the actual trusted state. Command execution waits\nfor the matching palette row instead of assuming contributions are already loaded.\nTerminal creation selects the exact command with bounded pre-submit preparation,\nchecks that its captured input remains connected, visible and focused, and submits\nonce. One twenty-five-second wait allows initial terminal profile availability.\nOutput and cleanup remain scoped to the captured terminal, preserving other\nvisible editor-group terminals. Inspection enables accessibility only when that\nterminal's tree is absent. The standalone cold first-use and two-preexisting-\nterminal regressions passed; actions use an eight-second default while ordinary\n`expect` assertions retain five seconds.\nEach probe runs every five minutes;\nits Rust supervisor enforces a sixty-second browser deadline and\nsuppresses private browser output. A dedicated Linux subreaper adopts detached\nChromium descendants, selects targets from kernel-owned child lists and kills\nand reaps them before successful settlement. The native subprocess regression\npassed with separate middle and leaf process groups; actual NixOS/Firecracker\nrecurring browser and recorder/collector fault histories remain separate evidence.\nDirect native helper execution passed through the complete NixOS fleet. Ubuntu\nreached its expected origin but failed initial workbench visibility; fixed closed\nsubstages/categories now identify visibility/folder/trust without private output.\nNo runtime cause or new native result follows from that diagnostic-only edit."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6927
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Overalls documentation"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6928
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Overalls keeps no compatibility code for older releases, peers or stored formats\n(ADR-0159). A change to anything two hosts exchange or a release reads ships as\nordered pushes: the consumer first tolerates absence, then the producer stops,\nthen the decoder becomes strict or a hand-written migration drops the column or\ntable. Hosts fetch only the branch tip, so each dependent push waits until both\nhosts report `phase=healthy` on a revision descending from the previous push.\nOld-format durable data is exported with a recorded digest, then purged; a backup\ntaken before such a purge is not a supported restore source."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6932
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Overalls provides persistent development machines backed by Firecracker microVMs.\nMarshall owns durable intent and access. Lilly owns physical execution on each\nprovisioner. A machine keeps its identity across stop, start, and relocation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6936
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Overalls runs a separate Rust `telemetryStorageProbe` on IPv4 loopback port9465.\nPrometheus scrapes fixed aggregate telemetry-store sizes and root free space.\nThe root probe receives read-only mounts for Prometheus and Tempo inside an\notherwise empty state/runtime/configuration namespace; it has no provider keys\nor application authority. Its memory/CPU/task limits and independent unit keep\ncapacity collection separate from producers, recorders and admission. Missing\nprobe metrics raise a capacity-diagnostics alert rather than SLO success."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6940
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Overwriting a full scrollback ring evicts the oldest byte before appending, reusing sufficient backing without capacity growth. The [native Ring review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-terminald-ring-overwrite.md) records the backing-bound failure and passing47-test/Clippy repair with an independent exact newest-byte/base/tail model. Fresh positive ring limits remain fixed in that property. Resize/growth, actual PTY aggregate backing, viewer-stream ordering and VM/hosted composition remain separate."
msgstr ""

