#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6953
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Path to Audiobookshelf config and metadata inside of /var/lib."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6957
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Pause prevents new moves. Accepted moves and their source restoration/cleanup\nretain campaign authority even if the requesting administrator is later demoted.\nContinue and subsequent controls require fresh user authority. Every running\nworkload requires its own placement/epoch downtime approval, because every move\nstops it for the full copy; stopped workloads need none.\nReplanning rotates that workload's revision and clears prior downtime consent.\nOld browser revisions cannot approve or replan the replacement revision."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6961
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Peer's Lego responder port."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6962
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Pending export admission budget per producer, within retained archive budget."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6966
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Per-host queue alarm threshold; align with each writer budget."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6970
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Per-instance TLS health overrides; default uses publicHost and the configured certificate as trust anchor."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6974
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Permissions are checked at execution time. Access shown in a previous list is\nnot a guarantee that a later operation is allowed. Sharing roles are `viewer`,\n`operator` and `manager`; ownership and current permissions determine which\noperations you may perform. SSH key commands affect only your own keys."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6978
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Personal account reconciliation obtains a fresh boot-bound roster. Lilly may wait\nup to one second for definite contention on the placement lock, then verifies the\nsame owned boot and confinement and renews its route and command checks. The guest\nrequest retains its three-second deadline. Exhausted contention or unconfirmed\nauthority denies creation; an existing account never bypasses this proof."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6982
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Personal integration admission requires an explicit source attachment even for\nthe owner. Current owning-team membership remains an independent team path.\nNeither bypasses owner/team liveness, Customer exclusion or execution fences.\nGenerated histories verify refused management leaves mutation audit and durable\nstate unchanged, and actual account retirement/removal withdraw prior admission.\nThe packaged HTTP/1 lease guardian interrupts blocked frontend I/O by closing\nthe native socket while preserving request-owner cleanup. Its isolated upload\nfault test measures EOF/reset and no retries; production timing and broader\nconnect/response fault permutations remain distinct gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6986
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Personal integration ownership grants management authority only. Every source\nVM, including the owner's VM, needs an explicit attachment. Detach removes\nadmission and renewal authority; existing configurations receive no automatic\nattachments or compatibility exemption. Personal-owner retirement and owning-team\narchival refuse access despite retained rows. See [services](#services) for lease\ncancellation and the distinction between current and historical acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6990
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Physical IPv4 destination admitted for WireGuard handshakes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6994
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Physical/workflow sources commit admissions and terminal accounting with business\nstate in PostgreSQL. Original admission clocks, immutable deadlines, canonical\nreceipts and exact execution bindings fence completions. Retry success requires\nboth matching physical-running and committed-readiness evidence inside its\noriginal window. Late readiness can update actual state without rewriting a\nterminal measurement. Timeout settles accounting only; it cannot cancel work,\nrelease reservations or change guest execution."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6998
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Pinned Rust request recorder package."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6999
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Pinned Underclass package."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7000
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Pinned public Ed25519 keys for SSH and optional recovery."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7001
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Pinning requires current Cedar read access, checked under the machine's row lock\nin the same transaction, and refuses a machine with deleted intent (`vm_deleted`),\na machine whose observed state is failed (`machine_failed`) or a 21st pinned\nmachine (`pin_limit`). A pin taken before the machine failed stays, and its holder\ncan still unpin it; the Pin control is hidden on failed machines while Unpin\nremains. Unpinning needs only a live row, so a user\nwhose access ended can still clear the pin; a never-pinned machine refuses with\n`forbidden`. Repeating either request returns the row unchanged and emits no\nevent. A pin grants no authority: it does not appear in the Cedar entity and\ncannot keep a revoked user on the machine."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7005
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Platform boot, networking, identity, terminal, and access paths are protected.\nKeep credentials out of image inputs and the Nix store. Public platform roots are\ndelivered at boot over bound vsock before networking and SSH. Guest accounts and\nterminals use the current per-user account model, including NixOS and Ubuntu."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7009
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Plugin setting names mapped to root-only runtime secret files."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7013
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Poll Marshall for host-bound agent model calls."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7014
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Porsche integration and team lists return an object with `items` and\n`next_cursor`; `team show` returns `members`. Pass a non-null cursor through\n`--after` to continue after the preceding page. Empty pages retain object shape.\n`integration add NAME --peer --peer-vm MACHINE` treats `--peer` as a boolean flag.\nGenerated API/parser checks and the production failure history are recorded in\nthe [integration review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-02-galileo-production.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7018
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Porsche is the SSH machine-management interface. Lyra supplies the local client\nand SSH integration. Management commands call Marshall's authorized domains;\nPorsche does not acquire independent scheduling or ownership authority.\nIts source-owned candidate SSH dispatch SLI counts eligible terminal command\nresults and fixed duration buckets; invalid and forbidden requests stay out\nof the denominator. An accepted asynchronous command measures dispatch only,\nnot physical VM completion.\nAn execution host reconnect clears its capacity freshness until a new native\nreport arrives. A refused restart preserves the explicit `host_unavailable`\nerror and its request ID; callers can retry after readiness returns. Porsche\nnever resubmits a mutation implicitly. Capacity and other closed conflict reasons\nshare the transport's command-exit classification."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7022
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Porsche manages machines; it does not provide a guest shell, guest file transfer,\nport forwarding or an SSH agent forwarding service. Machine console access is\navailable separately in Marshall's web interface, subject to account permissions.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7026
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Porsche reports Customer sharing as `forbidden`; the profile restriction cannot\nbe repaired by retrying a temporary outage. Rejected sharing records no grant,\nchange receipt or SSH request result. Owner Customer start, stop and deletion\nenter only through the browser power controls or Porsche `stop`/`start`/`rm`:\na used request key replays the same operation and a changed kind conflicts\nwithout new durable work. Member, stranger and administrator lifecycle commands\nare refused at both entries and persist nothing; a persisted administrator flag\ndoes not create CLI authority because SSH sessions carry no passkey elevation.\nDeletion receipts remain readable to their issuing owner after archival and a\nname-reused machine never inherits them. The\n[customer controls review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-customer-controls.md)\nrecords the generated profile/actor histories, the browser key-reuse pins, and\nthe native journey where the owner's CLI restart kills and recreates the real\nguest process tree around its retained ZFS identity while the egress fence\nremains closed."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7030
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Porsche status polls (`request show`, listings) are read-only. They validate the\nsession, key and user but do not queue on the account's command lock, so polling\nnever waits behind that account's in-flight mutations (ADR-0140). A transport\nerror, 503, 429 or other non-2xx poll keeps waiting until the deadline. Only a\ndenial, an invalid receipt or the deadline ends a wait."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7034
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Porsche's default Proof callback validates a current, correctly signed,\nsingle-principal host certificate matching its private leaf key before the\nlistener calls the SSH daemon. A new local property records 54 fresh OTP\nfirst-child refusals across 18 real key/certificate mutations. It checks the\nexact listener failure, expected supervisor/listener attempts, no daemon/status/\nobservability starts or surviving service state, preserved private fixture\ncustody and material/path-safe output. Signed invalid type/options/principal\ncases retain valid cryptographic signatures."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7038
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Post-deployment acceptance at `b7e29b8f` also passed the 7,487,562,572-byte\ncheckpoint: NixOS published a miss then reused it, and Ubuntu reused it twice.\nBoth guests matched unchanged independent pre/post SHA-256 references with\ncurrent-owner/generation completions. An earlier concurrent rollout interrupted\na second Ubuntu transfer; that stage remains failed. In-flight connection survival\nacross proxy restart remains outside this acceptance."
msgstr ""

