#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7228
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Readiness checks the local worker fence as well as authenticated control and\nfresh publication. Restoring control alone cannot make a halted worker ready.\nPending socket work may return unproven while the shared client holds a terminal\nversion refusal. Audi now preserves that permanent class for the caller; it\ndoes not report domain completion or resend the request. Ordinary idle-close\nloss remains transient. Actual verified-TLS close histories observe both pending\nidentity/DNS requests before closing and independently check the DNS worker's\nautomatic-work fence, retained snapshot and original five-second expiry.\nThe focused file passed nine checks in56.6seconds before adding idle controls;\nthe refined two-property close file passed33.3seconds. Full migrated Audi precommit\npassed 182 checks (51 properties, 131 tests), with zero-error forced Dialyzer.\nTargeted classifier mutations fail at the early error/work-fence assertions;\nthey do not establish mutation coverage of later expiry assertions. Other consumer\ngates and native gateway acceptance remain open; see the\n[pending-close review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-audi-pending-version-close.md).\nRecorded properties cover verified TLS and actual owner/job death. The packaged\nDNS check at the pre-migration revision proves stopped requests, original\nfive-second expiry, UDP/TCP SERVFAIL and operator restart recovery. It does not\nverify the migrated WebSocket fixture or package. Packaged gateway SSH/Fleet refusal and physical\nmixed-version deployment remain open; see the\n[review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-audi-terminal-version-refusal.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7232
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Ready requires fresh execution-ready host and pool reports, no current workloads,\nno retained holds and no unfinished relocation. Completed jobs or old ready\ntimestamps are insufficient. Restore admission rechecks physical emptiness and\ndoes not move guests back. Retirement additionally revokes host credentials."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7236
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Rebuilt NixOS and Ubuntu images default to Bash with Starship's standard\ninteractive prompt for root and ordinary users, including accounts created after\nboot. NixOS enables its global Starship module. Ubuntu installs Bash and Starship\nfrom its signed snapshot lock, sets the ordinary `useradd` shell default and\nsources one initializer through `/etc/bash.bashrc` and\n`/etc/profile.d/overalls-starship.sh`. Both login and non-login interactive Bash\ninitialize the prompt once per shell; nested Bash gets its own hooks. The native\nNixOS module skips initialization when `TERM=dumb`; normal browser and SSH\nterminals advertise a capable terminal. Ubuntu initializes interactive Bash\nthrough its guarded initializer, including `TERM=dumb`.\nNoninteractive commands retain exact output without prompt initialization noise.\nUsers may configure Starship through `~/.config/starship.toml`; personal dotfiles\nare not rewritten. Service accounts keep their non-login shells."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7240
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Reconnecting later is the same everywhere: `ssh HOST`. (On Windows, if you\ndeclined the administrator prompt, use `overalls ssh HOST` instead.)"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7244
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Reconstruction admits at most 4,096 eligible events before requiring an existing\ncheckpoint. Exceeding that bound returns `context_history_too_large`; it never\nsilently keeps only the latest events. This is an explicit implementation bound,\nnot a retention limit on the transcript."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7248
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Recorded protection evidence pins the current boundary without changing it. In the\nnative restore drill the release boots operator-mode against the isolated restored\ndatabase with no serving listeners and an Oban instance normalized to no queues,\nplugins, staging or peer leadership, so no AshOban trigger or queue consumer runs;\ndecryption succeeds only with the matching restored keyring. Lilly's\nmonotonic-per-placement command receipts, unauthorized and stale-session fencing\nand guest-facing fresh-incarnation refusals retain fixed-test evidence. An\nambient-host inventory assertion was removed because readable empty inventory is\nlegitimate acceptance. The present native unit-inventory fixture uses real\ntracked units and cgroups to inspect acceptance, omitted-placement refusal and\nunknown-cgroup refusal. Its incoming `d4499c4c` merged subtest passed in 8.22\nseconds within the complete native-zfs run that later failed unrelated\nauto-update receipt validation: fixture `enrollment.json` omitted its required\nstring `revision`. No complete native suite pass is claimed. Later incoming\n`bee03919` restores a deterministic child-BEAM unknown-unit/failed-scan utility\nfixture; its incoming focused unit capture is separate from native cgroup\ninventory. Composition of\ninventory refusal into Runtime's host-wide initialization fence remains\nsource-inspection evidence, without a recorded complete native startup-fence\njourney. A code-level historical-authority quarantine\ngate remains a **proposal-only design pending user delegation** (candidate ADR-A\nquarantine gate, ADR-B default-deny re-enablement); see the\n[characterization review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-historical-authority-characterization.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7252
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Recovery membership authorizes every inventoried document; host membership is\nscoped to selected documents. Login-only users and nonselected hosts have no\nrecipient authority. Rekey requires an explicitly supplied retained recovery\nidentity, keeps private conversion files outside the checkout/store and cleans\nthem up after ordinary success or failure. Runtime bundle preparation remains a\nseparate privileged systemd boundary."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7256
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Recurring probes hold real operator browser storage only through private runtime\ncredentials. Their closed fixture must identify a reviewed Markdown probe file\nbecause the journey edits/saves it. The current helper positively checks the\nserver's unconditional trust-disabled bootstrap without trust-storage injection\nor a UI approval action; native extension acceptance separately checks\n`workspace.isTrusted`. Fixture review selects disposable content and confers no\nMarshall authority or direnv approval. Source supervisor, durable recorder, numeric\nreader/exporter and collector intake are separate UIDs/groups. Private browser\noutput is suppressed; no cookie, URL, path, account ID or fixture field becomes a\nmetric label. Lost recorder/collector coverage and missing credentials withhold\nhealth, while an owned sixty-second deadline and Linux subreaper cleanup kill and\nreap browser descendants and forbid late success. Targets come only from owned\nchild groups and kernel child lists. A native detached-leaf subprocess regression\npassed; production credentials and actual NixOS/Firecracker recurring browser\nfailure/revocation and recorder/collector faults require separate acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7260
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Registration accepts bounded ASCII mailboxes on any valid domain. Requests,\ninvitations and verified-token sign-ins validate mailbox syntax independently of\nLinux naming: valid plus aliases, numeric-leading local parts and `root` mailboxes\nare eligible. Malformed domains and header injection refuse; there is no\norganization allowlist. Complete case-insensitive email addresses identify\ndistinct Users, each with a separate reserved guest UUID/UID. All email edits of\nthe same User preserve its guest identity. No profile username, public email-edit\naction or onboarding step is added; the only profile preference is the display\ntime zone of [ADR-0195](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0195-user-time-zones.md),\nset in the profile section of `/settings` through the self-only `set_time_zone`\naction, which\nchanges no identity, guest account or authority (see\n[time zones and local time](#interactive)). Native plus-alias/numeric-leading mailbox\nsign-in and SMTP inbox delivery remain separate gaps in [scenario coverage](#coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7264
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Registration, manual refresh and removal require current administrator authority\nand a recent passkey check. ADR-0160's accepted new browser flow uses a fixed\nfifteen-minute receipt and retains the exact pending catalog action inline while\nan enrolled passkey verifies. No-key administrators visit Security for fresh-email\nfirst enrollment, return, and explicitly resubmit the catalog action. Retry rechecks current\nlogin, role, Cedar, catalog handle and canonical arguments; cancellation, replay,\nexpiry or substituted input creates no catalog intent. Its new continuation\ncatalog-specific native evidence remains pending in [scenario coverage](#coverage).\nMarshall holds the current actor row through the\naudited mutation; demotion, reset, session revocation and retirement cannot pass\nthat row while a catalog write commits. Refresh/removal also serialize on the\nrepository row. An already refreshing or removing mirror refuses manual refresh.\nAn administrator can see mutation controls before elevation; submitting them\nopens passkey verification without creating catalog intent. The historical\nfive-minute redirect tests below do not establish the new inline continuation.\nOrdinary accounts\nretain the read-only repository browser and cannot mutate the catalog."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7268
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Release-independent runtime configuration; null uses the deployed configuration."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7280
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Renewal rechecks current VM-owner membership and explicit attachment to the\ncurrent named integration. It returns only a bounded TTL: an existing upstream\nattempt retains its selected target and credentials and never receives another\npeer token. Generated authority/configuration histories and three independent\nMarshall token consumers have recorded passing application execution in the\n[integration renewal review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-integration-renewal-verification.md).\nThe packaged `integration-renewals` journey passed on captured tree `901d7fd4`\nwith actual team removal and detach after a successful HTTPS renewal. It verifies\nexact current-authority refusal, origin socket closure, unchanged accepted TLS\nconnection counts and fresh success after restoration. The counters run before\nHTTP credential validation. All eight stages passed in 413.94 seconds; the review\npreserves the execution revision and cleanup evidence. These local fixtures do\nnot establish real-provider behavior or independent physical availability."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7284
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Repeated Start of a proven confined running VMM adopts the exact current intent's\ngeneration into the same placement/epoch boot journal without replacing its\nchallenge or restarting the process. Missing, corrupt, foreign and regressing\nboot identities remain refused. Current-generation readiness is still required;\nthe generated metadata histories and native repeated public Start with unchanged\nprocess identity passed. Lilly keeps clone effect results only in memory: after\na Lilly restart Marshall re-offers every effect without a receipt and Lilly\nre-executes it; correctness rests on idempotent effects and durable journals\n(permits, snapshot index, copy journal, received datasets, keys), not on a\npending-result journal. Native clone cancellation accounting, restoration and\ncleanup also passed. The final complete native clone matrix passed in 1539.61\nseconds, including both independent cloned-guest relocations and surviving-copy\nreads after source deletion. Native foreign/corrupt boot refusal and relocation\ndestination retry/cancellation accounting remain open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7288
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Replacement hardware enrolls under a fresh machine identity, a new name and its\nown ZFS pool/dataset GUIDs; a retired host's name is never recycled, and its row\npersists as evidence. Retire the old host first (see Routine operations), then\nprepare the replacement through the protected SSH bridge, deliver only through\nthe sealed bundle and activate with the enrolled binding. The replacement stays\ndisabled until its fresh execution-ready report satisfies the same readiness\ngate as every host. Confirmation that real guest traffic to private services\nruns again before the old credentials disappear from circulation is part of the\nprocedure. The native journey and generated histories are indexed in the\n[host replacement review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-27-host-replacement.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7292
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Replacing an executor invalidates its old lease and retires claimed commands as\ncancelled. A started command becomes uncertain and its turn fails with\n`tool_uncertain`; it is not dispatched again. A never-started cancellation enters\nthe normal model tool-result path. Lease expiry refuses old calls; subsequent\nregistration supplies command retirement and a new fence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7296
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Repository launch capture is public input storage, not a login or provision grant.\nThe configured extension transmits only after an explicit toolbar click. A URL\nwithheld by browser permissions leaves the action available for that click's\nactiveTab grant, then provider validation decides whether to open capture; unknown\nstate alone sends nothing and grants no Overalls identity or machine authority.\nThe extension also requests optional site access only for its explicitly saved\nnormalized Overalls origin. Its packaged detector marks that document with a local\ninstalled attribute; Marshall uses the attribute only to hide setup affordances.\nA marker is spoofable and never grants identity, machine, thread, terminal, editor\nor launch authority. Missing configuration, denied or withdrawn permission, a\nregistration failure or detector outage leaves setup visible.\nThe extension removes source queries/fragments before opening capture. Direct\ncapture removes them before browser storage or the CSRF POST and refuses URL user\ninformation; raw authority/path still undergoes strict backend validation.\n`POST /launch/pending` requires CSRF and stores canonical source, 128-bit visit and\nserver expiry for thirty minutes in the existing signed, encrypted session cookie. A valid\npending launch returns through ordinary sign-in to fixed `/launch`, including\na magic link opened in another tab of the same browser. Expired or malformed input\ncreates nothing. Connected admission uses the current completed stored login and\nordinary provision authority. Its signed completion receipt is cleared only by a\nCSRF HTTP POST with current owner/read authority and matching pending source/visit;\na newer capture survives the old clear. A singleton cookie does not queue concurrent\ntab intents. See [guest workspaces](#guests) and [security boundaries](#security)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7300
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Request sources use an independent durable Rust recorder. It authenticates kernel\npeer UID and exact cgroup, fences completion by producer identity and immutable\ndeadline, and uses boot identity, process start ticks and pidfds for death evidence.\nUnknown kernel evidence remains unknown. Checkpoint writes fsync file and directory\nbefore acknowledgment; lost/corrupt initialized state refuses. Unknown crash\nduration adds no invented latency bucket. Restarting the recorder cannot control\nthe application or a guest."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7304
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required certificate hostname and TLS SNI for traffic and health checks."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7308
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required human-readable owner or purpose for this grant."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7309
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required human-readable owner or purpose for this listener."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7310
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required native ZFS pool and dataset identity."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7311
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required operator settings and private credential/host-key custody are validated\nbefore Porsche starts its supervisor or serving children. Generated local OTP\nhistories pass 171 refusals across 57 cases, including control/public origin,\nlistener bounds, paths, config/credential/key custody and CA defects. Refusals\npreserve recursive fixture bytes, types, permissions, ownership and link counts,\nand diagnostics exclude original/mutated credentials, host-key/CA bytes and\nfixture paths. The unset control starts exactly five live named base children\nwithout listener or status startup. These are test-build checks. Baseline\nsynthetic host-key bytes establish loader custody acceptance only; configured\nSSH/host-certificate startup, packaged refusal, file-replacement races, native\nisolation and hosted config faults remain open for this property."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7315
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required preparation services that publish runtime credentials."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7319
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required preparation services that publish runtime secrets before startup."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7323
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: A bundle with guest_agents none never reports guest_ready: trust is recorded as skipped for the exact boot, provisioning ends in the terminal unattested phase (no boot UUID, no path to ready), and readiness, terminal options, workspace sources and the Inception profile are refused before any host effect. Marshall refuses terminal sessions, agent turns, the agent executor binding, web search and Inception admission for such an image, hides the corresponding controls, and admits only the physical service level. An older Lilly fails closed on a firmware bundle, which is why the converged push precedes any placement. Lilly's host policy drops every unmarked packet between the host and a Customer guest, so nothing on the host reaches the Windows guest except the SSH and editor ingress paths it does not yet have. The guest bootstrap refuses an MMDS document whose fields fail validation or whose MAC is not the adapter's and never logs the token or boot challenge."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7327
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: A foreign Unix peer, malformed binding, unbounded or forged outer metric, wrong route, and customer-profile private connection must be refused."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7331
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: A full spool refuses new provider effects; an incomplete admission cannot be acknowledged as completed usage or replayed as inference after restart. A conflicting completion remains visible as its own class and keeps the disputed receipt."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7335
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: A full64MiB ring reservation budget refuses new sessions without replacing live PTYs; retirement permits only exact replacement capacity."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7339
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: A non-https origin, a foreign management host or zone, or a host outside the zone is refused before any download; a digest mismatch or failed SSH configuration leaves the installed binary and SSH profile unchanged; a client without hostname protection stops setup; an executable path containing a double quote is refused for ProxyCommand."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7343
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: A pending handshake remains unready; only a hello response enables readiness. Stream shutdown closes the opening socket without guest effects."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7347
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: A refused pre-spawn callback must create no child. Running refusal must cancel the separate process group, reap the direct child and discard output; execute must not publish a result under the failed lease. Missing/failed private authority and supervisor stop fail closed without logging command bytes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7351
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: A retired session cannot retain its backing scrollback after returning quota; natural EOF preserves every independently queued output byte."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7355
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: A silent outgoing hop must retire and notify its viewer; the incoming application must release its budget slot after resumption."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7359
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: Actor restart must not launch the completed generation again or replace its recovered outcome identity."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7363
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: Actual HTTP426 upgrade, close4001 or an unsupported-version request error halts automatic work; recovered control, stale ticks and queued publication cannot reopen the worker or extend existing authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7367
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: Actual close4001 must retire both pending operations as unsupported_version and prevent later dispatch; close4008 and prior service unavailability stay transient."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7371
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: All pending callers settle as unproven, further requests remain disconnected, and no replacement upgrade occurs after the former sixty-second retry interval."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7375
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: An expired delayed grant must close the SSH channel without connector calls or guest admission."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7379
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: An unknown agent set string, a workspace source version 2 on an agentless manifest or a ninth manifest key is refused by the protocol; an older Lilly refuses a windows-v1 bundle, so the converged push precedes any placement. A missing, corrupt or mismatched manifest yields every capability false in Marshall. A bare image path or any image key beyond path, including the retired standby key, refuses Lilly's configuration. The probe carries no identity or credential material. The editor and the Inception profile stay refused for windows-v1."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7383
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: Anonymous Grafana queries, reader credentials on insert paths and unprivileged credential reads refuse. Marshall has no diagnostic reader credential or query path."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7387
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: Anonymous browsers redirect to sign-in; unknown viewer events halt; insert credentials are refused on /select/*; reader credentials are refused on /insert/*; unverified CA chains and plain unauthenticated requests fail."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7391
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: Anonymous or revoked readers cannot retain the page. Missing seven-day history, sparse traffic, changed source lifetime, missing host coverage, malformed or duplicate recordings and foreign labels remain Unknown. Missing, duplicate, stale, failed or foreign burn rules cannot display an inactive warning."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7395
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: Any marker mismatch, changed, extra or missing managed root, missing bundle block or link, or failed rebuild takes the full replace path: the marker is withdrawn before mutation and written only after update-ca-certificates verifies. A retired root fails bundle and CApath verification after the next boot."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7399
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: Before-submission loss must fail that generation without launch; after-submission loss must preserve the exact native VMM. Reopens cannot replace original outcome identity or unrelated guests."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7403
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: Candidate spawn failure or unsuccessful registration restores the predecessor; a stale executor cannot retain authority. No semantic rollback is provided after registration."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7407
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: Close a live response after access becomes private; expire authority during a control outage. After gateway credential rotation, refuse the old credential and any conflicting certificate installation while accepting the newer current generation of the same service."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7411
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: Close4001 must refuse every pending caller as unsupported_version, while draining4008 must remain a transient loss without request replay."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7415
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: Competing growth and creates cannot exceed the shared budget or replace survivors; retirement permits only exact growth and replacement capacity."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7419
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: Corrupt or non-v2 primary state fails closed without rewriting, and diagnostic I/O cannot occur under the native writer lock."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7423
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Required refusal: Dangerous client defaults remove prompts and client-level command sandboxing but cannot manufacture identity, revive stale execution, bypass Customer private-inference refusal or enable a disabled provider. Wrong CA trust or hostname must fail rather than disable TLS verification."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7427
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
