#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8130
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Run `mix precommit` in the independent `elixir/diagnostics/` project when reviewed\nevent catalogs, runtime instrumentation or the SDK change. Its read-only\n`mix schema.check` compares production literals with the generated finite trace\nvocabulary without starting services or rewriting files. Review vocabulary\nchanges before regeneration; a synchronized artifact alone does not establish\ndelivery to the native spool or Tempo.\nSchema generation orders object keys explicitly. A fresh-VM regression verifies\nthat opposing atom-loading orders produce the same reviewed artifact, so the\ngate can distinguish source drift from serialization order."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8134
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Run component gates before publication. Release builds use locked dependencies and\nan explicit source allowlist. Stage private secrets, verify schema and credential\ncompatibility, run serialized compatible migrations, then switch and verify health.\nServing application startup does not run migrations. Independent automatic updates\nperform their own pre-switch migration and health sequence. Enrolled hosts poll\nthe `trunk` branch of `ssh://git@github.com/ghuntley/overalls` with the shared\ndeploy key and the pinned GitHub host key from their declaration."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8138
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Run operator commands with the release's protected environment and\n`PHX_SERVER=false`. Use `eval` in a separate process, not `rpc` against a serving\nnode. The operator starts persistence and authority services without consuming jobs."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8142
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Run the [Porsche-to-SSH benchmark](repo:scripts/provisioning_benchmark.py) only\nagainst the exact baseline or enabled release whose per-host update status has\nconverged. Supply already verified management, control and guest SSH identities\nand known-hosts files; the script does not install trust or read a secret bundle.\nIt creates a new private evidence directory, fsyncs all creation/deletion IDs\nbefore effects, and never substitutes another mutation ID after an uncertain\nreply. Reconcile an unresolved attempt by its original receipt before another\ncampaign. Ten sequential samples per NixOS/Ubuntu image and four concurrent\nsamples follow separately recorded prewarm attempts. Guest SSH `ls` must succeed\nagainst the returned `ssh_host`; read-only physical state and independent catalogued logs record\nhost, pool, timing and cleanup without storing terminal bytes or command output."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8146
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Run the corresponding application gates for changed consumers and the protocol\nlibrary. Shared governance changes also run Marshall's validator tests. Select\nnative checks from the maintained test catalog; do not run destructive harnesses\nagainst production resources."
msgstr ""

