#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8195
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "SQL-backed Marshall properties/fixed histories and protocol/Lilly/Audi component\nchecks have scoped evidence in the\n[editor review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\nThe NixOS browser fixture uses the real package/broker and synthetic roster/bridge.\nIts complete Linux UID/socket/refusal/restart and real browser-tool assertions\npassed in 60 seconds, including a positive fresh worker PID after loss and changed\norigin replacement preserving files. That\nrecord does not establish full service authentication, packet-mark, boot-trust,\nFirecracker or Ubuntu execution.\nThe complete NixOS journey separately passed real service authentication,\nFirecracker tools/custody/recovery, unsafe Origin refusal and sign-out closing\nestablished WebSockets with fresh sign-in recovery. The corrected merged NixOS\nsnapshot passed these stages again with exact current physical readiness;\nhistorical results retain their original revision. Corrected Ubuntu provisioned\nand reached the expected origin but reproduced workbench visibility failure\nbefore those assertions, with runtime cause unproved.\nTwo-writer native separation, multi-gateway failover and physical host faults\nremain explicit gaps in [scenario coverage](#coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8199
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "SSH CA operational retirement in Unix seconds (2046-09-25)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8200
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "SSH certificate operations use `porsche-ssh-certificate.timer` and\n`audi-ssh-certificate.timer` on gateways and the existing guest sync timer. A\nfailed renewal retains valid files; expired certificates fail new handshakes and\ngateway readiness. Verify the certificate with `ssh-keygen -Lf` on its public\n`ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub` file. The ordinary installer must connect without\nan authenticity prompt. Never copy the CA private key into a guest to repair\nreadiness."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8204
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "SSH host identity uses one dedicated CA held by Marshall. Native certificates\ncover management, gateway and guest peers; account keys and Cedar retain their\nseparate login authority. See [developer SSH](#interactive) and\n[security boundaries](#security)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8208
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "SSH host issuance authenticates service credentials or a physically bound guest\nboot before signing an authoritative principal. A valid host certificate still\nrequires the user's proved registered key and current Cedar grant. The shared\nCA private key never reaches Audi, Porsche, images or guests. Ephemeral per-boot\nleaf keys prevent cloned disks from sharing host identity. Native transport tests\nexercise certificate negotiation, rekey, principal rejection and CA revocation;\nfull installer, reboot, clone and relocation acceptance remains separately\ntracked in the scenario ledger."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8212
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "SSH uses a complete owned key-only policy and pinned PAM modules, with a\nrequisite private login receipt before a session opens. Locked `sshd` and\n`overalls-ssh` system identities receive collision-checked distinct UID/GIDs;\naccount lookup uses local files and reconciliation resolves pinned account tools\nthrough an explicit PATH. The image contains a regular root-owned setuid sudo\ncopy; only current reconciler-managed per-user policies grant access. Vendor\nsshd enablement resolves to the same readiness-gated listener. These assembly\ncontracts and account-allocator tests alone do not establish a working\ndistro-native SSH/PAM or sudo session; the later exact-image results below\nrecord that scope."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8216
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Secret preparation units required before Underclass starts."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8217
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "SecretSpec names under project overalls-BUNDLE, profile production."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8221
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Security boundary: the installation guest reaches no network other than the\npinned file server; the bootstrap Administrator logs on interactively exactly\nonce, during the build, and the finished image carries no autologon value\n(the Administrator itself is retired by the roster agent, ADR-0171);\npackage code enters the image only through reviewed pins;\nafter boot, users may run winget against its live sources like any other\nsoftware they install. The offline installation and a named fleet image have\nbeen recorded, including a create, relocation and workspace clone. WSL 2 inside\na Firecracker guest (nested SVM under Windows' hypervisor) remains unproven;\nVisual Studio Community is supplied by the reviewed pinned offline layout."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8225
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Security is enforced in layers. Passing an outer check never substitutes for the\nnext one. A signed-in user is not automatically a VM owner; an authorized request\nis not automatically current execution; a current placement is not proof that a\nnative disk or process belongs to it."
msgstr ""

