#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10556
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Unattended Marshall candidates must retain the database URL, shared cookie and\ntoken-signing authority. A candidate Cloak ring may add keys or reorder inactive\nkeys, up to sixteen entries, while retaining the active key and every prior\nkey's ID and bytes. Removal, promotion and material replacement require coordinated\nmaintenance. Preflight compares the staged candidate with every serving local\nMarshall environment. It reads the installed environment file only when none\nare serving; replacing that file cannot approve a candidate against older live\nauthority. Correct a refused candidate explicitly and submit it again."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10560
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Unavailable source capability refuses automatic restart while committing the\nconfirmed crash or resize outcome and any valid host report. Confirmed stopped\ncompute is released; disk and network address remain retained. A confirmed resize\nkeeps its target sizes and completes with `workspace_source_unavailable`, allowing\nordinary deletion and recreation on a current image. Unconfirmed effects retain\ntheir existing holds and fencing requirements. The final focused SQL-backed set\npassed 39 checks (3 properties, 36 tests), including six new source/snapshot\nregressions and editor publication; native recovery acceptance remains separately\nscoped in the [review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-launcher.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10564
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Underclass keeps one durable totals record in its admission journal\n(`slo-totals.sqlite`). Its single duration histogram has fifteen finite bounds\nthrough twenty-four hours and is the only Underclass p95 source; the exporter\nrefuses any other bound set. No code reads or converts the retired seven-bound\n`slo.sqlite`, so source lifetime and metric continuity restarted with the new\njournal. Terminal removal and aggregate changes commit together. Unknown recovery\nduration stays unmeasured, and overflow beyond the last finite bucket remains\nunavailable."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10568
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Unique host address in the dedicated 10.90.0.0/24 fleet network."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10572
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Untested boundaries: a live Porsche SSH session or packaged browser driving a\npin natively, and cross-node pin/delete races beyond the shared row lock\nargument. Expected refusals: `machine_pinned` on delete, `pin_limit` on the 21st\npin, `vm_deleted` when pinning a deleting machine, `forbidden` for a reader\nwithout access or an unpin without a live row."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10576
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Untested boundaries: the packaged browser sending the connect param, and a\nsaved zone whose rules change between tz releases. Expected refusals:\n`invalid_time_zone` for unknown identifiers, `Forbidden` for non-user actors,\n`unauthorized` for retired accounts."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10580
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Untested boundaries: the production Tailscale control plane and tailnet policy,\nthe macOS exit node, and stage-2 activation. Root clearing the preference\nmid-run leaks until the next start. Evidence: the `underclass-egress` machine\ncheck and the [Underclass operations](repo:docs/services/underclass.md) guide."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10584
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Untested gaps: Hyper-V synthetic timers are not emulated and timekeeping under\nload is unobserved; `C:` growth after a host-side extension is only known to\nleave a bootable guest. The host policy drops unmarked\ntraffic between the host and a Customer guest by design, so the machine test's\nreachability probe is a test-only allowance for one address, never a product\npath or a Marshall observation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10588
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Update the four extension pins separately from the official Code OSS/runtime pins:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10592
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Upload bandwidth cap in KiB/s; zero means unlimited."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10593
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use Grafana's fleet operations dashboard for independent logging health, finite\nbackup/updater states, resource measurements and trace custody. Missing source or\ninvalid counters are unavailable observations. Inspect canonical Marshall receipts\nand Lilly durable state separately when reconciling lifecycle work. Diagnostic\ndelivery failure cannot authorize a replacement mutation or cancel a guest."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10597
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use NixOS machine integration tests for native effects and property tests for\nauthority/state histories. The [scenario ledger](#coverage) records exact evidence\nand remaining gaps for sharing, execution, ingress, private services and recovery.\n[Enrollment histories](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/enrollment_history_test.exs)\ncover the Compute enrollment/credential/drain/retire ownership boundary against a\npure model; the [replacement journey](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/host-replacement.py)\nrepeats it on the real topology with fresh physical identities.\nThe [fleet lifecycle scenario](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/lifecycle.py)\nexercises real guests, but is not exhaustive coverage of every action in this\ninventory. There is no complete generated cross-domain authorization matrix;\nadd stale/foreign-authority histories and a native allowed/refused journey when\nchanging a sensitive action. Extension-generated resource versions are not\nenumerated by this source view; inspect their retention and redaction separately.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10601
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use Overalls from your browser or manage machines over SSH with Porsche. Marshall\nprovides the web interface and account permissions. Use the same account in both."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10605
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use Porsche to manage machines over SSH, with the same account and permissions\nas Marshall’s web interface."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10609
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use SSH exec commands and durable request IDs to automate machine management."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10613
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use `--json` for machine-readable results. An exec invocation writes one result\nto standard output; progress goes to standard error. Check the SSH command's exit\nstatus as well as its result. A failed command exits nonzero."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10617
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use `--platform ec2` for supported EC2 bare metal. Review the full hardware and\nnetwork inventory before publishing `fleet/hosts/example/host.json`. Select disks\nby stable IDs, firmware, a persistent nonzero host ID, budgets, public Git trust,\nand `reviewed = true`. Hetzner uses mirrored system disks; EC2 separates persistent\nEBS system state from local NVMe guest storage. Local NVMe loss is guest data loss\nunless a usable backup exists."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10621
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use reviewed x86-64 hardware with working KVM, supported firmware, stable disk IDs,\nand authenticated administrative SSH. The host tool requires Python, OpenSSH,\nlsblk and iproute2. Pin the rescue host key out of band. Keep operator private keys\nand generated plans outside the checkout."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10625
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use the Porsche hostname supplied by your operator. In a local terminal, run\n`ssh YOUR_PORSCHE_HOST help` for one command, or `ssh YOUR_PORSCHE_HOST` for an\ninteractive prompt. Verify the server host-key fingerprint using your operator's\ntrusted instructions. Management uses port 22."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10629
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use the [package update procedure](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/vscode-web/README.md) to review\nthe official source, maintained patches, native ABI and signing keys. Build the\nthird-party package and its native check before assembling new guest images:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10633
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use the command reference in [verification and reference](#reference). Supply\nsecret values only through supported stdin/private-file interfaces. A management\nSSH listener cannot be used as an administrative host shell. Fleet OpenSSH and\nthe restricted transfer endpoint have separate ports and trust purposes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10637
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use the machine's **Access** page to grant or revoke sharing. It lists the owner\nand every current grant with the role and what it allows, and one form grants,\nreplaces or removes a registered account's role (web apps only, viewer, operator,\nmanager). Grant the narrowest role that permits the intended action. The **Teams**\npage switches between your teams, lists each team's members with their role and\nwhat it allows, and holds the member form (admins and the owner) and the\nownership offer, acceptance, decline and cancel controls. Teams manage shared\nresources and ownership transfers; a transfer is a durable workflow, not a label\nchange. Revocation must\nreach new requests and renewable capabilities already in use."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10641
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use the machine's installation instructions to install the `overalls` CLI and\nconfigure local SSH. The installer and direct CLI setup fetch deployment-bound\nSSH CA policy through verified HTTPS, then install scoped `@cert-authority`\nentries. One dedicated CA authenticates Porsche, Audi and new NixOS/Ubuntu guests\nwith native OpenSSH certificates. Conflicting managed CA trust and explicit\nrevocation require reconciliation; host-key checking remains strict."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10645
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "User account under which Audiobookshelf runs."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10646
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "User controls lock their host, campaign and relevant VM records before retaining\nthe current actor User through audit commit. This preserves the VM-before-User\norder used by personal guest identity allocation; the actor lock permits ordinary\nforeign-key references while excluding authority changes. Overlapping elevation\nlock or sign-out therefore either follows an accepted control or causes refusal\nafter the control waits. Durable workers do not reacquire requester elevation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10650
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "VM disks have a maximum capacity of **500 GiB** (536,870,912,000 bytes).\nCreation and resize requests above this limit are rejected, including Porsche\n`new --disk` requests."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10654
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "VM disks have a maximum capacity of **500 GiB** (536,870,912,000 bytes).\nCreation and resize requests above this limit are rejected, including Porsche\n`new --disk` requests.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10658
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Verification: `firecracker-vmm` (version, `--enable-pci`, static pair),\n`windows-firmware` (PVH note, patched aperture), `windows-guest-unit`\n(offline KVM assembly rules, EMS, no autologon, eight-key manifest, bootstrap\ntask, viosock in the driver tree, the agents directory and probe task only when\nsupplied, the launcher's vsock device), `lyra` (Linux tests and clippy plus the\nWindows-target type check), the long-running `windows-guest` machine test\n(operator launcher to the `SAC>` prompt on nested KVM, then the probe's answer\nthrough the launcher's vsock socket and its published log; first recorded\nexecution 2026-10-14, probe execution recorded in the\n[agents review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-14-windows-guest-agents.md)),\nthe long-running `windows-lilly-guest-agents` machine test (the `windows-v1`\nimage through the real Lilly driver: the jail carries the vsock device, trust is\n`installed` by the guest with a boot UUID, provisioning reaches `ready` with the\nsame UUID within the 600 s budget, the daemons' published logs show\n`receipt_sent` and `ready_answered`, and a restart yields a new boot UUID) and the\nlong-running `windows-lilly-guest` machine test (real Lilly driver: firmware\nbundle on the dataset, skipped trust, `unattested` provisioning, `SAC>` on the\nboot log, the guest's bootstrap log read from the EFI system partition of the\nlive disk, reachability of the delivered `/32` through a test-only accept in the\nhost policy with the tap guard intact and counted, restart from the portable\nbundle, delete). Protocol, Lilly and Marshall unit and property tests\npin the version-4 and version-1 shapes unchanged. Recorded executions are\nlisted in the\n[spike review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-13-windows-firecracker-spike.md),\nthe\n[launch review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-14-windows-lilly-launch.md)\nand the\n[agents review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-14-windows-guest-agents.md).\nProtocol tests pin the capability table and the `windows-v1` manifest and bundle\nvectors; Lilly tests pin the agentless jail configuration, the vsock addition for\n`windows-v1`, the recorded readiness budget and the image configuration\nshape; Marshall tests bind the capabilities to the exact\nimage ID for every agent set and exercise the per-capability surfaces."
msgstr ""

