#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3517
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "- **unit, present**: [windows_v1](repo:protocol/test/guest_agents_test.exs) — The agent set wire values, the capability table and the readiness budgets are closed and pinned; no manifest or guest is involved..\n- **unit, present**: [windows_v1](repo:lilly/test/vm/jail_test.exs) — The agentless firmware jail configuration is unchanged and windows-v1 adds exactly the vsock key; no Firecracker process runs..\n- **unit, present**: [cacheability is the artifact size against the pool budget, without hashing](repo:lilly/test/host/image_template_cacheable_test.exs) — Cacheability is a size check against the pool budget on staged images; no pool or dataset exists..\n- **property, present**: [windows-v1](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/image_guest_agents_capability_test.exs) — Capabilities are bound to the validated manifest and its exact image ID for both firmware agent sets and fail closed otherwise; sandboxed Ash resources only..\n- **unit, present**: [viosock](repo:nix/verification/tests/evaluation/windows-guest.nix) — Builder rules: viosock in the driver tree, the agents directory and probe task only when agents are supplied, manifest agent set and workspace source version from the builder arguments, the launcher's vsock device. No installation or boot..\n- **unit, present**: [windows-v5-editor=false](repo:nix/verification/tests/evaluation/editor-target-boundaries.nix) — Static package metadata asserts the editor and broker target x86_64-linux and the Windows v5 package has no editor field or capability. This preserves the windows-v1 editor refusal; no Windows broker, browser origin or browser journey is exercised..\n- **unit, present**: [editor_capability == false](repo:nix/verification/tests/evaluation/windows-editor-runtime.nix) — Pinned Windows Node and ripgrep runtime metadata evaluates with editor_capability=false and no references; this stages executables only and does not build or run a Code OSS bundle..\n- **property, present**: [proptest!](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/vscode-web-broker/src/windows_model.rs) — Portable Rust properties and fixed tests bind names and peer custody to the boot/descriptor/account/SID identity, refuse foreign or incomplete recovery without cleanup, reject truncated SIDs and ambiguous local paths, and quote Windows command lines. No Win32 API, listener, VM or browser runs..\n- **unit, present**: [ensure_account](repo:lyra/src/bin/overalls-ssh-sync-windows.rs) — The Windows authorizer serializes account ensure with the shared roster lock and requires the exact canonical username/UID roster pair before mutation; no Windows account or SSH daemon is exercised..\n- **machine, recorded**: [overalls-winprobe](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/windows-guest/driver.py) — Installs the image with the viosock driver and the probe, boots it under the patched Firecracker on nested KVM to the SAC prompt, dials vsock port 1099 through the launcher's Unix socket, asserts the probe's JSON answer names host CID 2, and reads the probe's published log from the EFI system partition. Operator launcher only; no Lilly, no agents. Passed on 2026-10-14 (318.8 s script time; probe answered 23.7 s after the SAC prompt with address family 40 via the control device).; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-14-windows-guest-agents.md).\n- **unit, present**: [validation_binds_boot_digest_and_certificate_shape](repo:lyra/src/guest/trust.rs) — Shared trust rules: frames are bounded and round-trip, a request is accepted only for the exact boot with a matching digest and well-formed unique certificates, and the bundle is assembled from the base roots; the MMDS client's token-per-fetch exchange and document validation and the readiness line's six keys are covered beside it. Rust unit tests in the Lyra check..\n- **unit, present**: [authorized keys are pulled per account and follow key removal](repo:marshall/test/marshall/ssh/guest_access_test.exs) — The pulled key list names the roster's writers with exactly their unarchived registered keys, drops a removed key on the next pull, refuses a foreign or bootstrap binding and a bad credential, and records no login. Sandboxed Ash resources; Ziggy's route tests refuse the bootstrap binding on the new path..\n- **unit, present**: [reconcile_activates_deactivates_and_journals](repo:lyra/src/guest/ssh_roster.rs) — Shared roster rules with a fake account backend: names fit both platforms, stale and diverging rosters are refused without mutation, departed accounts are disabled before new ones are activated, and a failed activation leaves the staged union in the state..\n- **machine, recorded**: [ready_answered](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/windows-lilly-guest/driver.py) — The windows-v1 image through the real Lilly driver on nested KVM: the jail carries the vsock device, the guest's trust daemon installs the delivered roots and answers the installed receipt with a boot UUID, provisioning reaches ready with the same UUID within the 600 s budget, the unattested commit is refused, terminald authenticates the boot over vsock, lists root first, refuses an account the roster never created and runs a root PowerShell under ConPTY that prints a computed marker, a workspace delivery is recorded settled for the boot, port 22 stays closed without a roster, Inception stays refused, and a restart from the portable bundle yields a different boot UUID. Passed on 2026-10-15 in 2863 s on the reference-guarded image. No roster SSH, roster-user terminal, clone or agent turn.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-14-windows-guest-agents.md).\n- **machine, present**: [agentd start](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/windows-lilly-guest/driver.py) — The agents composition reads the closed agentd startup line from the live Windows EFI partition after the real guest reaches ready. This proves native agent task startup only; the Lilly-only fixture has no Marshall context snapshot, provider exchange or Windows fleet turn. Execution remains present until the composed check is recorded.."
msgstr ""

