#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "**Gaps:** Catalog completeness, placeholder parity, browser layout/bidi behavior, locale isolation and protocol compatibility need executed evidence. Native linguistic review and packaged NixOS browser journeys are not established."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3097
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "- **property, present**: [distinct generated releases remain bound to finite configured targets](repo:marshall/test/marshall/editor/releases_test.exs) — Generated Linux/Windows registry normalization and SQL rows, finite target names, distinct release admission and duplicate refusal. Pure configuration boundary; no native gateway runs..\n- **unit, present**: [distinct release receipts coexist and publication requires their complete fresh set](repo:marshall/test/marshall/editor_publication_test.exs) — Actual PostgreSQL publication query requires both configured releases, preserves independent receipt expiry and removes editor/webview discovery after one expires. No DNS packet, TLS listener or multi-gateway fault history..\n- **unit, present**: [v7 Windows editor publication matches only its target's exact approved release](repo:marshall/test/marshall/editor_publication_test.exs) — Actual SQL fixtures publish a v7 Windows owner only for its configured Windows tuple; swapping valid target descriptors removes that owner while complete neutral assets remain discoverable. No Windows guest or browser runs..\n- **unit, recorded**: [Customer editor DNS and neutral webviews require live attested assets](repo:marshall/test/marshall/editor_publication_test.exs) — Actual publication SQL with matching certificate/route/service fixtures, asset absence/readiness/expiry and foreign attestation refusal; not a DNS packet or native publisher.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **property, recorded**: [untrusted paths never select a file outside the three release assets](repo:audi/test/editor_assets_test.exs) — Generated path selection and fixed symlink/release/origin/method refusals inspect immutable local serving without guest connector authority.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [asset readiness follows the actual HTTPS service after nested suspension](repo:audi/test/http_front_test.exs) — Actual local TLS listener and operator roots prove healthy current-release serving, refuse wrong release/SNI and refuse nested acceptor suspension while files and supervisor remain alive. No multi-gateway DNS or Firecracker claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3465
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "- **unit, present**: [Linux and Windows approve distinct releases together without cross-target substitution](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/image_editor_capability_test.exs) — Pure validated image capability checks retain separate exact target tuples, reject swapped descriptors and preserve empty-registry refusal. No Windows guest, package execution or browser admission runs..\n- **unit, present**: [same_account_pipe_requires_job_and_executable_custody](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/vscode-web-broker/src/windows_model.rs) — Portable modeled custody rejects a same-account pipe without exact retained job and executable identity; no native SAM, Job Object or pipe API runs..\n- **unit, present**: [pipe_slots_remain_reserved_until_retained_operation_is_released](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/vscode-web-broker/src/windows_model.rs) — Portable slot reservations remain bounded until retained state drops; no native overlapped cancellation or completion is exercised..\n- **property, recorded**: [Windows editor identity binds its release and survives portable storage](repo:protocol/test/windows_editor_image_test.exs) — Pure generated v7 identity and v4 bundle round trips, field mutations and closed refusal. Existing Windows v1 remains false; no native image runs.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-18-cross-platform-editor-status.md).\n- **unit, recorded**: [native_pipe_copies_completed_bytes_and_retires_timeout_without_caller_storage](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/vscode-web-broker/src/windows_pipe.rs) — Executed real Windows named-pipe completion and timeout with copied operation storage; not the full worker or browser lifecycle.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-18-cross-platform-editor-status.md).\n- **machine, present**: [windows-editor-native-browser-journey](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/windows-editor/browser.py) — Source-present actual relay/workbench, native save/PTY and broker/worker recovery harness. Static