msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4100
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Apply the receipt-index migration before enabling concurrent releases. Rebuild\neach host's application and generated configuration atomically. During a\ncoordinated rollout, a gateway serving only Linux assets cannot satisfy a\ntwo-target registry: its editor and neutral webview discovery stays withdrawn\nuntil both current release receipts exist. Every advertised gateway must serve\nthe entire configured set because neutral webview DNS cannot choose a gateway\nby release. Changing either target's package changes its immutable identity and\nrequires corresponding image and gateway updates."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4569
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Boundary: Ingress EditorAssetsReceipt binds each approved target's full release tuple independently to current host session/service generation. Every advertised editor/webview gateway must hold the complete configured set because neutral DNS cannot route by release; discovery remains separate from personal Editor admission."
msgstr ""

